(23791475, 0, 'Senior Accountant', 'SPAR INFORMATION SYSTEMS', '', '1', '60', '04 Jun, 2017', '3', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Missouri City, MO', 'License/Certificates: Certified Public Accountant preferred, 3 to 5 years accounting experience, health care, Claim, Medicare coverage and services', '', '31', '79', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Position Purpose: Develop, analyze, and execute accounting and finance functions. Prepares managerial reports, financial reports, and general ledger.<br />\r\nPrepare and analyze journal entries, income statement, balance sheet, profit and loss statement, and other financial reports on a regular basis<br />\r\nReport and advise on organizationâ€™s financial status<br />\r\nDevelop integrated revenue/expense analyses, projections, reports, and presentations<br />\r\nCreate and analyze monthly, quarterly, and annual reports and ensures financial information has been recorded accurately<br />\r\nDevelop, implement, modify, and document accounting processes<br />\r\nAdapt accounting and recordkeeping functions to current computerized accounting systems technology<br />\r\nPrepare and maintain claims liability lag reports<br />\r\nReconcile and review claims system reports and claims liability reports to checks paid and other empirical data<br />\r\nMay be involved with due diligence, integration activities with acquired companies, technical accounting research, and other business issues<br />\r\nConduct special studies, develops, or recommends enhancements to accounting methods and procedures<br />\r\nAssist with provision of Medicare coverage and services<br />\r\nQualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEducation/Experience: Bachelorâ€™s Degree in Accounting and 3 to 5 years accounting experience, preferably in public accounting or the health care industry. Masterâ€™s Degree preferred.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLicense/Certificates: Certified Public Accountant preferred', 'Recruiter Four<br />\r\nSPAR INFORMATION SYSTEMS<br />\r\nPlano, TX', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '05 April, 2017', '2017-04-05', 42, '2017-04-05 05:19:40', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(23886550, 21094, 'Iseries System Administrator', 'Allianceit', '', '3', '0', '', '1', '4', 'Part-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '3039', '1301656', 'Plano, Plano', 'Financial', '', '23', '40', '', '', 'Y', '', 'SkillStorm is looking for an IBM iSeries System Engineer to work with one of our Fortune 500 clients. In this dynamic role, you will be responsible for replication and data recovery environments on IBM iSeries hardware platforms. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesired skills: <br />\r\n<br />\r\n7+ years experience with IBM I platform â€“ preferably on or migrating toward Power 8 hardware architecture, V6R1 or higher. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nProficient in LPAR design, build and validation <br />\r\n<br />\r\nProficient in Replication using OMS and MIMIX solution <br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience with OMS and MIMIX Replication Technology, and supporting third party products installations and maintenance. Works under the direction/supervision of team manager, project manager, or senior technical person. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nProficient in link / data group creation, balancing and optimization <br />\r\n<br />\r\nKnowledge of DR environment creation, documentation, maintenance, and role swaps/failovers <br />\r\n<br />\r\nKnowledge of third party product installation, maintenance, apply license keys â€¦etc. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nProficient in problem determination and overall troubleshooting skills <br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience with hardware break/fix events <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to communicate clearly in a large enterprise environment <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to work independently and strives for results <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to support 24/7 on-call <br />\r\n<br />\r\nKnowledge and ability to work with MS Office products <br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Requirements: <br />\r\n<br />\r\nDemonstrated knowledge of Save/Restore techniques for all object types. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to perform a failover/role swap between production and DR environments <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to read job logs, and understand how to indentify/fix/rectify issues related to save/restore activities <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to configure/debug issues relating to any and all outside communication methods (SNA, TCP/IP, etc <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to support System tools and utilities (Job scheduler, third party products, including DBU, NDM, Robot, etc <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to read job logs/system logs to diagnose application issues, and identify the root cause. Be able to properly triage the issue and possibly correct the root cause. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nDemonstrated proficiency supporting file journaling, journal analysis, and journal receiver management. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to debug/correct system issues, including storage management, and basic admin tasks (Exit programs, system values, etc <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to work in a team environment, and also independently with little supervision on occasions. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to communicate clearly, and effectively, in verbal and written communications. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to understand and support change control procedures and policies. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to understand and support work management objects (Subsystems, Job Queues, etc <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAble to understand and support security policies, and how those work within the applications (Authority lists, private authorities, etc ', '', 'We have direct management Contact for these Roles! <br />\r\n<br />\r\nThree iseries system admin/engineers, moving from power 7 to power 8, San based storage, , OS upgrade 6.1 to 7.2, IVM DS800 external storage, exp with Vios, Iseries at the end will be global mirroring, will be taking one system to global mirroring for ML. Power 8 systems will stay, not developers but admins- but with the Power 8 experience. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nMIMIX is NOT required but replication experience in general is needed. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nSkillStorm is seeking an IBM iSeries System Engineer to work with one of our Fortune 500 clients.', '', 'Bachelor\'s degree in computer science, computer engineering or related technical discipline', 'Formal', 'US Citizen, GC, EAD (OPT/CPT/GC/H4)', 'W2-Contract, 1099-Contract, Contract to Hire', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '13 February, 2017', '2017-02-13', 93, '2017-02-12 22:28:39', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(23946653, 45185, 'Business Development Executive (Fresher)', 'Focus Ideas', '', '80', '0', '', '0', '0', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'Kolkata / Bhubaneswar', 'Knowledge of Business Development Executive', 'http://www.focusideas.co.in', '10', '110', '', '', 'Y', 'Incentive', 'Key Job Responsibilities<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1) Quality acquisition of Current Account & Saving Account for Resident / Non-resident Indian.<br />\r\n2) Ensure quality sourcing of new customer to sell different banking product like Demat Account, Life Insurance, Credit Card etc<br />\r\n3) Penetration of Fixed Deposit to existing & new customers<br />\r\n4) Generate leads of customer through referral, meeting branch walk-ins customer, associates, e-mailing, direct mailing, ATMs & cold calls in the catchment area.<br />\r\n5) Ensure quality customer service is delivered<br />\r\n6) Meeting productivity norms as defined through support of channels & own efforts<br />\r\n7) Strictly adhere & maintain KYC norms compliance<br />\r\n8) Adhere the norms, regulation & practices of banks religiously<br />\r\n', '', 'Position : Business Development Executive<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLocation : Kolkata / Bhubaneswar<br />\r\n<br />\r\nObjective :Providing support to branch profitability by selling bank products through different<br />\r\nacquisition channels in the catchment area.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKey Job Responsibilities<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1) Quality acquisition of Current Account & Saving Account for Resident / Non-resident Indian.<br />\r\n2) Ensure quality sourcing of new customer to sell different banking product like Demat Account, Life Insurance, Credit Card etc<br />\r\n3) Penetration of Fixed Deposit to existing & new customers<br />\r\n4) Generate leads of customer through referral, meeting branch walk-ins customer, associates, e-mailing, direct mailing, ATMs & cold calls in the catchment area.<br />\r\n5) Ensure quality customer service is delivered<br />\r\n6) Meeting productivity norms as defined through support of channels & own efforts<br />\r\n7) Strictly adhere & maintain KYC norms compliance<br />\r\n8) Adhere the norms, regulation & practices of banks religiously<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCompetencies Required<br />\r\nHonesty & integrity	Go getter attitude<br />\r\nHard & smart working	Ability to convince & influence<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPREFERABLE	TWO WHEELER WITH VALID LICENCE, LOCAL RESIDENCE<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEducation / Qualification	GRADUATE (REGULAR ONLY), NO MBAâ€™S.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWork Experience :	FRESHER<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPerformance Incentives	Monthly performance incentives (best in banking industry)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary Range	Rs 10.5 Net Take Home Per Month<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAge Criteria 	Below 26 Years<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf interested, send updated CV with photo to career.focusideas@gmail.com Or  call 08961795851<br />\r\n', 'Interest candidate are apply who are work Key Job Responsibilities of Quality acquisition of Current Account & Saving Account for Resident / Non-resident Indian. & Ensure quality customer service is delivered<br />\r\n', 'Any Graduate ', 'No Require.', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '05 January, 2017', '2017-01-05', 132, '2017-01-05 05:02:23', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(24033617, 58574, 'Finance Functional Analyst', 'Raising Global Solutions', '', '5', '0', '', '8', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Hyderabad, ', '', '', '23', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'â€¢	8- 10 Years of experience on Oracle ERP Applications in Finance modules.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Skills: Worked on US GAAP, US GAAP Reporting, IFRS<br />\r\nâ€¢	Act as Subject Matter Expert on Oracle ERP applications and related technologies.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Functional expert of R12 Oracle apps, driving resolution of production support issues/ Implementation predominantly in Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivables, General Ledger, Fixed Assets, Cash Management, Revenue Recognition and Purchasing.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Effectively resolve problems and roadblocks as they occur, consistently following through on details while driving innovation as well as issue resolution and anticipates and prevents problems before they occur.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Debug complex issues and present their impact along with recommended solution to users and management<br />\r\nâ€¢	Supporting key business processes/activities including but not limited to Month end and Year end support activities to Business users<br />\r\nâ€¢	Excellent communications skills (Written and verbal) and should be able to independently engage with business stakeholders throughout the ticket lifecycle<br />\r\nâ€¢	Ability to orchestrate multiple activities simultaneously<br />\r\nâ€¢	Ability to present facts in a simplified manner for mixed audience from technical & business background<br />\r\nâ€¢	Detail understanding of the following Oracle tools in connection with Oracle Release 12: SQL, Workflow.<br />\r\nâ€¢	This role might require availability in night shift<br />\r\n', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '13 December, 2016', '2016-12-13', 155, '2016-12-13 04:09:50', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(24418903, 87339, 'Planing Engineer, Mechanical Engineer, Prodcution Engineer', 'RISE INDIA ENTERPRISES MANPOWER PVT LTD', '', '', '0', '', '0', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', '', '', '', 'Mumbai ,Pune ,Navi Mumbai ,Thane ,Dubai', '', '', '16', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Daily duites & responsibility -<br />\r\nReview production schedules, engineering specifications, process flows, and other information to understand methods and activities in manufacturing and services<br />\r\nFigure out how to manufacture parts or products, or deliver services, with maximum efficiency<br />\r\nDevelop management control systems to make financial planning and cost analysis more efficient<br />\r\nEnact quality control procedures to resolve production problems or minimize costs<br />\r\nWork with customers and management to develop standards for design and production<br />\r\nDesign control systems to coordinate activities and production planning to ensure that products meet quality standards<br />\r\nConfer with clients about product specifications, vendors about purchases, management personnel about manufacturing capabilities, and staff about the status of projects<br />\r\nIndustrial engineers apply their skills to many different situations from manufacturing to business administration. For example, they design systems for<br />\r\nmoving heavy parts within manufacturing plants<br />\r\ngetting goods from a company to customers, including finding the most profitable places to locate manufacturing or processing plants<br />\r\nevaluating how well people do their jobs<br />\r\npaying workers<br />\r\nIndustrial engineers focus on how to get the work done most efficiently, balancing many factorsâ€”such as time, number of workers needed, available technology, actions workers need to take, achieving the end product with no errors, workers\' safety, environmental concerns, and cost.<br />\r\nTo find ways to reduce waste and improve performance, industrial engineers first study product requirements carefully. Then they use mathematical methods and models to design manufacturing and information systems to meet those requirements most efficiently.', 'Intrested Candidates can send there resumes - riseindia.hr@gmail.com/riseindia.resume@gmail.com<br />\r\nor contact on below no.<br />\r\nManish -7208215350<br />\r\nRam varma- 9967658866<br />\r\nRegards,<br />\r\nRise India Enterprises Manpower Pvt Ltd.', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '18 October, 2016', '2016-10-18', 211, '2016-10-18 11:15:26', 'IN', 'D', '', '', '', ''),
(24424922, 0, 'Telesales / Telemarketing Executive', 'ACCREDIUM CONFORMITY ASSESSMENT SERVICES PVT LIMIT', '', '2', '90', '04 Jun, 2017', '0', '2', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'IN', '', '434079', 'Delhi', 'telesales   telemarketing  tele sales ', '', '29', '116', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Executive Sales/ Executive Telesales<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNew Client Acquisition<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Summary: The person will be required to make 70-80 calls and fix meetings for certificates and thereby acquire new clients.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKey Responsibility Areas: The job will be of pure sales profile and based out at locations as to be decided by the company . The short job profile is as under<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCall & set-up appointments on daily basis.<br />\r\nAchievement of weekly sales targets<br />\r\nEnsure strict adherence of sales process and internal procedures<br />\r\nTo interact with the Decision Making Authority/CEO of SME and Corporate Clients<br />\r\nConvince them to go for company\'s certification and Product Certifications by demonstrating them System Certifications and product certifications benefit.<br />\r\nGenerating new business from the new and existing channel partners as well as direct customers<br />\r\nFollow up with the prospective direct customers and meet the target of per month.<br />\r\nResponsible for fixing and making the meetings with the clients to generate the business.<br />\r\nResponsible for making strategies for generation of revenue.<br />\r\nResponsible for sales till the fixing meetings for Business Development Managers.<br />\r\nResponsible for making strategic tie ups with the associations for profitability of the organizations.', 'Email: channel6acascert@gmail.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 7290018215', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '06 March, 2017', '2017-03-06', 72, '2017-03-06 02:33:14', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(24540185, 0, 'Sales Coordinator', 'Marking Services, Inc.', '', '', '90', '21 Jun, 2017', '3', '8', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Milwaukee, WI', ' Sales - Inside, Customer Service - General, Admin - Data Entry/Billing', '', '22', '80', '', '', '', '', 'Sales Process<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Obtains and tracks project numbers.<br />\r\n    Ensures that pre-qualification packages are completed.<br />\r\n    Coordinates terms & conditions review process.<br />\r\n    Participates in request for quotation response and ensures requested documentation is completed.<br />\r\n    Submits the Requests for Information to Engineering Support and ensures information is obtained, filed and sent to Business Development.<br />\r\n    Obtains customer drawings and submits them to Document Control.<br />\r\n    Manages all project documentation.<br />\r\n    Prepares and reviews draft Technical and Commercial Sales proposals.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\nAdditional Duties and Responsibilities:<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Other duties as may be necessary to fulfill the responsibilities of this position.<br />\r\n    Cross train on other department areas to provide backup assistance.<br />\r\n    Assists Business Development with travel coordination<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n <br />\r\nKNOWLEDGE AND SKILL REQUIREMENTS:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Working knowledge of the MSII turnkey sales process and project execution a plus.<br />\r\n    Computer proficient.<br />\r\n    Working knowledge of MS Office applications, Great Plains, ACT (or CRM) and internet resourcing.<br />\r\n', '', 'POSITION SUMMARY:<br />\r\nThis entry-level position will provide assistance to the Business Development Manager in daily activities of turnkey projects, and will carry out tasks for all phases of sales and project processes.<br />\r\n <br />\r\n <br />\r\nPOSITION DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:<br />\r\nProjects<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Assists with the preparation and distribution of Project Definition Documentâ€™s.<br />\r\n    Obtains and distributes layouts.<br />\r\n    Communicates project specific information to Engineering Support and Production.<br />\r\n    Prepares progress billing from Sales/Field information based on contract type (time & materials, percent complete or actual complete).<br />\r\n    Prepares invoices for review and releases to accounting for invoice submittal.<br />\r\n    Provides Accounting/Project Cost Tracker with invoice breakdown (material, engineering, installation, tax)<br />\r\n    Tracks change orders and invoices on billing summary.<br />\r\n    Reviews orders to ensure they meet Project Definition Document specifications.<br />\r\n    Monitors project orders.<br />\r\n    Reviews client edit lists for compliance with Project Definition Document specifications.<br />\r\n    Prepares project follow up documentation and re-order checklists.<br />\r\n    Maintains project files and documentation.<br />\r\n    Prepares project summary binders to send to Clientâ€™s.<br />\r\n', '<br />\r\nToll free: 800.234.0135<br />\r\nPh: 414.973.1331<br />\r\n8265 N. Faulkner Road<br />\r\nP.O. BOX 240027<br />\r\nMilwaukee, WI 53224<br />\r\n', '10+2', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '23 March, 2017', '2017-03-23', 55, '2017-03-23 02:45:08', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
