(34815717, 0, 'SAP Business Systems Analyst HR & Administration', 'DC&M Partners', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '5', '12', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Los Angeles, CA  ', ' â€œhuman resourcesâ€, â€œtimekeepingâ€, and â€œpayrollâ€', '', '23', '115', '', '', '', '', 'Job Requirements:<br />\r\nâ€¢ Typically requires a bachelorâ€™s degree in Information Technology or a related field and fourteen or more years of progressive applications experience with at least three of those years in management/lead solution architect role. Equivalent professional experience may be substituted in lieu of education.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must demonstrate a thorough understanding of SAP principles, theories, concepts and techniques.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must possess a minimum of 7+ years of hands-on SAP functional experience in the HCM, Payroll, and Time & Attendance modules<br />\r\nâ€¢ ABAP debugging skills, knowledge of user exits, function modules, and relational database skills are preferred<br />\r\nâ€¢ Cross-functional working knowledge of other SAP modules (FI, CO, MM, PP, QM, EAS, and their various sub areas)<br />\r\nâ€¢ SuccessFactors experience is preferred<br />\r\nâ€¢ Proven track record as a senior SAP Business Analyst or as a senior functional consultant with multiple implementation projects as well as support experience at medium to large size companies<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must possess the ability to follow best practices regarding documentation and unit testing<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must be able to manage several projects, tickets, and other deliverables in a fast-paced environment and multi-task without sacrificing quality of work<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must demonstrate a thorough understanding of SAP methodology, principles, theories, concepts and techniques<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must demonstrate strong Project Management skills and project execution<br />\r\nâ€¢ Demonstrate leadership skills including planning, scheduling, and coordinating work assignments to meet project milestones or established completion dates.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must possess the ability to contribute to the development of new processes, as well as effectively identify, analyze and resolve highly complex business process and technical issues.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must be customer focused, demonstrate excellent verbal and written communication skills to accurately document, report, and present findings, and possess excellent interpersonal skills to interface with all levels of employees.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must be a team player with demonstrated professional/social interpersonal relationship management skills<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must be able to maintain the strict confidentiality of sensitive information<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must be able to work extended hours and travel between Company facilities as required.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must have proven leadership skills including planning, scheduling, and coordinating work assignments to meet project milestones or established completion dates.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must possess the ability to understand new concepts quickly and apply them in an evolving environment while contributing to the development of new processes.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must be customer focused and possess: (1) the ability to identify and analyze issues and develop solutions to a variety of highly complex and diverse problems; (2) excellent analytical, verbal and written communication skills to accurately document, report, and present findings; (3) excellent interpersonal skills to interface with all levels of employees, management and external contacts; (4) the ability to maintain the confidentiality of sensitive information; and (5) excellent computer skills. Ability to work independently or in a team environment is essential, to multi-task in a fast-paced work environment. Experience working in a Government contracting environment<br />\r\nâ€¢ SAP and SuccessFactors functional experience in Aerospace and Defense industry is a major plus<br />\r\nâ€¢ Knowledge of general business processes in â€œhuman resourcesâ€, â€œtimekeepingâ€, and â€œpayrollâ€ areas<br />\r\nâ€¢ Must be a U.S. Person to work in Export/Control areas.', '', 'DC&M Partners, a specialized IT and SAP staffing and consulting team, is currently assisting our direct clients in California in locating a SAP Business Systems Analyst â€“ HR & Administration<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRole: SAP Business Systems Analyst â€“ HR & Administration<br />\r\nEmployment Type â€“ Direct Hire<br />\r\nPay Rate: $140K<br />\r\nLocation: Los Angeles, CA<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis position is responsible for hands on solution architecture, delivery, and ongoing management of the Human Resources (HR) and Payroll (PY) functions using SAP application suites - ECC, CATS, SuccessFactors, and Business Intelligence (BI), and various HR.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDuties & Responsibilities:<br />\r\nâ€¢ As part of ITS Value Stream team, the individual will participate in supporting the business in the following value stream tracks:<br />\r\nâ€¢ Human Resources<br />\r\nâ€¢ Payroll<br />\r\nâ€¢ Timekeeping/Labor<br />\r\nâ€¢ Facilities<br />\r\nâ€¢ Lead meetings and discussions on new project initiatives throughout all the phases of typical ITS projects under minimal supervision:<br />\r\nâ€¢ Perform Project Management Duties<br />\r\nâ€¢ Facilitate process-oriented meetings<br />\r\nâ€¢ Understand and identify areas for process improvement through functional and technical solutions<br />\r\nâ€¢ Distinguish between a reasonable business requirement vs. solution requirement<br />\r\nâ€¢ Document the process flow in a swim lane format<br />\r\nâ€¢ Prototype solution options theoretically and in an available system such as a sandbox<br />\r\nâ€¢ Write functional specifications for complex development objects (Forms, Reports, Interfaces, Conversion, Enhancements, and Workflow)<br />\r\nâ€¢ Configure SAP system in the responsible modules:<br />\r\nâ€¢ HR: Employee Master, Organizational Management, Reporting<br />\r\nâ€¢ Payroll: Payroll calculations, Reporting<br />\r\nâ€¢ Time and Attendance: CATS, Labor processing<br />\r\nâ€¢ Configure SuccessFactors:<br />\r\nâ€¢ Employee Central<br />\r\nâ€¢ Talent Solutions<br />\r\nâ€¢ Engage customers for user acceptance test<br />\r\nâ€¢ Manage transports involved in system configuration and development using Solution Manager - CHARM<br />\r\nâ€¢ Identify, track, and resolve issues from all phases of the project<br />\r\nâ€¢ Communicate project statuses both positive and negative in a concise and meaningful manner<br />\r\nâ€¢ Work closely with the SAP technical developers, basis, security, and other functional analysts for cross-functional delivery of complex solutions<br />\r\nâ€¢ Follows established change control procedures for migration to QA and Production.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Provide direction, guidance, and training to less experienced staff and may on occasions be asked to lead Projects<br />\r\nâ€¢ Represent ITS and the value stream as a delegate when necessary<br />\r\nâ€¢ Performs other duties as assigned or required<br />\r\n<br />\r\no apply, please send your current resume/Click here to Apply<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDC&M Partners LLC provides clients with a wide range of SAP development, consultancy, and management services. At DC&M, we pride ourselves on the high quality and experience of our consultants and the timeliness with which we deliver solutions. These factors help build a foundation of trust â€“ and thatâ€™s the foundation upon which we built this business.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQuality and Experience â€“ The Foundation of our Business<br />\r\nOur consultants have in-depth knowledge of SAP and have witnessed its evolution into todayâ€™s industry standard ERP package. They also have a critical understanding of todayâ€™s business environment and how it relates to SAP and IT advances. The quality and experience of our consultants is what enables our clients to execute their business processes in the most optimal and efficient manner.', '', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '10 April, 2017', '2017-04-10', 37, '2017-04-10 05:52:19', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(34947862, 0, 'Software Engineer / Senior Software Engineer', 'Salus Alpha Information Technologies Private Limit', '', '1', '90', '04 Jun, 2017', '3', '9', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'IN', '', '435795', 'Pune', 'Design Patterns', '', '23', '29', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Minimum 3+ years of working experience in application development using Microsoft technologies like ASP.NET3.5 and above, C#, SQL Server 2008, SSIS, SSRS<br />\r\nC#.NET,ASP.NET 3.5 and above, so most of the projects should be on Web application rather than on Windows application<br />\r\nWorking experience in object-oriented design (OOAD, UML, Design Patterns etc.)<br />\r\nExcellent programming skills is a must<br />\r\nStrong code debugging experience in visual studio 2010 IDE<br />\r\nStrong aptitude and analytical skills<br />\r\nWCF services<br />\r\nApplication deployment experience and working knowledge of Web servers like IIS 7.0<br />\r\nJavaScript and AJAX<br />\r\nEnterprise library (added advantage)<br />\r\nStrong working experience in SQL 2008 (preferably in SQL Server)', '    Company Name: Salus Alpha Information Technologies Private Limited.<br />\r\n    Email: archita.tandon@salusalpha-it.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 2027297900', 'BE/BTech', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '06 March, 2017', '2017-03-06', 72, '2017-03-06 02:21:33', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(35015842, 0, 'Data Analyst', 'libsys inc', '', '2', '90', '04 Jun, 2017', '5', '7', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '12', 'US', '', '1206528', 'Waltham, MA', 'Claims, Clinical Data, External Reporting, HEDIS, member data, Pharmacy, provider data', '', '1', '141', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Position Purpose: Responsible for analytic data needs of the business unit. Handle complex data projects and acts as a lead for other Data Analysts.<br />\r\nProvide advanced analytical support for business operations in all or some of the following areas: claims, provider data, member data, clinical data, HEDIS, pharmacy, external reporting<br />\r\nExtract, load, model, and reconcile large amounts of data across multiple system platforms and sources<br />\r\nReview data to determine operational impacts and needed actions; elevate issues, trends, areas for improvement and opportunities to management.<br />\r\nDevelop reports and deliverables for management<br />\r\nModel data using MS Excel, Access, SQL, and/or other data ware house analytical tools<br />\r\nEnsure compliance with federal and state deliverable reporting requirements by performing data quality audits and analysis.<br />\r\nAssist with training and mentoring other Data Analysts.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEducation/Experience: Bachelorâ€™s degree in related field or equivalent experience. 4+ years of statistical analysis or data analysis experience. Healthcare experience preferred. Advanced knowledge of Enterprise Reporting and Analysis tools, SQL, and Microsoft Office applications, including Excel and Access. Experience managing projects or heavy involvement in project implementation.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBUSINESS ANALYTICS:<br />\r\nBachelorâ€™s degree in related field or equivalent experience. 4+ years of statistical analysis or 2+ years of related IT experience, including data warehouse, coding or ETL experience. Healthcare experience preferred. Advanced knowledge of Enterprise Reporting and Analysis tools, SQL, and Microsoft Office applications, including Excel and Access. Experience managing projects or heavy involvement in project implementation. Encounters experience preferred.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEmployee Status:<br />\r\nRegular<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Level:<br />\r\nStaff<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Type:<br />\r\nRegular<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMore information about the job<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIs Relocation Available?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYes, nationwide<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIs there a bonus structure?<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6%<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAre you open to sponsorship?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNo<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis position is:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBackfill<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIs there a possibility to work remote?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNo<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIs there equity?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYes<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAre there flexible work hours?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNo<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDoes this position have direct reports?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNo<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWho does this position report to?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nManager, Data Analytics & Reporting intake call recording: , desired salary, current location, healthcare exp, claims exp, SQL exp and availability in the Recruiter Notes of submittal.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhat are the 3-4 non-negotiable requirements on this position?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nat least 4 yrs. of statistical or data analytics Solid data skills, especially in SQL and Microsoft Office (Excel and Access in particular) Familiarity with Enterprise Reporting and Analysis tools and data visualization tools. Experience in supporting physician and hospital contracting activities through contract interpretation, quality reporting and analysis of claims.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhat are the nice-to-have skills?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience in a health economic role at a health plan or related IT experience including data warehouse, coding or ETL experience. Experience managing projects or project implementation.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhat is exciting about this opportunity? Please use this section to describe team and company culture.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe also have a Data Analyst II requisition open.', 'Abdul Razak<br />\r\nlibsys inc<br />\r\nNaperville, IL<br />\r\nwww.libsysinc.com<br />\r\n +1-630-799-1556', '', 'Formal', 'US Citizen, GC', 'W2-Contract', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '06 March, 2017', '2017-03-06', 72, '2017-03-06 02:49:40', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(35511680, 0, 'Client Relations Manager', 'Ingram Content Group', '', '1', '90', '14 Jun, 2017', '9', '15', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '12', 'US', '', '', 'New York, NY', 'Customer Service - General, Sales - Representatives/Service, Business Ops - Business Development', '', '1', '61', '', '', '', '', '', '', ' Client Relations Manager<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNew York<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNew York<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUnited States<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Description<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIngram Content Group (ICG), is currently seeking a Client Relations Manager with experience in book trade sales, marketing, or distribution to join our team in New York City. In this role, you will manage the day-to-day relationship with a group of client publishers who use our services for print and eBook sales and distribution. You will facilitate communication between clients and departments across the company including sales, marketing, finance, and all operational and service areas.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf you are good at problem solving, being organized, and enjoy working with publishers, this is the job for you.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEssential Job Duties:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Serves as liaison between assigned client publishers and the Ingram organization across departments including sales, marketing, finance, and all operational service areas.<br />\r\n    Develops and maintains profitable and successful relationships with a mix of trade and academic client publishers.<br />\r\n    Develops client-specific agenda and objectives; prepares appropriate reports; discusses client\'s current/year-to-date business; communicates changes in policy/procedure, explains benefits and requirements; discusses any issues and concerns; and commits to a follow-up plan.<br />\r\n    Works closely with client publishers and shared assistant to help produce effective sales materials and prepare for seasonal sales meetings.<br />\r\n    Helps develop print projections for frontlist titles and track progress of orders against projections.<br />\r\n    Provides guidance on print and eContent merchandising opportunities.<br />\r\n    Operates as the expert for all things pertaining to assigned clients.<br />\r\n    Coordinates and/or provides basic training on all systems to clients as needed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nis one of the world\'s largest and most trusted distributors of physical and digital content. Thousands of publishers, retailers, and libraries worldwide use our products and services to realize the full business potential of books, regardless of format. has earned its lead position and reputation by offering excellent service and creating innovative, integrated solutions. Our customers have access to best-of-class digital, audio, print, print-on-demand, inventory management, wholesale and full-service distribution programs.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMinimum Qualifications<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe would like our talented associate for this role to have at least these minimum skills & experience:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Bachelor\'s Degree<br />\r\n    4+ years of experience in a client services, sales, or marketing role within the book industry<br />\r\n    Proficient, professional capabilities using MS Office applications<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPreferred Qualifications<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe\'d be excited to hear if you also have the following experience:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Strong knowledge of the book publishing industry<br />\r\n    Experience in trade or academic publishing welcome<br />\r\n    Some travel availability<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIngram Content Group is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, work related mental or physical disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or genetic information.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEEO/AA Employer/Vet/Disabled<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe participate in EVerify.<br />\r\n', '', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '16 March, 2017', '2017-03-16', 62, '2017-03-16 02:57:47', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(35765623, 0, 'Pega Claims Workstation expert.', 'Centraprise', '', '1', '90', '04 Jul, 2017', '7', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Tampa, FL', 'PEGA Experience â€¢ Knowledge and implementation and development experience with Health Care Industry Foundation and Health Care', '', '31', '79', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Hi,<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlease share profiles on below ASAP.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Title: Pega Claims Workstation expert.<br />\r\nClient Rate - $DOE/Hr<br />\r\nLocation â€“ Tampa, Florida<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Description:-<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMinimum 6 - 10 yrs. of PEGA Experience<br />\r\nKnowledge and implementation and development experience with Health Care Industry Foundation and Health Care Claims Workstation frameworks<br />\r\nShould be familiar with Healthcare Payers domain and Claim work object life cycle and automation thatâ€™s part of Health Care Claims Workstation.<br />\r\nMust have working knowledge on Enterprise Class structure<br />\r\nShould have knowledge on Rule resolution<br />\r\nShould have knowledge on DCO, Application profiler, Application Accelerator<br />\r\nMust have working knowledge on Performance Tuning (PAL, Log Analyzer, DB Tracer/ Preflight)<br />\r\nMust have working knowledge on SMA (System Management Administrator) tool<br />\r\nShould have working experience in Pega Framework implementation experience (CPM, NBAM, Smart Investigation, etc<br />\r\nMust have working knowledge on Node & Thread level page<br />\r\nMust have working knowledge on advance Pega OOTB Integration (Exp - Exception handling, Data mapping for services and connectors, Security model for SOAP connectors & services)<br />\r\nMust have working knowledge on Pega Deployment experience / knowledge (Deployment Architecture) / Rules import & Export<br />\r\nShould have knowledge on Rule Passivation and Pega Cache<br />\r\nShould have working knowledge on single and multivariate circumstancing<br />\r\nShould have working knowledge on Pega Authentication & Authorization, Authenticate using LDAP and implement Single-Sign-On (SSO)<br />\r\nShould have working knowledge on Agents & listeners<br />\r\nShould be Pega CSSA certified<br />\r\nShould have working knowledge on Data Model (Data Tables, Data Pages, Advanced properties options, linked properties)<br />\r\nShould have knowledge on Case Management (Case Designer to create a case types, sub cases, add process to case, Covers and Folders)<br />\r\nShould have knowledge on Push & Pull routing, skill based routing<br />\r\nShould clear with key concepts and tools of the Designer Studio<br />\r\nMust have knowledge on Pega-RULES Agents like System Indexer, System Pulse<br />\r\nReporting with expertise in BIX (Business Intelligence Exchange) is preferable<br />\r\nExperience or knowledge in Pega 7.1 features and concepts<br />\r\nAgile, Pega Scrum Methodology knowledge<br />\r\nExperience installing and managing an Application/Web server<br />\r\nFamiliarity with relational database<br />\r\nMust have lead at least 2 Pega projects in CSSA capacity<br />\r\nGood with BPM Concepts and Terminologies', 'Surendra Penumala<br />\r\nCentraprise<br />\r\nEdison, NJ<br />\r\nwww.centraprise.com<br />\r\n +1-732-301-3826', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '05 April, 2017', '2017-04-05', 42, '2017-04-05 05:12:39', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(35898374, 0, 'Supply Planner', 'Briggs & Stratton Corporation', '', '1', '90', '20 Jun, 2017', '2', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Wauwatosa, WI', ' Production - General, Supply Chain/Logistics', '', '32', '80', '', '', '', '', 'Educational Requirements:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Bachelor\'s degree or equivalent experience <br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience Requirements:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Minimum of two to four years planning, production planning, forecasting and supply chain analytics<br />\r\n    Minimum of two to four years working in planning tools such as Demand Solutions, Logility or equivalent planning software<br />\r\n    Strong desire to achieve APICS or other forecasting certificate <br />\r\n<br />\r\nBriggs & Stratton Corporation, headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, is the world\'s largest producer of gasoline engines for outdoor power equipment. Its wholly owned subsidiaries include North America\'s number one marketer of pressure washers, and it is a leading designer, manufacturer and marketer of power generation, lawn and garden, turf care and job site products through its Simplicity, Snapper, Snapper Pro Ferris, Allmand, Billy Goat, Murray, PowerBoss Branco and Victa brands. Briggs & Stratton products are designed, manufactured, marketed and serviced in over 100 countries on six continents. For more information visit www.basco.com and www.briggsandstratton.com.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBriggs & Stratton Corporation is committed to a policy of equal employment opportunity. The Company conducts all employment practices without regard to race, sex, color, religion, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran\'s status, pregnancy, genetic information, sexual orientation or any other basis prohibited by law. Briggs & Stratton also undertakes affirmative action to assure equal employment opportunity for minorities and women, for persons with disabilities, and for protected veterans.', '', 'As an Integrated Business Planner you will be responsible for adequate supplies of all resources necessary to support the supply of products and services to meet customer needs at an optimal cost in accordance with the monthly Integrated Business Planning (IBP) process calendar. Collaborates with Sales, Marketing, Finance, Platform Management, customers and other sources to understand how environmental factors, market dynamics, competitors and internal programs or overrides generate the need to adjust the mathematical forecast. Presents data, conducts analysis and facilitates dialog across key stakeholder groups to deliver the supply plan to meet the unconstrained demand plan.<br />\r\nJob Responsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Validates balancing of supply with demand over the short and long-term planning horizon<br />\r\n    Confirms adequate supplies of all resources necessary to support the supply of products and services to meet customer needs at an optimal cost<br />\r\n    Interacts frequently with business, sales, marketing, demand management and manufacturing leadership to effectively plan the resources<br />\r\n    Contributes to and/or prepares a Supply Review Deck that reviews plans for a rolling 1-36 month period by family for approval in the monthly Supply Review (future IBP) process meetings<br />\r\n    Ensuring continuous improvement of all Supply Review and Supply Planning process utilizing key metrics and business results<br />\r\n    Maintains and utilizes a Resource Requirement Planning model of key resources, based on demonstrated capacity, to enable validation of the Supply Plan<br />\r\n    Compile an aggregate Supply Plan (volume and inventory) to meet the unconstrained demand plan represented in volume units and dollars of cost<br />\r\n    Ensures that issues and imbalances which occur during the monthly supply cycle are cross functionally reviewed, resolved or escalated with recommendations and alternatives for closure<br />\r\n    Identifies, develops and implements process improvement plans to optimize the Supply Management process to meet company objectives for quality, cost, responsiveness and growth<br />\r\n    Ensures Valid Achievable Supply Plans<br />\r\n    Performs other duties and responsibilities as requested or required <br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Skills Requirements:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Excellent communication, presentation and interpersonal skills<br />\r\n    Must be comfortable with ability to make presentations in front of small to medium size groups<br />\r\n    Ability to work with multiple business functions and find balance in conflicting priorities<br />\r\n    Advanced analytical and statistical abilities including concepts such as standard deviation, forecast error, bias, safety stock calculations and mean average percent error (MAPE)<br />\r\n    Intermediate level computer skills (Excel, Word, Access, PowerPoint)<br />\r\n    Knowledge and experience working in ERP systems such as SAP, Oracle, JD Edwards ', '', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '22 March, 2017', '2017-03-22', 56, '2017-03-22 01:06:50', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(36008970, 75712, 'Sr Php Developer', 'Staffing Solution and Services', '', '4', '0', '', '3', '8', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', '', '', '', 'New Delhi, ', 'PHP, MYSQL, Jquery, Java Script, HTML/CSS , Phpfox, Joomla, Mobile application.', '', '23', '16', '', '', 'Y', '', '   A contributor who has proven experience with Joomla and WordPress.<br />\r\n    Strong concepts working with Object Oriented Programming.<br />\r\n    Experience working with latest social networking technologies.<br />\r\n    Ability to write W3C standards compliant, cross browser compatible (IE7+, Firefox, Safari, Chrome) front-end markup in XHTML/CSS/AJAX (Jquery).<br />\r\n    Can work with a number of MVC frameworks and write strong, scalable code.<br />\r\n    Ability to write and performance optimize SQL queries for MySQL (PostgreSQL a plus)<br />\r\n    Mobile application development a big plus (iPhone, Android, Blackberry, WinMo)<br />\r\n    Experience programming APIs<br />\r\n    Strong work ethic and ability to construct complex projects quickly<br />\r\n    You should be enthusiastic about your work, results-driven and keen on developing in an agile environment.<br />\r\n    An ardent problem-solver.', '', '  Strong concepts working with Object Oriented Programming.<br />\r\n    Experience working with latest social networking technologies.<br />\r\n    Ability to write W3C standards compliant, cross browser compatible (IE7+, Firefox, Safari, Chrome) front-end markup in XHTML/CSS/AJAX (Jquery).<br />\r\n    Can work with a number of MVC frameworks and write strong, scalable code.<br />\r\n    Ability to write and performance optimize SQL queries for MySQL (PostgreSQL a plus)<br />\r\n    Mobile application development a big plus (iPhone, Android, Blackberry, WinMo)<br />\r\n    Experience programming APIs<br />\r\n    Strong work ethic and ability to construct complex projects quickly<br />\r\n    You should be enthusiastic about your work, results-driven and keen on developing in an agile environment.<br />\r\n    An ardent problem-solver.', '', 'Bachelors', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 October, 2016', '2016-10-24', 205, '2016-10-24 05:20:44', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(36115190, 0, 'Exellent opening for R2R with a CMMi level 5 organisation-Gurugram', 'PES HR Services', '', '2', '90', '05 Jun, 2017', '1', '6', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Delhi', 'accountant record to report account execuitive general accounting account associate general ledger', '', '10', '1', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Job Title: R2R<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking days: 5 days working , fixed Sat and Sun off,CAB Facility Available <br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary: As per market standard<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAssigned Role: General Accounting Ops Practitioner<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualification: Graduate / Post Graduate in Commerce and Accounting (MBA / M Com, B.Com)Accountant (CA inter / CWA inter) is preferred<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLocation: Gurugram<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterested candidates can send the CV at vijayata@peshr.com<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOVERALL PURPOSE OF JOB<br />\r\n<br />\r\nâ€¢ Work closely with the business unit of the customer organisation and provide them with financial accounting support in particular on period-end close of the General Ledger so as to be able to report financial results in a timely and accurate manner and also to support in exercising financial control over the General Ledger mainly through the process of account reconciliations. Also requires ability to prepare and present financial information through reports.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPROCESSES : General Accounting<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nResponsibilities/Authorities<br />\r\n<br />\r\nâ€¢ Responsible for financial accounting and reporting that has a material impact on key components of the clientâ€™s financial statements.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Responsible for the preparation, coordination and review of financial accounting analyses and journal entries to properly recognize actual results for material components of the clientâ€™s operations.<br />\r\nâ€¢ May be required to prepare a wide range of financial reporting applicable to scope of the assigned responsibilities.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Analyzes transactions, understands and explains variances, and proactively identifies potential problems and solutions.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Ability to recognize unusual transactions, trends, or variations and communicate findings to supervisor or manager.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Ability to manage/monitor accounting close responsibilities<br />\r\nâ€¢ Initiates and facilitates the sharing of process knowledge and best practices within the team and across the engagement, and is capable of impacting and influencing others.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Develops and maintains documentation on projects and team assignments.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Identifies, recommends and implements process improvements in procedures of team assignments.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Demonstrates analytical and problem solving skills<br />\r\nâ€¢ Coordinates and contributes to accounting processes.<br />\r\nâ€¢ Proactively recognizes problems within scope of responsibilities, draws from appropriate resources to identify options and solutions based on<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\nvijayata D<br />\r\nPhone : 022-49856823', 'Email: vijayata@peshr.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 022-49856823', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '07 March, 2017', '2017-03-07', 71, '2017-03-07 01:45:49', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(36247184, 69645, 'Business Development Manager', 'Habiliss Systems Private Ltd', '', '', '0', '', '3', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'Chennai, ', '', '', '', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', 'Note: Immediate Joinees or who can join in less than 20 days will be preferred. Interested candidates can walk-in to the below address on the below timings.<br />\r\nSalary will be best as per industry standards.<br />\r\nCandidates willing to work in night shifts are preferred. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nHabiliss Systems Pvt Limited.<br />\r\nJVL Plaza, 4th Floor, 501 Anna Salai,<br />\r\nTeynampet, Chennai -600018<br />\r\nLandmark - SIET College Signal (Opp to Voltas building).<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterview Time : 10.30 AM to 5.00 PM (Only Weekdays)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf you have any doubts, please give a call to 044-49086130 / 49086146 (10.00.AM to 6.00 PM)', '', '', 'We are currently hiring Business Development Executive / Senior BDE for our Business Development team. <br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBringing New business development and client follow-ups<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGenerate leads from social media and various sources <br />\r\n<br />\r\nIdentifying the prospect &Requirement gathering<br />\r\n<br />\r\nProposal writing - Responding to RFP/RFQ<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCoordinating with Pre-sales team and preparing on presentations<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCold Calling - Focusing on UK and US market / SME Market.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nScheduling appointments with Clients and Project Stakeholders to brief on the experience and expertise of the company.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEffectively communicate with clients to gain commitment to purchase<br />\r\n<br />\r\nProvide time-phased, qualified reports on achievement and activities<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMaintain accurate records of all contacts with clients<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFixing appointment with Decision makers over Phone & Email <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPreparing and maintaining the master report of entire activity, including daily activity, leads, follow ups, closure and future prospects.', '', 'UG: Any Graduate - Any Specialization, Graduation Not Required PG:Any Postgraduate - Any Specialization, Post Graduation Not Required Doctorate:Any Doctorate - Any Specialization, Doctorate Not Required', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '26 August, 2016', '2016-08-26', 264, '2016-08-25 23:34:04', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(36302530, 0, 'Digital Marketing Manager', 'The Creative Group', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '6', '12', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'El Segundo, CA', 'CMS, Development, Manager ', '', '1', '72', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Hiring - Digital Marketing Manager<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLocation - El Segundo<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFull Time<br />\r\nThe Creative Group is currently looking to fill a Digital Marketing Manager role for a company within the Retail Development Industry.<br />\r\nMust Have:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe ideal candidate MUST HAVE experience within the Retail Development Industry.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience launching & managing websites with a strong knowledge of best web practices, managing timelines & web projects and having an overall understanding of guiding the customer experience online.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKnowledge of SEO & Analytics - Background working in traffic analytics, CMS platform and SEO.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOverseeing email campaigns, PR and social media campaigns<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Requirements<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nClick here to Apply<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDepartment: Mktg/Comm Manager ', '', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '25 April, 2017', '2017-04-25', 22, '2017-04-25 08:03:33', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(36413081, 0, 'Great Opening with CSS Corp for Spanish Language Expert', 'CSS Corp.', '', '2', '90', '21 Jun, 2017', '1', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '', '', 'Chennai/Madras', 'Spanish Language Expert Spanish Language Specialist Spanish Language ', '', '9', '11', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'We are looking out for Spanish Language Expert in Customer Support Process.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience: 0 - 4 yrs<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Location - Chennai<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Designation - Spanish Language Expert<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExpertise:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Should be good in Spanish oral and written.<br />\r\n- Should be interested to work for customer support process.<br />\r\n- Must be willing to work in night shifts.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEducation:<br />\r\n*Any Bachelor\"s degree or demonstrated skill and/or related industry experience.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterested candidates kindly send across your updated resume to sripriya.ramanathan@csscorp.com or feel free to reach me at 044-61041800 Extn:7270034<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRegards,<br />\r\nHR Team.', 'Email: sripriya.ramanathan@csscorp.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 044-61041800', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '23 March, 2017', '2017-03-23', 55, '2017-03-23 03:03:47', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
