WI<br />\r\nContact Number<br />\r\n(262) 228-6733', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '22 March, 2017', '2017-03-22', 56, '2017-03-22 01:17:38', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(37733836, 0, 'AM/ Manager', 'Pinnacle Solutions', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '2', '7', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '', '', 'Bangalore', 'Tax Regulat y Finance Accounts Audit Assurance', '', '2', '117', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Manage the overall finance & accounts strategy for the location/ organisation including AR, AP, annual operation plan, cash flow planning etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Vendor empanelment & negotiations rate contracts & MOU\'s with vendors.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Employees payroll processing', 'Email: pinnacle_nm29@yahoo.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9768976834', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '26 April, 2017', '2017-04-26', 21, '2017-04-26 06:48:18', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(37883101, 0, 'DFT Engineer', 'Infotech Spectrum Inc', '', '1', '90', '26 Jun, 2017', '7', '12', 'Contract', '', '6 - 12 Months', '', '', '', 'US', '', '', 'San Jose, CA', 'JTAG, 1687, 1500, Scan, MBIST, LBIST, ATPG, BSCAN and LOBIST is a must.', '', '6', '59', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The Candidate would be focused on delivering DFT methodology solutions through automation and design for leading edge SoC microprocessor designs<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou will work with IP & integration design teams to understand the design and functional-mode behaviors of the logic & circuits.<br />\r\nYou will become familiar with the DFT designs of products to leverage their best-known methods and learn from their silicon experiences.<br />\r\nTake those learnings, feed it back into the centralized DFT team and deliver it to the other teams who would also benefit from the solutions.<br />\r\nYou will assist in the RTL, schematic implementation, pre-silicon validation & post silicon debug of these DFT features.<br />\r\nYou will be expected to deliver high-quality documentation for consumption by the pre/post-silicon teams who will use the DFT features.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualifications<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMust have a MSEE degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or Electrical Engineering<br />\r\nExperience with 5+ years of silicon design and validation Experience.<br />\r\nKnowledge of JTAG, 1687, 1500, Scan, MBIST, LBIST, ATPG, BSCAN and LOBIST is a must.<br />\r\nExperience with Agile and Scrum working flow is a plus.', 'Arjun<br /><br />\r\nInfotech Spectrum Inc<br /><br />\r\nSanta Clara, CA<br /><br />\r\nwww.infotechspectrum.com<br /><br />\r\n +1-408-372-0833', 'MSEE degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or Electrical Engineering ', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '28 March, 2017', '2017-03-28', 50, '2017-03-28 02:36:46', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(37893583, 28595, 'Hiring Web Designer  with Experience 1- 4 yrs', 'Browsewire Consulting Pvt. Ltd.', '', '', '0', '', '1', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Chandigarh, Mohali', '', '', '23', '16', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Are you a creative web designer having knowledge of Photoshop, HTML5, CSS, JS, Jquery willing to join our team of professionals & work on some of the cutting edge/challenging projects<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKeyskills :<br />\r\nPhotoshop, HTML5, CSS, JS, JQueryWeb Graphic Design, Web Savvy, Web User Interface Design, Illustration Tools, Multimedia Content Development, Understanding Browser Capabilities, Internet Presence, Verbal Communication<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience: 1-4 yrs<br />\r\nBenefits: Monthly Appraisal + Unlimited Planned Leaves<br />\r\nEducation: B.Tech, MCA, M.Tech<br />\r\nWe are looking for:<br />\r\n# Effective English Communication Skills<br />\r\n# Would be an advantage if able to manage CMS<br />\r\n# Passion for best design and a desire to develop new bold ideas<br />\r\n# Eye for details & able to match the expectations<br />\r\n# Logical Thinker along with the technical efficiency & imagination<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKNOW THE COMPANY:<br />\r\nBrowsewire Consulting Pvt. Ltd . India-based global IT solution provider focused on providing Web Application Development, Design and Consulting Solutions to SMEs across the globe. We plan to make a niche for ourselves by creating a unique Service & Products Model for our clients<br />\r\nVisit our Website: www.browsewire.net<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Type: Full-time<br />\r\n<br />\r\n', 'ishar@browsewire.net', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '13 January, 2017', '2017-01-13', 124, '2017-01-13 03:55:57', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(38405629, 0, 'HR Technical Developer/ Analyst', 'Cal State University, Chancellors Office,', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '7', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Long Beach, CA ', 'Oracle PeopleSoft HCM ', '', '23', '115', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Join our team at the California State University, Office of the Chancellor, and make a difference in providing access to higher education. We are currently seeking experienced candidates for the position of HR Technical Analyst/Programmer. The CSU Chancellor\'s Office, located on the waterfront adjacent to the Aquarium of the Pacific in downtown Long Beach, is the headquarters for the nation\'s largest and most diverse system of higher education. The CSU Chancellor\'s Office offers a premium benefit package that includes outstanding vacation, health, and dental plans; a fee waiver education program; membership in the California Public Employees Retirement System (PERS); and 14 paid holidays a year.<br />\r\n	<br />\r\nSalary<br />\r\n	<br />\r\nThe salary range for this classification is $4,372 to $9,401 per month.<br />\r\n	<br />\r\nPosition Information<br />\r\n	<br />\r\nThe California State University, Office of the Chancellor, is seeking a HR Technical Analyst/Programmer to provide technical support for CSU\'s Oracle / PeopleSoft HCM application within Information Systems. Information Systems\' Application Development area encompasses application support and upgrade activities for 23 campuses and the CSU Chancellor\'s Office (CO), integration with other third-party/external and/or internal systems, the consolidation of the HR databases implementation (CHRS Completion Project), and the HR/Student split project. The technical analyst requires proactive initiative to resolve the most complex HCM application issues in support/development areas that include implementation, system analysis, planning, design, development and support of the HR application. Specific technical support assignments may change at any time based on Application Development\'s projects and priorities, including supporting other applications within the area.<br />\r\n	<br />\r\nResponsibilities<br />\r\n	<br />\r\nUnder the general direction of the Project Manager, the HR Technical Analyst/Programmer will: provide technical production support for 23 CSU campuses and the Chancellor\'s Office by analyzing and troubleshooting campus application issues reported through Service-now cases; adhere to published Service Level Agreements (SLAs) and Application Development procedures; conduct unit, system, integration and regression testing of Oracle/PeopleSoft bundles, maintenance pack releases, PeopleTools and Oracle upgrades, and CSU updates and fixes; coordinate program and technical specification development/testing as well as time and cost estimates for customizations, upgrades and other project activity; this includes conducting conference calls or webinars with the HUG (HR User Group), sub-committees and campus representatives; participate on project teams as appropriate to implement new system functionality within the Oracle/PeopleSoft HR application; analyze, test and document custom modifications required to address CSU business requirements; support the HR / SA split activities as well as the CHRS implementation project; create and maintain technical documentation required to support the CSU Oracle/PeopleSoft HR application; collaborate with all Application Development teams to understand and resolve campus application issues as needed; produce deliverables that adhere to quality standards and comply with Application Development procedures and practices; undertake special projects as directed including working with other SME teams to facilitate cross training and coverage of all application areas.<br />\r\n	<br />\r\nQualifications<br />\r\n	<br />\r\nThis position requires a Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science or a related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience, as well as course work in the Oracle/PeopleSoft HR application; minimum 3-5 years of HR technical experience working with the Oracle PeopleSoft HCM application or other similar ERP is required; in-depth technical knowledge and experience with at least one HR module, such as Absence Management, Faculty, Security, etc. is preferred; excellent application implementation life cycle skills including experience developing requirements, fit/gap analysis, application configurations, technical specifications and the ability to translate business requirements into technical designs; excellent written and advanced verbal communication skills (including exceptional listening mentoring and collaboration abilities); working knowledge and experience with Human Resources practices and systems in a higher education environment and proficient knowledge of PeopleSoft rules based processing is preferred.', '', 'MBA HR', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '10 April, 2017', '2017-04-10', 37, '2017-04-10 05:43:02', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(38429085, 0, 'Peoplesoft HCM Lead with PUM Upgrade role in ', 'Addison, TX', '', '1', '90', '06 Jun, 2017', '4', '8', 'Contract', 'USD 30 - 50 Per Hour', '3 - 6 Months', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'New York, NY', 'PUM', '', '1', '115', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'PeopleSoft HCM Lead with strong functional knowledge of PeopleSoft 9.2 on PeopleTools 8.54/8.55 technology and familiar with the PeopleSoft Update Manager (PUM) process. Modules in HCM include HR, Benefits and Administration, T&L, NA Payroll, Candidate Gateway, TAM, eBenefits, ePay, eProfile and Pensions. Knowledge of ELM 9.2 is a plus. Strong communication and facilitative skills required. As the HCM lead, this position will require liaising and working with technical and development team to obtain status.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n*This position requires the consultant to be onsite M-F at the client site in New York city.', 'www.rigusinc.com', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '08 March, 2017', '2017-03-08', 70, '2017-03-08 04:01:19', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(38650105, 0, 'CAD Drafter / Estimator', 'ADK Design, Inc.', '', '1', '90', '29 Jun, 2017', '3', '7', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '10', 'US', '', '', 'Milwaukee, WI', 'Health Insurance Simple IRA Paid Time Off', '', '1', '101', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'CAD Drafter/Estimator<br />\r\n <br />\r\nADK Design, Inc. is looking for an experienced CAD Drafter/Estimator for our custom architectural fixture and millwork shop. This position is responsible for the creation of shop drawings and 3D modeling using AutoCAD, Cabinet Vision and Sketchup.<br />\r\n <br />\r\n <br />\r\nResponsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Review plans and specifications in preparing the drawings<br />\r\n    Take accurate site measurements<br />\r\n    Create accurate, detailed shop drawings and 3D modeling from architectural drawings in a timely manner<br />\r\n    Assist in project design<br />\r\n    Review drawings with staff to clarify details and address issues/questions<br />\r\n    Determine cost of producing architectural fixtures and provides quote information for customers<br />\r\n    Coordinates with architect/customer to revise, update, value-engineer the shop drawings/BOM<br />\r\n    Provide recommendations regarding feasibility of using alternative approaches, modifying or replacing materials to reduce cost or improve quality<br />\r\n    Create and send submittals to the reviewing architect or customer<br />\r\n    Utilize Cabinet Vision to create shop drawings and process the project on the CNC router<br />\r\n    Maintain data of every project and is well organized <br />\r\n    Provides backup support for Project Managers and when required<br />\r\n    Performs other duties as assigned<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n <br />\r\nRequirements/Qualifications:<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n    2 Year Tech Degree or Drafting Certification preferred<br />\r\n    At least 3 years of prior CAD drafting experience of architectural millwork and cabinet manufacturing<br />\r\n    At least 3 years of experience in cost estimation<br />\r\n    Must have a thorough understanding of drafting principles and strong analytic and mathematical capabilities<br />\r\n    Software proficiency at the intermediate to advanced level for AutoCAD, SketchUp, Cabinet Vision and Microsoft Office<br />\r\n    Works well in a fast-paced work environment with a strong commitment to meet deadlines<br />\r\n    Valid WI driverâ€™s license and reliable vehicle<br />\r\n    Selected candidate will be submitted to background check<br />\r\n', '', '2 Year Tech Degree or Drafting Certification preferred', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '31 March, 2017', '2017-03-31', 47, '2017-03-31 03:22:12', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(38805834, 0, 'URGENT HIRING FOR SALES BD', 'EQS Placement Pvt Limited Hiring For SALES EXECUTI', '', '2', '90', '28 Jun, 2017', '1', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Industry Standards', 'IN', '', '', 'Faridabad', 'SALES BD FIELD SALES SALES EXECUTIVE MARKETING EXECUTIVE SALES BD BUSINESS DEVELOPER BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT DIRECT SALES', '', '9', '80', '', '', '', '', '', '', '***HELLO CANDIDATES***<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nIMMEDIATE REQUIREMENTS FOR SALES EXECUTIVE (SALES BD) FOR HT MEDIA FOR DELHI NCR !!.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nJOB DESCRIPTION:-<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n**COMPANY - HT MEDIA <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n**LOCATION - DELHI NCR <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n**SALARY - 12-18K<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n**SHIFT - DAY SHIFT <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n**PROFILE - SALES EXECUTIVE (SALES BD) <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n**MINI. 1 YR EXPERIENCE IN SALES <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n**COMPLETE GRADUATION !!.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nFOR MORE INFORMATION CALL AND EMAIL:-<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nSACHIN<br />\r\n<br />\r\n8130199010<br />\r\n<br />\r\nsachin@eqsplacements.com', 'Email: sachin@eqsplacements.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 8130199010', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '30 March, 2017', '2017-03-30', 48, '2017-03-30 03:23:58', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(38873417, 21094, 'Software Development Engineer', 'Amazon Corporate LLC', '', '3', '0', '', '2', '6', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '13', 'US', '3026', '1254556', 'Brant, Seattle', 'Java, C++, Linux, Javascript, Oracle', '', '40', '29', '', '', 'Y', '', 'Work in our platform will provide the opportunity to contribute to the complete vertical stack of an SOA based system, which is horizontally connected to most systems in the larger Amazon ecosystem. Areas include business intelligence, web service implementation, database design, web based applications, UI design and usability optimization. Developers have the choice to specialize in particular areas or work throughout the system as a whole. <br />\r\nDevelopers in this position will use a variety of mainstream and open source technologies like Java, C++, Linux, Javascript, Oracle, as well as in-house Amazon technologies. The technical skills required for this role include strong object-oriented design and programming in Java or C++. Some scripting, SQL and data modeling is helpful. An understanding and experience with web based technologies is essential. These may include HTML, HTTP, Javascript, JSON, AJAX, apache, tomcat. Experience working pragmatically under deadlines with operational software is highly desired. In addition the role will offer project management, leadership and system design opportunities.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPreferred Qualifications<br />\r\n<br />\r\nStrong, object-oriented design and coding skills (C/C++ and/or Java preferably on a UNIX or Linux platform)<br />\r\nKnowledge of Perl or other scripting languages a plus<br />\r\nExperience with distributed (multi-tiered) systems, algorithms, and relational databases<br />\r\nExperience in optimization mathematics (linear programming, nonlinear optimization)<br />\r\nAbility to effectively articulate technical challenges and solutions<br />\r\nDeal well with ambiguous/undefined problems; ability to think abstractly<br />\r\nPrevious technical internship(s) preferred<br />\r\nGraduate degree a plus', '', 'SDEs at Amazon work on real world problems on a global scale, own their systems end to end and influence the direction of our technology that touches our customers around the world. <br />\r\nWithin Amazon, Customer Service Technology is looking for a software development engineer to work on the in-house relationship management platform that delivers one of the industryâ€™s best customer satisfaction scores (ACSI). Our platform is used 24x7 by thousands of users globally in multiple languages who are satisfying millions of Amazon and our partnerâ€™s customers. <br />\r\nDevelopers in the CS technology team have the opportunity to work on software services that are designed to adapt to the evolving businesses of Amazon while improving the quality and productivity of our operations teams. These gains are driven by the controls and feedback of our systems, business metrics and user community to enable continuous improvement to our software, system design, and development processes. Our software allows our userbase to likewise improve their quality, timeliness, efficiency and policy adherence of customer support interactions.', '', 'Bachelor\'s degree in computer science, computer engineering or related technical discipline', 'Formal', 'US Citizen, GC, H1B', 'Corp-Corp, W2-Permanant, W2-Contract, 1099-Contract', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '13 February, 2017', '2017-02-13', 93, '2017-02-12 22:07:48', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(38959741, 99293, 'Education Counsellor', 'Balaji HR Consultancy', '', '10', '0', '', '1', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'Chandigarh, Delhi, Bhopal, Patna, Kanpur, Guwahati, ', 'Communication Skills, Confident, Education Counsellor', '', '36', '91', '', '', 'Y', '', 'Candidate should be Graduate, Post Graduate', '', 'Good Communication Skills<br />\r\nCandidate should be confident<br />\r\nCalling to the student.<br />\r\nFollow up to the customer<br />\r\n', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '12 December, 2016', '2016-12-12', 156, '2016-12-12 04:46:54', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(39258734, 0, 'Required Sales Officer & Sr. Sales officer For Mandovi Motors', 'Mandovi Motors Pvt. Ltd.', '', '1', '90', '29 Jun, 2017', '0', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Bangalore', 'Retail Automobile Sales Retail Automobile Sales ', '', '7', '44', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Requirements<br />\r\n<br />\r\na) Graduate/Diploma holders with 1 to 3 years of experience<br />\r\n<br />\r\nb) Fluent in English & Kannada , and other languages are added advantages<br />\r\n<br />\r\nc) Good Communication skills and convincing ability.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nd) Should have Two Wheeler Vehicle and should have Driving License of 2 & 4 Wheeler.<br />\r\n<br />\r\ne) Should have good knowledge of local Topography.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nf) Target Oriented and Should have Go getter attitude<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Description<br />\r\n<br />\r\na) Shall follow the procedures pertaining to the Marketing to both the individual and Corporate Customers.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nb) Shall attend Daily Marketing Brief.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nc) Shall be responsible for physical delivery of the vehicles during the peak hours.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nd) Shall collect the outstanding payments.<br />\r\n<br />\r\ne) Shall introduce new customers.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nf) Maintaining and developing relationships with customers via meetings, telephone calls and emails.<br />\r\n<br />\r\ng) Visiting customers to prospect for business and gaining a clear understanding of customers and requirements.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nh) Acting as a contact between a company and its existing and potential markets.<br />\r\n<br />\r\ni) Negotiating the terms of an agreement and closing sales.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nj) Gathering market and customer information.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nk) Representing the organization at events and demonstrations.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nl) Negotiating variations in price, delivery and specifications with managers.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nm) Reviewing own sales performance, aiming to meet or exceed targets.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nn) Making accurate, rapid cost calculations, and providing customers with quotations.', 'Email: hrd@mandovi.in<br />\r\nTelephone: 9880912403', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '31 March, 2017', '2017-03-31', 47, '2017-03-31 02:59:44', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(39339044, 0, 'Resident Property Manager', 'JANARDAN FARMS AND RESORTS LLP', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '0', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Lucknow', 'Sales, Procurement, Inventory, Manufacturing, Planning, ECO and Finance)', '', '32', '113', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Job Title: Resident Property Associate ~ enrolling of the Lodging units and coordinating the stay of our guest in those enrolled lodging facility<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Location: Anywhere in India<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCompany Name: Janardan Farms and Resorts<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Description:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n1) Resident Property Associate has to operate at the above mention city, under the instructions of the Manager (Admin) in Lucknow head office.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2) Under this scheme, the Resident Property Associate needs to identify the property proximity to the tourist of interest place, most suitable for housing our guest, getting the property on rent and enrolling it under our scheme under the guidance of Manager (admin).<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3) Resident Property Associate needs to enrol fresh property under our banner of Janardan Home stays, whose details are given in Annexure 1 & 2 of this document.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4) Resident Property Associate will coordinate with our guest booked to such property under the Banner of Janardan Home Stays, guiding them to the property and ensuring it that they are comfortably lodged and are happy with the arrangements.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5) Resident Property Associate Need to have high self-confidence to achieve the above said proficiency target and should not indulge in any experiment with our system. He should be confident with his hospitality abilities and ultimately leading to comfortable experience of the guest in his city of operation.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6) Resident Property Associate must possess communication skills in terms of the ability to negotiate, convince, self and influence professionals, corporate employees and/or tourist ultimately leading to comfortable experience of the guest in his city of operation.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n7) Arranging all travelling requirement of the guests and visiting the Property along with the clients to ensure that the commitment with the clients are met at all levels right from start to end of the visit.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n8) Achieve targets.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n9) Customer service/ customer relations - a proactive attitude with the clients is needed & the ability to deal promptly with any issues as and when they arise.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n10) Completion of all relevant paperwork accurately and promptly in compliance to the local prevailing law of the land.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n11) Responsible for safekeeping of record related clients.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n12) Plan and promote new scheme/ program for customers.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nReimbursement:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n1) Salary will be provided of 3 Lacs per annum.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2) Salary will be proportionate to the target achievement.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3) Reimbursement will be done on monthly basis on or before 10th of every month.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4) There will be a local travelling allowance of Rs. 2000/- per month & nothing more will be paid on this account.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5) No advance in any form will be released under this setup.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nTargets:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· You are required to maintain 200 lodging units in your city of operation for our guests in that particular month and with a minimum business of Rs. 5 Lac per month.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nTermination of appointment:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· For not at all achieving of the target for 3 subsequent months, your termination will be processed without any reimbursement or payment and no claim will be entertained in this regard.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesired Candidate Profile:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEducation<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPG/UG in MBA/ BHM/ Marketing, in Hotel management or equivalent. (Can be relaxed for Applicant having adequate experience in his previous job profile)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n1) Able to achieve targets with previous successful experience.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2) Confident, friendly, flexible and enthusiastic with a good sense of humor.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3) Committed to achieving excellent customer service.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4) Good time management and organizational skills.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5) Ability to self-motivate and to work without supervision.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6) Experience of team management and staff motivation.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n7) Marketing Experience of working within the Hotel industry.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n8) Able to work well under pressure.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n9) Good team player.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n10) Excellent written and spoken English<br />\r\n<br />\r\n11) Good knowledge of common IT programmes, including EXCEL, WORD, and email.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n12) Driving License<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nCompany Profile:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJanardan Farms and Resorts<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n1) Established in 2010, it is owned and operated by Janardan Farms and Resorts. We strive to be the best provider of lodging at a very economical affordable price all over Pan India destination.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2) We are in process of introducing Janardan Home Stays system, a step ahead to provide a very basic and economical stay arrangement better than the hotel lodging to our guests.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3) We are also working on promoting eco-tourism as we believe that eventually that is where the whole natural tourism sector will head towards.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4) Eco-tourism is the tourism of visiting an ecosystem in such a way as to leave a minimal impact on the environment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5) This helps conserve the natural ecosystem for our future generations so that they too could enjoy the calmness of nature as we are now.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6) This is what has given us to install solar panels / solar water heaters over the roofs which power Janardan Resort.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAnnexure 1<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nJanardan Home Stays<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAthithi Devo Bhava<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIndians consider it a huge honor to have guests in their home, and go out of their way to please them. There\'s nothing like Indian hospitality. Sadly, most visitors who come to India and stay in hotels never get to experience true Indian hospitality.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJanardan home stays is coordinating with lot of home stays properties, duly verified and consolidated to gather and displayed in our portals for easy booking by the guest at his choicest destination.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nBenefits with Janardan Home Stays:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1) Distinctive and Character full Accommodations -- There\'s no better way to experience the incredibly diversity and charm of India than at a home stay. The options are almost endless and include plantation bungalows, and remote rural cottages.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2) Personalized Service -- In contrast to a hotel, a Janardan Home Stays usually only has a few rooms. This guarantees that guests receive plenty of individual attention.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3) Indian Culture -- Regardless, staying with an Indian family is the easiest way of finding out about Indian culture and way of life. Many guests and hosts find that they bond with each other so much, that they keep in touch long after the vacation is over.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4) Local Knowledge -- The wealth of information that the hosts have about their local area makes deciding what to see and do a breeze. Many hosts are delighted to show their guests around their local area, providing them with invaluable insights that simply aren\'t available from a guide book.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5) Home Cooked Food -- By staying at a Janardan Home Stays, you\'ll be able to taste authentic Indian home cooked food, made to order. It\'s a lot lighter, and has more variation and flavor than restaurant food. Some Janardan Home Stays even welcome their guests into their kitchen, and let them watch and participate in the cooking process.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6) Unique Activities -- As a guest at a Janardan Home Stays, the focus is on you, and your likes and preferences. The hosts are usually very accommodating and will put a great deal of effort into arranging activities that are of interest to you. These activities will vary depending on location. Exploring a coffee plantation in Coorg, watching a polo match in Rajasthan, herding animals in remote northern India, village visits, picnics, and temple tours are just some of the options. Guests are often invited to attend weddings, or other festivals that are happening, as well.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAnnexure 2<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nStaying at a Janardan Home Stays in India is all about immersing yourself in India. Join our JANARDAN HOME STAYS program and earn 2 times than your existing monthly rental for your spare room/house / flat/ land in any location.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. If you have a spare room , we can weave it to a revenue generation mechanism , through our JANARDAN home stay system<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. You having choice to give access to your property only to family travellers, couples, individuals male or female or old couples,<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. Before each booking to your property system ask permission sharing the details of the travellers, and on your acceptance, the system will book your room, 100% safe booking.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. 20% of the booking amount will be deducted by Janardan Resort as revenue sharing; the rest amount will be transferred to you at the time of customer check-in.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. For enrolment please message us or call, our Manager will inspect your property, & will enrol it to our system, with a small MOU agreement between us.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nRecruiter:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nName: Mr. Atul Singh<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAddress: Janardan Farms and Resorts<br />\r\n<br />\r\n537/181, Dilkush Market, Lucknow, Uttar Pradesh<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEmail Address: hr@janardanresort.in<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTelephone & WhatsApp: 8808311777; 8808133777; 7678810007; 9795005888', 'Email: hr@janardanresort.in<br />\r\nTelephone: 8808311777', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '26 April, 2017', '2017-04-26', 21, '2017-04-26 07:22:30', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(39498053, 0, 'Architectural Intern', 'PGAL', '', '2', '90', '29 Jun, 2017', '4', '12', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Austin, TX', 'Architecture ', '', '6', '98', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Responsibilities / Qualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQUALIFICATIONS/RESPONSIBILITIES:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe are seeking to hire a talented architectural intern, with 1-5 years of experience in a wide variety of project types including corporate/commercial, public/institution and retail/hospitality.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCandidate must demonstrate working knowledge of AutoCAD or REVIT with strong drafting skills and the ability to work in a fast-paced environment on multiple projects in varying stages as part of a project team and individually. REVIT experience preferred with knowledge of other graphic programs a plus.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBachelor\'s degree from an accredited university in Architecture or related field preferred.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMust be legally authorized to work in the United States for any employer without sponsorship.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPGAL offers a diverse and energetic working environment and benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and 401(k) plans.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPGAL is an equal opportunity / E-verify employer. Protected veterans and persons with disabilities under applicable state and federal law are encouraged to apply.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCONTACT:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTo apply, please send your resume and work samples to careers@pgal.com and indicate which position as well as location you are applying to in your email.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAn Equal Opportunity Employer Females/ Minorities/ Veterans/Disabled', 'careers@pgal.com', 'Bachelor\'s degree in Architecture', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '31 March, 2017', '2017-03-31', 47, '2017-03-31 03:19:16', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(39743496, 74820, 'VP IT Infrastrcuture / Servers /application', 'Value C Consulting Services Pvt Ltd', '', '', '90', '12 Jun, 2017', '2', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '', '1325164', 'Mumbai', 'IT - Hardware & Networking, Server', '', '41', '123', '', '', '', '', '', 'Sr IT infrastructure and Application.. can message us of their interest on 09167771333', 'Manage Technology, infrastructure, servers, VPN, Firewall, UTM...pls sms us on 9167771333...we will call you back.', '', 'Any Postgraduate and Graduate', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '14 March, 2017', '2017-03-14', 64, '2017-03-14 04:36:08', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', '');
INSERT INTO `jobs` (`jobid`, `uid`, `job_title`, `company_name`, `about_company`, `vacancies`, `jobs_active`, `job_expiry`, `work_experience_min`, `work_experience_max`, `job_type`, `contract_rate`, `contract_duration`, `internship_salary`, `internship_duration`, `salary`, `job_country`, `job_state`, `job_city`, `location`, `key_skills`, `job_url`, `industry`, `functional_area`, `youtube_url`, `telecommute`, `security_clearance`, `benefits`, `requirements`, `instruction`, `description`, `how_apply`, `academic_degree`, `dress_code`, `WorkAuthorize`, `PreferredEmployment`, `us_citizen`, `gc`, `ead`, `h1b`, `corp_corp`, `w2_permanant`, `w2_contract`, `1099_contract`, `contract_hire`, `date`, `count_date`, `days_ago`, `datetime`, `country_from`, `status`, `facebook_url`, `twitter_url`, `gplush_url`, `message`) VALUES
(39781693, 74820, 'Information Technology in Networking', 'Amrutha Business Solutions', '', '', '90', '12 Jun, 2017', '3', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '', '436518', 'Chennai/Madras', 'Cissp, Cisa, Ceh, Networking, Information Technology, Operating Systems, programming, systems, database, information, retrieval, dba, systems, db, systems', 'http://amrutha.com', '24', '32', '', '', '', '- Lead the Company IT setup and enduring services, ensuring we have an accountable, proactive competent support service for the various technologies deployed by Company for the service of clients, customers and in-house requirements<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Establish, enhance and maintain an ITIL-literate service that meets the needs of Company\'s changing business environment<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Be accountable for all service performance delivered by IT delivered in India while maintaining agreed Helpdesk SLA- s<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Ensure that new or existing compliance regulatory standards are met, specifically in the areas of ISO 9001, ISO 27001 and PCI.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Develop the role of the Helpdesk ensuring an effective service is maintained while improving the implementation of standard processes. Managing all assigned Level1 and Level 2 Helpdesk tickets.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Prepare and deliver the various reports, statistics and KPIs associated with effective service delivery at Company<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Develop and implement the transfer of key support services to the Company India operation<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Develop effective working relationships with leaders in our business creating a culture of shared ownership and delivering accountability in service delivery<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Be an active member of the IT leadership team (ITLT) contributing to the overall mission of the IT function<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Be accountable to the Chief Technology Officer (and by extension the senior management of Company) for delivery of service across with the rest of the company.', '', 'You can reach us here: 9841681004, 9841681002', 'Looking for a should Information Technology in Networking who have an experience into cyber forensic, networking. We have this requirement earliest as possible.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIT Lead, Global Service Centre<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesired Qualifications, Training and Experience :<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Degree or masters qualification in technology, IT or technical discipline<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- A Qualification in ITIL or service delivery is desirable<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- At least 10 years- experience in the delivery of services in IT, Software Development and in the management and support of complex systems<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Experience in working in a multinational environment<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Extensive project management experience in leading large IT/Software projects<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Detailed working knowledge of applied information technology - application configuration and support, application hosting, middleware, networks, voice systems, end-user computing etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPersonal Attributes required :<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Understanding of service metrics and their role in service delivery planning and accountability<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Proven history of formation and maintenance of good relationships both inside the business and with third parties<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Clear understanding and vision of the opportunities offered by cloud computing, commoditised IT services, - internet of things- and the role that specialised third parties can play in the construction and delivery of IT service for Abtran<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Extensive experience in the service / contact-center / identity management industry<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Proven team-leadership capabilities as well as a demonstrable record of team and people development<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Good written and oral English communication skills - ability to address audiences and to speak clearly on the telephone<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Proven ability to focus on the delivery of documentation and reports and to keep disparate stakeholders connected<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Strong leadership skills - ability to lead when the road ahead is not clear, ability to sell an idea or a vision and in doing so to take account of the needs of all stakeholders<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Ability to deal with sudden changes in agenda, direction or speed of programs and priorities<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Motivated and enthusiastic - can work on own initiative without direction', 'You can reach us here: 9841681004, 9841681002', 'Graduate', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '14 March, 2017', '2017-03-14', 64, '2017-03-14 03:10:46', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(39885283, 74820, 'Political Writers opening in Media company', 'SB Promedia', '', '', '90', '14 Jun, 2017', '0', '3', 'Contract', 'INR 50 - 200 Per Hour', '3 - 6 Months', '', '', '2', 'IN', '', '435795', 'Pune', 'Writers, Content Writing, Articles', '', '3', '74', '', '', '', '', '', 'Contact Person : - Prakash - 02025439239', 'Intelligent & Ambitious young people with dynamic & Pleasing personality.Good communication skills, fluency in Marathi & English.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPreferable Experienced & 1+ years Knowledge in film production house/Political/TV Channels/Media/advertising company.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Type: For Documentary Films<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Location: Pune, Maharashtra<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequired education: Bachelor\'s<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequired experience: 1 year Experience<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequired language: Marathi', '', 'Bachelor\'s', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '16 March, 2017', '2017-03-16', 62, '2017-03-16 02:10:04', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(39938834, 93107, 'JUNIOR CONTENT WRITER', 'XENTRIC TECHNOLOGIES PVT LIMITED', '', '2', '0', '', '0', '2', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'KOLKATA', 'BLOG WRITING, WEB CONTENT , BROCHURE WRITING, LEAFLET WRITING,SMM WRITING, SEO WRITING', '', '23', '52', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Desired Candidate Profile:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nA) Min 6Months - 12 Months exp in Web Content Writing, Blog writing , Digital Marketing Writing on various Industries & topics as given.Exp in Brochures, Leaflets Writing will be an Added Advantage<br />\r\n<br />\r\nB) Min Qualification Graduation with excellent Computer Skills in MS Office ie MS Word & PowerPoint. Knowledge in Multimedia will be an Added Advantage. He/She must have English Medium Background/ Convent Background.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC) Candidate should have excellent Written Skills in English.Female Candidate Preferred.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD) Salary wont be a BAR for the right Candidate. Interested Candidates apply with CV & Write Up Samples to sreelagna@xentrictechnologies.com or Call 9836040404 to know more.', 'INTERESTED CANDIDATES APPLY WITH CV TO sreelagna@xentrictechnologies.com', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '20 October, 2016', '2016-10-20', 209, '2016-10-20 06:28:55', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(39955257, 0, 'HR Coordinator', 'Vertisystem Inc', '', '1', '90', '25 Jun, 2017', '1', '6', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'San Mateo, CA', 'employee engagement ', '', '1', '115', '', '', '', '', ' Qualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Bachelorâ€™s degree with at least 2 years of coordinator/administrative or equivalent experience<br />\r\n    Strong interpersonal communications skills with the experience to interact comfortably with employees, executives and individuals with diverse socioeconomic backgrounds<br />\r\n    Self-starter, able to work independently yet function well as a team member<br />\r\n    Ability to organize information and present findings effectively<br />\r\n    Project management and event planning skills are a plus: execute programs/offerings end-to-end<br />\r\n    Excellent organizational skills, critical thinking skills, and possesses the ability to address multiples priorities, be insightful to anticipate needs drawing from past experience and meet deadlines<br />\r\n    Must be customer service and detail oriented<br />\r\n    Highly resourceful ambitious team-player, with the ability to also be extremely effective independently. Comfortable with a fast paced environment<br />\r\n    Competent at managing numerous projects at once<br />\r\n    Excellent oral, written, negotiation, and interpersonal communication skills<br />\r\n    Ability to partner, influence and communicate effectively with leaders at all levels and across an organization and site<br />\r\n    Excellent communication (written and verbal) and interpersonal skills<br />\r\n    Proven relationship building and collaborative skills<br />\r\n    Ability to work with high degree of autonomy<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHave a Great day ahead!!', '', 'Employee Engagement Coordinator<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLooking for an outgoing, energetic individual that will help shape our commitment to CSR as we build out a program that services the communities in which we live and work. Through our commitment to corporate giving, we will support nonprofit programs and organizations that help make our communities better, stronger and more vibrant place to live, work and do business.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAs members of the Human Resources team, we are stewards of the companyâ€™s greatest assets: Our People and our Culture.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCome join the Employee Engagement team. The purpose of our team is to inspire employees to connect and be more than they thought possible! Weâ€™re looking for a passionate Employee Engagement coordinator to engage in a fast paced environment managing programs that serve and engage our employees. You will partner with site business leaders, site HR leaders and employee groups to drive employee engagement initiatives across specific site(s), community outreach, volunteering, employee recognition, and other experiences unique to the sites supported. This position reports to the Senior Manager, Employee Engagement.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKey Responsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Manage master employee engagement event and volunteer calendar<br />\r\n    Roll up your sleeves to be part of the team managing Diversity Employee Events and CSR activities<br />\r\n    Provide administrative support for team operations<br />\r\n    Support content updates under the web portal that manages employee donations and matches volunteer opportunities<br />\r\n    Use web analytics measurement tools to regularly provide reports on community programs, employee match and volunteer metrics<br />\r\n    Coordinate recruitment of volunteers for various activities<br />\r\n    Support a network of local champions at various locations for employee engagement events<br />\r\n    Respond to inquiries being routed to the Employee Engagement email box<br />\r\n    Partner with various teams to leverage and share best practices across organizations<br />\r\n    In conjunction with PR and other related departments, orchestrate outside tour requests<br />\r\n    Oversee coordination of employee/organizational hackathons.<br />\r\n    Engage and manage strategic partnership sponsorships packages<br />\r\n    Process invoices and work closely with financial budget to stay within budget<br />\r\n    Communicate and conduct raffles for sporting and special event tickets<br />\r\n    Potential travel to other locations in order to effectively develop & implement plans<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEmployee Recognition / Years of Service Awards:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Push timely communication emails to managers and recipients for years of service anniversaries<br />\r\n    Work directly with award vendor to order and ship monthly awards<br />\r\n    Run monthly employee data reports for recipient listings<br />\r\n    Identify discrepancies in research appropriate outcome', 'Manju Singh<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTeam Lead - Talent Acquisition Executive | 510-894-6200/ 510-361-0618(Dir', 'Bachelorâ€™s degree with at least 2 years of coordinator/administrative or equivalent experience', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '27 March, 2017', '2017-03-27', 51, '2017-03-27 03:48:40', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(40078211, 0, 'Assistant Manager', 'Tertium Technology Pvt. Ltd', '', '2', '90', '02 Jul, 2017', '2', '6', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Delhi', 'Supp t Financial Operational analysis to facilitate inf med decision-making ', '', '1', '117', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Develop an understanding of any new industry, the growth prospects, industry dynamics, value chain, competition etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nM&A - Target Identification and Analysis:<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Prepare list of possible acquisition/JV targets in an industry<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Evaluate the targets based on defined criteria<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Gatherintelligence on shortlisted targets including financial information, capabilities, technologies, infrastructure, credentials, customers, reputation, management etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Essentially be part of the core team managing the M&A project lifecycle - identify opportunities, screen targets, initiate dialogues, prepare business proposals, develop financial models & returns analysis framework, manage Due Diligence, negotiate and close transactions<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBusiness Proposals - Organic as well as Inorganic Ventures: <br />\r\n<br />\r\no Prepare information packet covering Strategic Rationaleand Quantification of Benefits<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Assist in preparing detailed Business Plans<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Support active projects and live transactions<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDevelop a basic understanding of financial models, valuation methodologies and risk-return frameworks<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBusiness Analytics :- <br />\r\n<br />\r\no Understand the current Intertek portfolio - Industries, services and customers<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Support Financial and Operational analysis to facilitate informed decision-making<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Actively engage in Competitive Benchmarking and Positioning<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Lead research on sector dynamics to facilitate idea generation for growth<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Conduct Service and Product Portfolio Reviews', '    Company Name: Tertium Technology Pvt. Ltd<br />\r\n    Email: rashmi.hr@tertiumtech.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 8041288824', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 April, 2017', '2017-04-03', 44, '2017-04-03 02:57:37', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(40134544, 74820, 'UI/UX Designer', 'Provisions Group', '', '', '90', '12 Jun, 2017', '1', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '11', 'US', '', '', 'Lincolnshire, IL', 'Angular 2, React, Ionic, Kendo UI, Apache Cordova, Telerik NativeScript', '', '23', '16', '', '', '', '', 'Work with various groups and users to gather requirements<br />\r\nDesigning of user interfaces; Identify design problems and devise solutions<br />\r\nMake strategic design and UX decisions related to functions and features<br />\r\nFacilitate product visions<br />\r\nColor theory design and layout<br />\r\nUser Acceptance Testing<br />\r\nDevelopment with Angular 2, React, Ionic, Kendo UI, Apache Cordova, Telerik NativeScript', '', 'We are seeking a UI/UX Designer to assist in developing, enhancing, and supporting a handful of web-based applications - both internal and client facing. One of the biggest initiatives this individual will be partaking in is making these applications accessible via the web in addition to tablets. This individual will be involved in re-designing applications and making interface changes.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThey will join a team of 5 and will work in environment where they will wear many hats and work with little direction. Thus, they will have the opportunity to work and make decisions independently and creatively. This is an HTML5 and MS SQL environment.', 'Please contact Paul DeGuzman for more information.', 'Any Postgraduate and Graduate', 'Formal', 'H1B', 'W2-Permanant', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '14 March, 2017', '2017-03-14', 64, '2017-03-14 05:39:24', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(40423365, 0, 'Interviews for General manager- Crew Rostering', 'Career Innovators Hiring For Career Innovators Pvt', '', '1', '0', '', '3', '6', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '6', 'IN', '1276', '434089', 'New Delhi, Gurgaon, Delhi', ' rostering  airlines  Routers', '', '8', '66', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'We are looking for General Manager- Crew Rostering for a Leading Airline Company based out in Gurgaon.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n***Airlines Experience Must***<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Description<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCREW ROSTERING MANAGER -LF<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Purpose<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nManage the monthly roster planning section and act as a focal point of contact with Flight Operations, Sky Cargo and Service Delivery managers to ensure continuity in monthly Crew Roster communications and operations.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nManage the complex Roster planning functions of Flight Crew and Cabin Crew rostering and ensure effective distribution of crew resources. This includes governing the Pairing construction and Pilot and Cabin crew monthly rostering process. Ensure an integrated approach among multiple planning teams and that the departments standards and procedures are in line with DGCA regulations, business requirements and policies.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJOB ACCOUNTABILITIES LINKED TO OBJECTIVE AREAS<br />\r\n<br />\r\nManage all aspects of Flight and Cabin crew rostering, ensuring the product is in compliant with international and local regulatory guidelines on legality and fatigue. Develop and maintain service level agreements (SLAs) between Crew Planning, Crew Scheduling, Pre-Operations, Sky Cargo, Flight Operations and Service Delivery departments. Monitor the SLAs through regular meetings and updates, and provide solutions to accomplish mutual strategic and tactical business needs.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nManage, maintain and develop rostering processes and systems to enhance quality of the rosters and achieve efficiency and optimal use of crew resources. Monitor the changing requirements of Flight Operations, Sky Cargo and Service Delivery to ensure rosters are in line with business requirement.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDetermine customisation requirements for the Crew Rostering system and ensure that cost effective solutions and tools are available to best meet the business objectives. Effectively communicate and liaise with stakeholders to ensure vision and requirements are translated to functionality of the systems.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nManage the rostering business analysis on all system development, testing and acceptance. This includes recommending and analysis of new process, testing system functionality, documenting specifications, new process mapping, requirement gathering from users and training end users.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFacilitate and lead meetings with Flight Training Planning Manager, Pre-Operations Manager, Crew Scheduling Manager and Crew Planning Controller to coordinate monthly rosters, build parameters and provide visibility of the expected workload for future months. Effectively coordinate monthly meetings with crew planning controllers / officers and crew Pairing controller to discuss and analyse various planning issues and strategies.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlay active role in the pilot rostering operational and policy meetings with Flight Operations and Service Delivery. Represent rostering by coordinating with crew planning controllers for new route start-up coordination.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHave a comprehensive understanding of the Emirates Fatigue Risk Management (FRMS) and play a major role in the FRMS team. Play a lead role in analysis and systems development and impart knowledge of our operating schedule, to continually revise and evolve the current rostering practices.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInitiate and continually update Roster Planning sections of Crew Operations Procedure Manual so that the team have reference document and standard operating procedures. Negotiate improvements with customer departments in common working practice areas and suggest IT systems enhancements to ensure efficient operation and attain improvements. Provide statistical Key Performance summary reports of the rosters to senior management on monthly basis.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nManage, train and motivate a team of crew planning controllers and officers to ensure consistent and efficient service is provided to all stakeholders. Provide active leadership for the team and practice effective performance management to ensure that required results are achieved.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3+ years experience in crew planning or a related environment of which 1years to be in a Managerial or Supervisory level.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary Bracket- Best in the Industry<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCall on to Apply:-<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCall +91 9654353696<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterested Candidates please send your Cvs on<br />\r\n<br />\r\njobs@careerinnovators.com<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWebsite :www.careerinnovators.com<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCorporate Office <br />\r\nCAREER INNOVATORS PVT.LTD Corporate Tower- 2nd floor, Dwarka Mor metro station, opposite Metro Pillar no 766, New Delhi Land Mark Above Yes Bank<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIMPORTANT NOTE: We are the Authorized Consultants for a lot Companies in India and Dubai Hence DO NOT CHARGE any Placement Charges Before or after your Job (FREE RECRUITMENT) www.careerinnovators.com<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n**** Thank You for Making us No.1 HR Consultant www.careerinnovators.com ****', 'Email: jobs@careerinnovators.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9654353696', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 February, 2017', '2017-02-24', 82, '2017-02-24 01:37:12', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(40459725, 18491, 'PHP Developer', 'Leom Internatioanal', '', '20', '0', '', '1', '17', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '8', '', '', '', 'Chandigarh, ', '', '', '23', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Candidate Must have knowledge of MVC/OOP along with any PHP framework. Demonstrable knowledge of web technologies including HTML, CSS, Javascript, AJAX etc Good knowledge of relational databases, developing web services. <br />\r\nPHP developer with 1.5 year   --  3 years experience   <br />\r\n<br />\r\nSkills: PHP, MYSQL, Wordpress,  Any PHP Framework<br />\r\nSalary - Hike on previous salary <br />\r\nSalary Range  - 15k to 30k', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '15 November, 2016', '2016-11-15', 183, '2016-11-14 22:45:27', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(40756098, 68533, 'Urgent opening for Technical Support Engineer for Gurgaon Location ', 'Acreaty Management Consultant  Pvt Ltd', '', '', '0', '', '6', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'Gurgaon, ', '', '', '9', '32', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Skill and Knowledge Qualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nâ€¢ Proper phone etiquette;<br />\r\nâ€¢ Ability to speak and write clearly and accurately;<br />\r\nâ€¢ Demonstrated proficiency in typing and grammar;<br />\r\nâ€¢ Knowledge of relevant software computer applications and equipment;<br />\r\nâ€¢ Knowledge of customer service principles and practices;<br />\r\nâ€¢ Effective listening skills;<br />\r\nâ€¢ Willingness to co-operate with others and work to the greater good;<br />\r\nâ€¢ Multi-tasking capabilities;', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '26 October, 2016', '2016-10-26', 203, '2016-10-26 04:33:13', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(40855202, 0, 'Parts Counter Assistant', 'Hanna Trailer & RV Supply', '', '2', '90', '28 Jun, 2017', '2', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Oak Creek, WI', 'Health Insurance, & paid vacation', '', '7', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Hanna Trailer & RV Supply, Inc is looking for an experienced Parts Counter person, Parts Counter experience and experience with trailers or RV would be a huge plus.  This position involves taking care of walk-in customers, assisting in house technicians with needed parts and assisting on-line customers to the right parts and accessories..<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDuties & Responsibilities<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Process parts orders for phone, store, website, & in house Service Department<br />\r\n    Answering phones<br />\r\n    Parts look up and special orders<br />\r\n    Maintaining inventory, placing daily and weekly stock orders<br />\r\n    Year-end inventory<br />\r\n    Load and unload shipments or parts & supplies<br />\r\n    Maintain store shelves and pricing levels<br />\r\n    Maintain in-store displays and weekly and monthly specials<br />\r\n    Entering inventory into computer system and processing vendor returns<br />\r\n    Picking up parts at various vendors  (Must have valid drivers license with good driving record)<br />\r\n    Assist in running cash register (Must have cash handling experience)<br />\r\n    General cleaning to keep up store appearance.<br />\r\n    MUST BE AVAILABLE EVERY OTHER SATURDAY FOR 8AM TO 1 PM SHIFT<br />\r\n    Shift hours are 8:00AM to 5:30 PM<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe right candidate must me able to work in a fast paced environment and handle multiple tasks.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMust have valid drivers license<br />\r\nHigh school diploma<br />\r\nMinimum 2 years experience in and automotive, marine, RV, or power sports environment<br />\r\n <br />\r\nLocated  2 miles south of the Mitchell Airport at 7575 S. Howell Ave in Oak Creek<br />\r\n <br />\r\nHours are M-F 8-5:30 & every other Saturday 8-1<br />\r\n <br />\r\nWeekly salary + commission, 401K , Health Insurance, & paid vacation<br />\r\n <br />\r\nHanna Trailer  7575 S. Howell Ave Oak Creek,  WI 53154 414-762-7950 ask for Paul', 'Hanna Trailer  7575 S. Howell Ave Oak Creek,  WI 53154 414-762-7950 ask for Paul', '10+2', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '30 March, 2017', '2017-03-30', 48, '2017-03-30 02:48:48', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(41166125, 0, 'Accounts Manager', 'Kandla Cargo Handlers', '', '2', '90', '29 May, 2017', '5', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'IN', '1287', '1325164', 'Mumbai', 'HR  COMPLIANCE  Transportation  Inventory', '', '7', '1', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Accounting Manager <br />\r\n<br />\r\nEssential Duties and Responsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPURPOSE<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis position addresses tight deadlines and a multitude of accounting activities including general ledger preparation, financial reporting, year end audit preparation and the support of budget and forecast activities. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nRESPONSIBILITIES & DUTIES<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Finalisation of Balance Sheet, P&L Account, Cash Flow statement Produces monthly, quarterly and annual financial statements.<br />\r\n    Supervise, directs and reviews the work of the accounting staff including, Cash/Bank reconciliations, account statement reconciliations- accounts receivable, vendor payment, payroll, recording of revenue and expenses.<br />\r\n    Monitoring of getting & issuing all Service Tax & HR Compliance related documents- PF, ESIC, Form 10/11 etc. and its timely uploading data in respective Government websites. Making necessary timely payments for the same.<br />\r\n    Manage daily accounting for purchases, field expenses, payments, banks<br />\r\n    Manage daily bank reconciliation and cash reconciliation<br />\r\n    Responsible for bill passing and processing TDS and Service Tax<br />\r\n    Creating, maintaining and updating MIS for cash and bank balance on daily basis.<br />\r\n    Daily sales audit and posting.<br />\r\n    Prepare daily MIS for outstanding payments from customers and manage vendor reconciliation.<br />\r\n    Responsible for financial year end closing activities <br />\r\n<br />\r\nMINIMUM REQUIREMENTS<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEducation<br />\r\nB.Com/ BA / M.Com/ C.A./ C.S. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nTechnical Skills and Prior Experience<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFive to seven years prior supervisory experience in the financial reporting/general ledger area. Experience working in a service firm is preferred.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMust be PC proficient and able to thrive in a fast -pace setting. Experience with Tally is a must. Must have strong experience with Microsoft Excel, Google Spreadsheets and Word.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nStrong verbal and written communication skills.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nStrong interpersonal, supervisory and client communication skills required.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to multi-task, work under pressure and meet deadlines required.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe marginal functions of this position have not been included. This job description in no way implies that these are the only duties to be performed. An employee will be required to follow any other job-related duties required by the appointing management.', 'Email: mayur.agarwal@kandlacargo.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9987169876', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '28 February, 2017', '2017-02-28', 78, '2017-02-28 03:08:35', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(41283405, 0, 'Medical Coding - Chennai, Trichy, Madurai, Salem, Erode, Karur, Nagercoil', 'Achievers Spot', '', '2', '90', '14 Jun, 2017', '0', '2', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Hyderabad', 'Medical Coding Executive Medical Coding Intern Allied Health Services Life science Paramedical Medical Coding Fresher ', '', '31', '106', '', '', '', '', '', '', '        Medical Coding is the process of conversion of text information related to healthcare services into numeric Diagnosis (Medical Problems) and Procedure (Treatments) Codes using ICD-10 CM and CPT code books.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        Healthcare, including Medical Coding and Billing, will generate Six million new jobs through 2020. That\'s more than any Other Industry.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        Healthcare Providers need efficient Medical Coders for HIPAA Compliant Claims filing and reimbursement.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEligibility:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAny Life Science, Paramedical, Medical Graduates and Post Graduates (M.B.B.S, B.D.S, B.H.M.S, B.A.M.S, Pharmacy, Physiotherapy, Nursing, Genetics, B.O.T, Microbiology, Biochemistry, Biotechnology, Biology, Bio-Medical graduates, Zoology, Botany, Bioinformatics, Endocrinology, Nutrition & Dietetics, Anatomy, Physiology , Chemistry, Medical Lab Technology, Health Education, etc.)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPay Scale:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n10000/- to 13000 per month initially with assured career growth (Incentives & Benefits as per Corporate Standards).<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nBenefits:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        1. Pick Up  & Drop Facility<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        2. Food Facility<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        3. Day Shift<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        4. Easily Accessible to Job<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n            Location<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        5. Weekend Off<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nCareer Growth:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nExcellent opportunity to enhance your career by getting CPC(Certified Association of Professional Coders) and AHIMA(American Health Information Management Professional Coders) and CCS(Certified Coding Specialist) Certification from AAPC(American Association) respectively.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nCPC, CCS - P Certification Training is also provided for fresher and experienced coders.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlacement Details:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlacement is provided to All Candidates Successfully Completing the Training Program in Leading Healthcare MNC BPOs.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlacement Locations: <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlacement Locations: Bangalore, Mangalore, Hubli, Mysore, Chitradurga, Bellary, Gulbarga, Shimoga, Tumkur, Chennai & Hyderabad<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPh: 9566157627/9566284629/7358425167/9566157632/9566133256/9840708203 044-42126317/42057586/45001158/45585310<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nEmail: ankitha@achieversspot.com', 'Email: ankitha@achieversspot.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9566157627', 'B.E. Biochemistry, B.Sc. Biochemistry, M.Sc. Biochemistry, M.E. Biochemistry', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '16 March, 2017', '2017-03-16', 62, '2017-03-16 04:40:37', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(41610354, 0, 'Manager of Provider Configuration Information Management', 'Molina Healthcare', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '3', '9', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', ' Long Beach, CA', 'Provider Configuration Information Management, Provider, Configuration, ', '', '1', '56', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Job Summary<br />\r\nResponsible for management of provider configuration analysts who are responsible for accurate and timely maintenance of critical provider information on all claims and provider databases. Maintains critical provider information on all claims and provider databases. Synchronizes data among multiple claims systems and application of business rules as they apply to each database. Validate data to be housed on provider databases and ensure adherence to business and system requirements of customers as it pertains to contracting, network management and credentialing. This job may require travel.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKnowledge/Skills/Abilities<br />\r\n* Assures that department, federal, and state specific standards are maintained and that overall provider processing accuracy is attained and maintained<br />\r\n* Organizational expert in responding to legislative and regulatory developments and audits as it relates to provider information.<br />\r\n* Supports others in facing out to regulators in developing and implementing appropriate Corrective Action Plans for submission of provider network files, etc.<br />\r\n* Establishes and maintains internal standard operating policies and procedures pertaining to provider functions and business analyses to ensure alignment with business objectives.<br />\r\n* Establishes staffing needs and ensures consistent training for staff through adoption of standardized processes.<br />\r\n* Works collaboratively with representatives in submission of provider data to ensure timely and accurate submissions.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Qualifications<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequired Education<br />\r\nBachelor\'s Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequired Experience<br />\r\n5-7 years<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPreferred Education<br />\r\nGraduate Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPreferred Experience<br />\r\n7-9 years<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTo all current Molina employees: If you are interested in applying for this position, please apply through the intranet job listing.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMolina Healthcare offers a competitive benefits and compensation package. Molina Healthcare is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) M/F/D/V.', 'Toll free: (800) 526-8196â€‹', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '25 April, 2017', '2017-04-25', 22, '2017-04-25 07:55:25', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(41905972, 0, 'Chartered Accountant', 'Disha Career Services.', '', '1', '90', '01 Jun, 2017', '0', '1', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'IN', '', '434079', 'Delhi', 'Reviewing the companys systems analysing risk. ', '', '10', '3', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Below are the responsibilities :-Liaising with clients (individuals or businesses) and providing financial information and advice.Reviewing the company\'s systems and analysing risk.', '    Company Name: Disha Career Services.<br />\r\n    Email: dcs.hrdelhincr@gmail.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 7500667444', 'CA', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 March, 2017', '2017-03-03', 75, '2017-03-03 03:52:00', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(42124408, 0, 'RELATIONSHIP MANAGER IN BANKING SERVICE', 'platinum services', '', '1', '90', '08 Jun, 2017', '1', '2', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Vijayawada', 'Branch Operations Banking Bank Cash Retention Branch Manager Equity Investment Cashier fresher Mutual Fund Branch Banking Branch Handling ', '', '10', '116', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'JOB DESCRIPTION<br />\r\n<br />\r\nA Relationship Manager could work in either Retail or Wholesale Banking and is required to help and advice clients. The range and scope of his work would range from helping clients with their account details to giving advice on financial investments. He/she needs to cater to individual clients while trying to generate new business and clients for the bank.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe Job Role and Responsibilities<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nA retail Relationship Manager would primarily deal with individual retail customers and advice them on various banking and financial products and services offered by the bank. A wholesale Relationship Manager would be catering to the corporate clients like SME\'s or large corporations.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSometimes a Relationship Manager might also be required to supervise other bank employees who communicate with his/her clients, like loan officers etc. A Relationship Manager is expected to have sound financial knowledge as well as thorough information about his/her company\'s various offerings in order to identify the need of the customer and advice him accordingly. He/she needs to have an understanding of banking regulations, latest products and services, specific markets related to the clients he/she is handling.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\njob location=near by location,Pan india level<br />\r\n<br />\r\nfresher salary-2.5lac to 4.5lac<br />\r\nexperinced salary dependend upon interview<br />\r\n and hike in bewteen 30% to 55% fro the lasst salary<br />\r\n<br />\r\nfor further query contact miss kanika rawat=+919205012655<br />\r\nfirstly send me resume to platinumservices121@gmail.com', 'Email: platinumservices121@gmail.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 09205012655', 'Graduate', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '10 March, 2017', '2017-03-10', 68, '2017-03-09 21:09:32', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(42227152, 0, 'Plant Finance Manager', 'DairiConcepts, L.P.', '', '2', '90', '28 Jun, 2017', '5', '13', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Zumbrota, MN', 'financial accounting related to physical inventory counts ', '', '4', '1', '', '', '', '', 'Required Skills<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Strong accounting and analytical skills<br />\r\n    Proficient in Excel<br />\r\n    High standards of accuracy, precision, and organization<br />\r\n    Articulate with strong verbal and written communication skills<br />\r\n    Ability to problem-solve and to collaborate with other teams<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequired Experience<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Bachelor of Science in Accounting and 5 years accounting experience in a manufacturing facility, or equivalent combination of education and experience<br />\r\n    Supervisory experience preferred <br />\r\n<br />\r\nOrganizational Relationships<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Reports to Business Unit Controller<br />\r\n    Titles Reporting to this Position<br />\r\n        Senior Accounting Specialist, Inventory Control Specialist/AP, and Receptionist <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPhysical Demands and Work Environment<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Office and manufacturing environment <br />\r\n<br />\r\nOther Responsibilities<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlease note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAs a leading provider of cheese and dairy ingredients for the global food industry, DairiConcepts is supported by a diverse and educated team of high quality employees. We seek personnel with expertise in their fields who also demonstrate our values of Safety, Integrity, Continuous Improvement, and Service. Headquartered in Springfield, Missouri, the company has eight manufacturing plants located throughout the United States.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDairiConcepts is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. We offer competitive compensation, bonus potential, and a full benefit program including 401K. For additional information, go to www.dairiconcepts.com.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Location<br />\r\nZumbrota, Minnesota, United States<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPosition Type<br />\r\nFull-Time/Regular', '', 'Job Description<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe Plant Finance Manager oversees all operational accounting activities at the Zumbrota facility, including financial reporting, internal controls, inventory, accounts payable, and fixed assets. It is also responsible for the plant manufacturing expense budget and measurement against that. It also includes timely and meaningful plant operations reporting and analysis, as well as supervision of plant accounting staff.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDuties and Responsibilities<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Maintains accounting systems and processes that ensure accurate and timely presentation of plant financial results and balance sheet reconciliations<br />\r\n    Responsible for accounting and control of plant inventory transactions, accounts payable, fixed assets, and internal controls<br />\r\n    Responsible for the financial accounting related to physical inventory counts<br />\r\n    Responsible for ensuring the fixed asset sub-ledger accurately reflects the condition and location of the plant\'s property, plant, and equipment<br />\r\n    Provides assistance with financial/other audits as needed<br />\r\n    Subject matter expert in plant KPI\'s, plant yields, and cost of non-conformance<br />\r\n    Analyzes current and past trends in plant KPI\'s and other metrics<br />\r\n    Participates in meetings with plant management on operational reviews<br />\r\n    Partners with operations on cost control, cost reduction, and gross margin improvement ideas<br />\r\n    Partners with operations to prepare and analyze capital project returns<br />\r\n    Directs, motivates, and trains employees to ensure functions are carried out efficiently and accurately<br />\r\n    Ensures effective departmental structure, talent development, and succession planning<br />\r\n    Provides support and training to plant personnel on system issues<br />\r\n    Prepares the annual plant manufacturing expense budget and provide result measurements to plant and corporate management<br />\r\n    Develops financial models and perform analysis to support pricing decisions<br />\r\n    Ad-hoc reporting, analysis, and special projects and duties as assigned <br />\r\n<br />\r\nTeam Development. Maximizes the operating and performance capacity of the plant accounting team by developing the capabilities of the individual team members.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTeamwork and Collaboration. Participates on cross-functional teams, and collaborates with other departments to improve processes and efficiencies.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLeadership. Acts with integrity. Treats others with dignity and respect. Models behavior that is consistent with DairiConcepts\' core values. Delivers on commitments and deadlines and holds others accountable for the same.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCommunication. Effectively communicates with all levels of the organization. Demonstrates excellent presentation, oral, and written communication skills. Executes outstanding customer communication and relationship building techniques.', '1-877-596-4374<br />\r\n1-417-829-3400', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '30 March, 2017', '2017-03-30', 48, '2017-03-30 03:03:44', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(42314563, 0, 'Hiring for chartered accountant cum cs chartered accountant', 'Job House', '', '1', '90', '02 Jul, 2017', '4', '9', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '', '', 'Jaipur', 'ca CS', '', '1', '121', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'chartered accountant cum cs or only chartered accountat<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLeading jewellery company<br />\r\n<br />\r\nmust have good experience<br />\r\n<br />\r\nc scheme,jaipur<br />\r\n<br />\r\nsalary 50-60k<br />\r\n<br />\r\nminimum 3 yeras experience after articleship<br />\r\n<br />\r\nmale/female<br />\r\n<br />\r\ncomplete taxation,audit,GL,reconcialation knowledge a must<br />\r\n<br />\r\npresentable<br />\r\n<br />\r\nurgent requirement<br />\r\n<br />\r\nmahendra.pathak18@gmail.com<br />\r\n<br />\r\n9829010787/7568054905<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3 sidharth colony ajmer road sodala opp old thana jaipur', 'MAHENDRA PATHAK(JOBHOUSE)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMumbai,delhi,jaipur,patna,Bangalore ,deoghar<br />\r\nEmail: mahendra.pathak18@gmail.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9829010787', 'CA', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 April, 2017', '2017-04-03', 44, '2017-04-03 02:48:46', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(42703890, 69645, 'java Developer', 'Right Infotech Solutions', '', '', '0', '', '1', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Delhi, Lucknow, Ahmedabad, ', '', '', '23', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '<p>Application Development ,Web Technologies, java ,Javascript ,mysql ,Linux ,php ,RestFul, web services html5 ,facebook, integration tomcat ,Amazon Web Services</p>', '<p>Minimum 2 years of experience in developing Java applications<br /> - Experience with Linux, MySQL, PHP, HTML5, JavaScript, RestFul web services <br /> - Experience in integrating with Facebook will be plus<br /> - MUST HAVE: Strong English writing/speaking skills</p>', '', '<p>- Develop, test, and maintain Java based consumer and enterprise applications<br /> - Deployment and management of the applications in Amazon cloud services<br /> - Implement server and client side JavaScript frameworks<br /> - Familiarity with MVC based architectures</p>', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 August, 2016', '2016-08-24', 266, '2016-08-24 02:39:43', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(42709487, 69645, 'Java Developer', 'Adecco India', '', '', '0', '', '3', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Chennai, ', '', '', '23', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', '<p><br /> Core Java<br /> Spring<br /> Hibernate<br /> NOTE : This is for Contract to Hire position Duration is more than 3 Yrs.</p>', '', '<p>We have an urgent requirement with one of our level 5 and product based company.</p>', '', 'UG: B.Tech/B.E. PG:Any Postgraduate - Any Specialization, Post Graduation Not Required Doctorate:Doctorate Not Required', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 August, 2016', '2016-08-24', 266, '2016-08-24 02:30:34', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(43487787, 51546, 'Uregent Requirement- .NET Developer and PHP Developer', 'Seefat Technologies', '', '2', '0', '', '1', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Mohali', '', '', '23', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Dear Candidates<br />\r\nGreetings from Seefat Technologies!!!<br />\r\nWe have required experienced ASP.Net MVC , C#,Website Developer and PHP Developer<br />\r\nCompany- Seefat Technolgies<br />\r\nDesignation- .NET Developer<br />\r\nExp- 1-3 yrs<br />\r\nDesignation- PHP Developer<br />\r\nExp.- 1-2 yrs<br />\r\nSalary-Good hike on current salary.<br />\r\nLocation- F353, 8B industrial Area Mohali<br />\r\nContact- 7355135209, 0172-5097209<br />\r\nJob Type: Full-time<br />\r\nYou can also recommend this job to others.', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 November, 2016', '2016-11-24', 174, '2016-11-24 01:22:06', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', '');
