(48243280, 21094, 'Application Developer/ Analyst', 'Surgeprofessional', '', '2', '0', '', '8', '14', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'US', '2998', '1180873', 'Chiquita, ', 'Java, J2EE, SQL, JSF, Struts, Hibernate, JPA, Spring, Acegi Security, JBoss, WebSphere, DB2, Informix, Eclipse, Ant, Maven, JDBC, JUnit, Eclipse, Team', '', '23', '138', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'The Application Analyst/Developer is responsible for leading in all facets of the systems development lifecycle for application enhancements of various sizes and complexities related to the Toshiba ACE application performing a variety of technical duties. The Application Analyst Developer performs many of these tasks independently and communicates with the appropriate teams to ensure that assignments are delivered with the highest of quality and in accordance to standards. The Application Analyst/Developer will assist with the implementation a new solution, test and help support the hardware and software for Self-Checkout project. A well-qualified candidate will have both application enhancements and a strong Java development background. Experience with optimizing performance, automating test, builds, and deployments are also critical. Qualified resource is experienced developing with web service development and Java/J2EE web services.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe Developer side of this position is responsible for aiding in the design, development, and testing, debugging, maintaining and documenting software components in accordance to Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) best practices. The Developer has overall responsibility in the technical design process. Participates in the application technical design process and completes estimates and work plans for design, development, implementation, and rollout tasks. The Developer also communicates with the appropriate teams to ensure that assignments are delivered with the highest of quality and in accordance to standards. The Application Developer strives to continuously improve the software delivery processes and practices. Role model and demonstrate the company\'\'s core values of respect, honesty, integrity, diversity, inclusion and safety of others.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEssential Job Functions:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPartner with appropriate teams and vendors to deliver software solutions according to SDLC best practices.<br />\r\nBuild partnerships across the application, business and infrastructure teams.<br />\r\nDevelop programming specifications. Design, code and unit test application code using Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) best practices.<br />\r\nPartner with the appropriate teams and vendors to expedite issue resolution and manage to SLAs.<br />\r\nSupport and maintain applications utilizing required tools and technologies. Provide support for applications, including involvement with the appropriate teams. Provide off-hours support (24 x 7) as required.<br />\r\nCreate technical system documentation and ensure that this documentation remains current throughout all phases of the SDLC.<br />\r\nEstablish priorities for enhancements/modifications of application.<br />\r\nDevelop programming specifications. May design, code and unit test application code using SDLC best practices for application services functions.<br />\r\nComplete estimates and work plans with the assistance of more senior team members as appropriate for design, development, implementation and rollout tasks.<br />\r\nAssist other personnel on assignments including mentoring or providing on-the-job training to more junior associates.<br />\r\nCompletes applications development by coordinating requirements, schedules, and activities; contributing to team meetings; troubleshooting development and production problems across multiple environments and operating platforms.<br />\r\nAbility to build scalable frameworks for enterprise solutions.<br />\r\nUnderstanding the architecture and developing Web Services on multi-tiered development architecture, production deployment and strong knowledge of Web Services and related UML diagrams<br />\r\nCreate technical requirements for the vendor for all enhancements.<br />\r\nUnderstand and follow the strategic direction set by management as it relates to the project goals<br />\r\nDefine and create operation procedures, processes and test scripts.<br />\r\nMust be able to perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodation.<br />\r\nDeliver high-quality solutions<br />\r\nSupport and maintain solutions utilizing required tools and technologies<br />\r\nProvide off-hours support (24 x 7) when needed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequirements:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5 or more yearsâ€™ experience in system analysis, design or programming and the associated development methodologies.<br />\r\n4 - 6 yearsâ€™ experience in systems analysis, design or programming and the associated development methodologies.<br />\r\nProven communication and presentation skills to effectively communicate information to customers and to all levels within the organization.<br />\r\nAbility to interact well in a team environment.<br />\r\nProven ability to work creatively and analytically in a problem-solving environment.<br />\r\nProven application development experience<br />\r\nCan work with minimal supervision<br />\r\nAbility to determine methods and procedures on new projects with minimal guidance.<br />\r\nKnowledgeable of appropriate change/release management practices.<br />\r\nMust be able to perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodation.<br />\r\nDesired Skills:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIS related associate degree, or a bachelor\'\'s degree, or comparable work experience in an Information Systems position or related business position.<br />\r\n4 - 6 yearsâ€™ experience in adjacent technologies.<br />\r\nPrior experience with project planning with medium size or medium level complexity projects.<br />\r\nBonus Skills: Desired Previous Job Experience<br />\r\nBachelor\'\'s degree in IS or related equivalent work experience in an Information Systems position.<br />\r\n6 - 8 yearsâ€™ experience in systems analysis, design or programming and the associated development methodologies with medium size or medium level complexity projects.<br />\r\nPrior experience with project planning with medium size or medium level complexity projects.<br />\r\nEducation Level: Bachelor\'\'s Desired', 'Gloria Ghramajo<br />\r\nSurge Professional<br />\r\nMason, OH<br />\r\nwww.surgeprofessional.com<br />\r\n +1-281-323-5974', 'MCA/B Tech./ M Tech.', 'Formal', 'US Citizen, GC, EAD (OPT/CPT/GC/H4)', 'W2-Permanant, W2-Contract, 1099-Contract, Contract to Hire', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '13 February, 2017', '2017-02-13', 93, '2017-02-13 02:42:34', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(48309868, 48219, 'Sr. Java Developer ', 'Daiwik Business Solutions Pvt Ltd', '', '3', '0', '', '3', '8', 'Contract', '', '', '', '', '5', '', '', '', 'Hyderabad, ', '', '', '23', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', 'Standard', 'â€¢	3 â€“ 8 years of Java development experience.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Certification can be added value', '', 'â€¢	Experience required in both frame Spring and Hibernate frame work (Mandatory)<br />\r\nâ€¢	Should have knowledge on SQL, Joins, Group by, Aggregate functions.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Strong experience in OOPS, Overriding, Collections, Exception handling, Strings, Multi-threading. JDBC, Servlets, JSP.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Good at using Maven, ANT<br />\r\n', '', 'BTech / MCA', 'Casual', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '31 August, 2016', '2016-08-31', 259, '2016-08-31 05:49:21', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(48335194, 0, '\"SAS Administrator\"', 'Infoways', '', '2', '90', '01 Jun, 2017', '3', '6', 'Contract', '', '3- 6 Months', '', '', '12', 'US', '', '1192703', 'New York, NY', '\"SAS Admin\" and \"SAS Grid 9.4\"', '', '41', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'SAS GRID 9.4 System Administration, configuration, system monitoring and Disaster recovery management<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEnsure the overall health of the SAS Grid platform which uses shared files systems and includes:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSAS Foundation / Base SAS /SAS Studio/ Office Analytics/Enterprise Guide<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesign solutions to reduce the operational and management complexity of the platform<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMonitor, log, and troubleshoot SAS servers and processes, including error messages<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExecute backups regularly as specified in your backup strategy, as part of your housekeeping schedule.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSAS client tools installation and maintain SAS Metadata security.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nApply Maintenance releases ,upgrades and hotfixes as required all SAS products in the platform in coordination with internal customer infra teams<br />\r\n<br />\r\nProvide guidance and assistance to SAS developers on operational<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDeployment of any SAS patches, product bug fix patches recommended by product vendor upon acceptance of the same by the customer<br />\r\n<br />\r\nServe as an escalation point for production and/or platform issuses.', 'Sailaja<br />\r\nInfoways<br />\r\nTrenton, NJ<br />\r\nwww.info-ways.com<br />\r\n +1-215-541-5366', 'MCA/B Tech./ M Tech.', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 March, 2017', '2017-03-03', 75, '2017-03-03 04:08:38', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(48402624, 0, 'Sysvine Technologies Private Limited', 'Quality Assurance', '', '2', '90', '25 Jun, 2017', '1', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Chennai', 'Software Engineering Quality Assurance', '', '23', '51', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Excellent Oral and Written Communication skills. <br />\r\nExcellent Analysis Skill. <br />\r\nStrong knowledge in Agile Process. <br />\r\nGood in Aptitude & Communication skills.<br />\r\nStrong Knowledge in Testing concepts.', '    Company Name: Sysvine Technologies Private Limited<br />\r\n    Email: gautham.rajan@in.sysvine.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 4440188463', 'B-tech(mech/EEE/civil/ETC/CSE)', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '27 March, 2017', '2017-03-27', 51, '2017-03-27 02:17:33', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(48418860, 0, 'Lab Customer Support', 'North Oaks Health System', '', '1', '90', '05 Jul, 2017', '2', '9', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Hammond, LA', 'medical terminology, excellent verbal, written, communication, interpersonal and organizational skills.', '', '1', '11', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'High School diploma or equivalent education with completion of secretarial course or equivalent experience, customer service or call center experience preferred. Good knowledge of computer and keyboard, familiarity with medical terminology, excellent verbal, written, communication, interpersonal and organizational skills. Must have patience and the ability to maintain composure in high stress situations. Must be detail oriented and handle confidential information appropriately. Strong problem solving skills and the ability to handle multiple tasks at once are essential as well as excellent customer service skills. Physical Effort Required: Strength: Sedentary Push: Occasionally Pull: Occasionally Carry: Occasionally Lift: Occasionally Sit: Frequently Stand: Occasionally Walk: Occasionally ', '', 'High School diploma', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '06 April, 2017', '2017-04-06', 41, '2017-04-05 23:21:33', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(48427285, 0, 'Immediate requirement for PeopleSoft Admin position ', 'Kollasoft', '', '1', '90', '31 May, 2017', '5', '10', 'Contract', '', '3- 6 Months', '', '', '', 'IN', '', '', 'Minneapolis, MN', ' Peoplesoft DBA/Admin', '', '23', '40', '', '', '', '', '<br />\r\nRequired Skills:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMust have skills : Key skills are strong unix, oracle, PeopleTools/upgrades/administration.<br />\r\nSoft skills and communication extremely important.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPeopleSoft Administrator<br />\r\nSenior type experience with all facets of upgrades/administration/etc.<br />\r\nKey skills are strong unix, oracle, PeopleTools/upgrades/administration.<br />\r\nSoft skills and communication extremely important.<br />\r\nThey will be supporting 100 environments. Itâ€™s a Peoplesoft app upgrade project. Need People software tools.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nClient : Wells Fargo', '', 'Greetings of the Day.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis is Ramkrishna from Kollasoft.Inc working on PeopleSoft Admin Position opened for Minneapolis,MN. Please check the requirement and Let me know if youâ€™re interested and respond with your updated resume & salary billing rates.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTitle : PeopleSoft Admin<br />\r\nDuration: 6+Months on W2<br />\r\nLocation: Minneapolis,MN<br />\r\nClient : Wells Fargo<br />\r\n', 'Kalyan Sharma<br />\r\nKollasoft<br />\r\nScottsdale, AZ', 'MCA/B Tech./ M Tech.', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '02 March, 2017', '2017-03-02', 76, '2017-03-02 03:40:20', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(48792335, 0, 'Data Analytics Manager', 'Cloudious LLC', '', '4', '90', '01 Jun, 2017', '2', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '12', 'US', '', '1184878', 'San Diego, CA', 'SAS, SQL', '', '23', '141', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'We are currently seeking a Data Analytics Manager for Full-time position with one of our direct client based out at San Diego, CA.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIn lieu of a Master\'\'s degree, 13 yearsâ€™ experience in data analysis and business logic development.<br />\r\nExtensive SAS knowledge and experience.<br />\r\nMinimum seven (7) years in extensive data analysis and business logic development.<br />\r\nMinimum five (5) years of extensive programming experience in managing and analyzing large and complex data.<br />\r\nProficient in SQL language.<br />\r\nFamiliar with the concept of Virtual Data Warehouse (VDW<br />\r\nKnowledge of Health Maintenance Organization Research Network (HMORN)\'\'s VDW.<br />\r\nExperience with SAS programming and preparation of analytical data files.<br />\r\nExperience managing teams preferred.', 'Arun Kumar<br />\r\nCloudious LLC<br />\r\nSunnyvale, CA', 'MCA/B Tech./ M Tech.', 'Formal', 'US Citizen, GC', 'W2-Permanant', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 March, 2017', '2017-03-03', 75, '2017-03-03 04:05:06', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(48924980, 0, 'Network Engineer', 'Squircle IT Consulting Services Pvt. Ltd.', '', '2', '0', '', '4', '9', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '1283', '434686', 'Bangalore, ', 'BYB501 IN Ericsson APZ 210 IOG11C Routing Concepts IN2.1 ', '', '24', '34', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Should have hands on experience on Ericsson APZ 210, IOG11C, BYB501<br />\r\nIN and Routing Concepts IN2.1<br />\r\nIN Call Flows<br />\r\nSignaling Protocol SS7 (INAP/ISUP) and ISDN 30<br />\r\nDatabase Concepts related to SMAS<br />\r\nTelesis Ocean fast SSP and Singnaling Unit<br />\r\nSonus System and Unit<br />\r\nGood knowledge of VOIP Functioning<br />\r\nGood knowledge of SO Services<br />\r\nKnowledge of KPN call flows and knowledge for used tools like, NMF or other Ticket Tracking tools<br />\r\nGood Written and Oral Communication skills<br />\r\nWilling to work in 24X7 Shifts between 10 AM to 11.00PM IST and on call after hours on rotation basis', '    Company Name: Squircle IT Consulting Services Pvt. Ltd.<br />\r\n    Email: recruiters.squircle@gmail.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 4065656629', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '23 February, 2017', '2017-02-23', 83, '2017-02-23 03:36:24', '', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49024821, 0, 'Human Resources Senior Technical Developer/Analyst', 'Cal State University, Chancellors Office,', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '4', '9', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Long Beach, CA ', ' HCM, Broker, PeopleTools, PeopleCode, Application Designer, Application Engine, SQL/SQR, ', '', '23', '115', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Chancellor\'s Office Statement<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJoin our team at the California State University, Office of the Chancellor, and make a difference in providing access to higher education. We are currently seeking experienced candidates for the position of Human Resources Senior Technical Developer/Analyst. The CSU Chancellor\'s Office, located on the waterfront adjacent to the Aquarium of the Pacific in downtown Long Beach, is the headquarters for the nation\'s largest and most diverse system of higher education. The CSU Chancellor\'s Office offers a premium benefit package that includes outstanding vacation, health, and dental plans; a fee waiver education program; membership in the California Public Employees Retirement System (PERS); and 14 paid holidays a year.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUNIQUE OPPORTUNITY!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis is an opportunity to join the largest public university in the nation and become part of the CSU team for a system-wide strategic initiative. Come join the excitement with this rather unique opportunity<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe salary range for this classification is $6,249 to $10,857 per month.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPosition Information<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe California State University, Office of the Chancellor, is seeking a Human Resources Senior Technical Developer/Analyst to provide technical support for CSU\'s PeopleSoft HCM application. Information Systems\' Application Development area encompasses application support and upgrade activities for 23 campuses and the CSU Chancellor\'s Office (CO), integration with other third-party/external and/or internal systems, the consolidation of the HR databases implementation (CHRS). The Human Resources Senior Technical Developer/Analyst requires proactive initiative to resolve the most complex HCM application issues in support/development areas that include implementation, system analysis, planning, design, development and support of the Human Resources application. The expert level position must possess advanced, comprehensive and technical knowledge of the HCM system and working experience with PeopleSoft Web Services. Specific technical support and development assignments may change at any time based on Application Development\'s projects and priorities, including supporting other applications within the area.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nResponsibilities<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUnder the general direction of the Project Manager, the Human Resources Senior Technical Developer/Analyst will:<br />\r\n-Create new technical development without assistance from other analysts based on functional specifications.<br />\r\n-Support technical development of the PeopleSoft HCM application using PeopleTools, PeopleCode, Web Services, Integration Broker, Application Designer, Application Messaging, Application Engine, complex SQR, etc.<br />\r\n-Provide production support for the 23 CSU campuses by analyzing and troubleshooting campus application issues reported through Service Now help desk tickets. Coordinate PeopleSoft updates, fixes, upgrades and installations. Advise campus programmers on technical development, environment control and maintenance issues. Collaborate with functional leads on ongoing maintenance and development.<br />\r\n-Mentor and assist Technical Developer/Analysts on development efforts, best practices and documentation.<br />\r\n-Lead and participate on project teams to implement new system functionality within the PeopleSoft HCM application.<br />\r\n-Analyze, design, code, and unit test application solutions from requirements using defined processes and procedures.<br />\r\n-Present analysis to management and other project teams.<br />\r\n-Document code changes throughout the development process.<br />\r\n-Provide estimates and timeframes for development work and deliverables.<br />\r\n-Deliver effective solutions on time and adhere to development and quality standards.<br />\r\n-Communicate and enforce best practice coding standards.<br />\r\n-Undertake special projects as directed including working with other subject matter experts (SME) teams to facilitate cross training and coverage of all application areas.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualifications<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis position requires:<br />\r\n-A BA/BS in Computer Science or a related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience, as well as course work in the PeopleSoft HCM application.<br />\r\n-Minimum 7-10 years of technical experience developing and supporting the PeopleSoft HCM application preferably Human Resources version 9.2 or higher and PeopleTools version 8.55 or higher.<br />\r\n-Development skills include expert proficiency with Integration Broker, PeopleTools, PeopleCode, Application Designer, Application Engine, Application Packages, Component Interfaces, Configuration Manager, SQL/SQR, XML Publisher.<br />\r\n-Proven recent technical end to end development on major projects and modifications.<br />\r\n-Proven ability to create new development unassisted based on functional specifications.<br />\r\n-Excellent application implementation lifecycle skills including experience with: translating business requirements into technical designs, contributing to fit/gap analysis, application configurations, and technical specifications.<br />\r\n-Creative problem solving/strategic thinking skills to improve processes and solve complex problems.<br />\r\n-Strong understanding of best practice coding techniques and testing skills.<br />\r\n-Excellent analytical skills, debugging techniques and root cause analysis skills.<br />\r\n-Excellent written and advanced verbal communication skills (including exceptional listening, mentoring and collaboration abilities).<br />\r\n-Ability to handle multiple tasks, prioritize, take initiative, and work well under pressure.<br />\r\n-Must be flexible and able to work independently or in a team environment.<br />\r\n-Desire and willingness to learn and implement new technology.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPreferred:<br />\r\n-Proficient knowledge of PeopleSoft rules-based processing.<br />\r\n-Proven advanced technical expertise within the Human Resources application, Absence Management module.<br />\r\n-Expertise with Web Services, PeopleSoft Update Manager (PUM) or Change Assistant.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nApplication Period<br />\r\n<br />\r\nResumes will be accepted until job posting is removed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHow To Apply<br />\r\n<br />\r\nApply online at https://cmsweb.cms.csulb.edu/HLBPRD/cocsu_jobs.html<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhen applying please include cover letter and resume in one document<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEqual Employment Opportunity<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe university is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate against persons on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, gender, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, medical condition, National origin, sex, sexual orientation, covered veteran status, or any other protected status. Reasonable accommodations will be provided for qualified applicants with disabilities who self-disclose by contacting the Senior Human Resources Manager.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nE-Verify<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis position requires new hire employment verification to be processed through the E-Verify program administered by the Department of Homeland Security, U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (DHSUSCIS)\' in partnership with the Social Security Administration (SSA).<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf hired, you will be required to furnish proof that you are legally authorized to work in the United States.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMandated Reporter Per CANRA<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe person holding this position is considered a \'mandated reporter\' under the California Child Abuse and Neglect Reporting Act and is required to comply with the requirements set forth in CSU Executive Order 1083 as a condition of employment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBackground<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe Chancellor\'s Office policy requires that the successful candidate complete a full background check (including a criminal records check) prior to assuming this position.', '', 'MBA HR', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '10 April, 2017', '2017-04-10', 37, '2017-04-01 05:47:06', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49037806, 55606, 'Software Development Engineer - ADAS', 'I Squaresoft Technology Services Ltd', '', '', '0', '', '3', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '5', '', '', '', 'Bangalore, ', 'Embedded C ,ADAS,Algorithm testing,Automotive,', '', '7', '18', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Title / Position	Software Development Engineer - ADAS<br />\r\nRole/ Job Description	â€¢	Perform customer & internal requirements analysis & definition.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Define corresponding architecture based on the defined requirements.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Create module level design, implementation and perform testing and review activities based on the BU ADAS ALGORITHM development process.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Analyze ALGORITHM testing result based on the defined requirements as black box and vehicle tests.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Establish and maintain documentation according to ADAS Development Process and common rules.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Deliver work products/results to agreed milestones and in agreed quality.<br />\r\nâ€¢	Share information regularly with peers.<br />\r\nSkills	<br />\r\nâ€¢	Embedded C<br />\r\nâ€¢	ADAS<br />\r\nâ€¢	Algorithm testing<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDomain	Automotive<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEducational Qualification	B.E/B.Tech<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYears of Experience	3-5 years<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWork Location/ Country	Bangalore<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf interested share me updated Cv to nageshchintha@isquaresoft.com<br />\r\neither reach me by this No:8431515947', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '20 July, 2016', '2016-07-20', 301, '2016-07-20 00:26:10', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49062626, 0, 'Assistant Engineer - LabVIEW - Development', 'ACG Inspection Systems Pvt Ltd', '', '1', '90', '26 Jun, 2017', '3', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Industry Standards', 'IN', '', '', 'Mumbai ', 'Assistant Engineer - LabVIEW - Development', '', '1', '56', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'LabVIEW code development and unit testing<br />\r\nModule development and integration<br />\r\nImage processing algorithm development  and deployment', '    Company Name: ACG Inspection Systems Pvt Ltd<br />\r\n    Email: sachin.badhan@acg-world.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 2239194700', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '28 March, 2017', '2017-03-28', 50, '2017-03-28 00:37:15', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49110591, 55606, 'Designer-Electrical harness', 'TOP CMM 5 Level Company - Bangalore', '', '5', '0', '', '3', '8', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '5', '', '', '', 'Bangalore', 'ATIA V5, A350 VPM,PDM , SSCI, CIRCE,	Referential TreND, SAP', 'http://isquaresoft.com/', '7', '59', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', '<p>Role/ Job Description &bull; Knowledge of SIDP Experience in GRM/Full 3D activities of Electrical harness design for A350 Programme<br /> &bull; 3-8 years of project experience, electrical harness / secondary structures in 3D environment<br /> &bull; Have Certification training on PDM Link SSCI, A350 VPM and CATIA AI methods<br /> &bull; Expertise with Catia V5 - Part Design/DMU/EHI/F3D, PDM link SSCI, A350 VPM, REFERENTIAL, CIRCE and SAP on relevant projects<br /> &bull; Onsite Experiences shall be an added advantage<br /> &bull; Candidates with valid open work permit will be given preference<br /> <br /> Skills &bull; CATIA V5, A350 VPM<br /> &bull; PDM Link SSCI, CIRCE<br /> &bull; Referential TreND, SAP<br /> Domain Mechanical</p>', '', 'B.Tech(mechanical),M.Tech,', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '26 August, 2016', '2016-08-26', 264, '2016-08-26 07:23:12', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49335031, 0, 'Junior Software & Software Engineer', 'Multi Recruit Hiring For Multi Recruit', '', '2', '90', '14 Jun, 2017', '1', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Bangalore ', 'C RTOS ', '', '23', '56', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Brigosha Technologies Private Limited<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nCompany Name, Profile, Work Culture: Brigosha Technologies, founded by Indian Institute of Technology Guwahati and Indian Institute of Science Bangalore alumni. Conception of Brigosha is the upshot of firm determination imbued with shared Vision. Brigosha is deeply involved in developing state-of-the-art solutions in the field of Aerospace, Consumer Electronics, Education, Industrial Technology and Medical Devices. Brigosha offers consultancy in Algorithm Development and Embedded Solutions.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPoint of Contact for CVâ€™s / Email ID: starter13@multirecruit.com â€“ 08041212005<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nNumber of Vacancies:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nKeywords: Software Engineer, Software Developer, C, Embedded Software, Embedded C, RTOS, C Programmer.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Title / Designation: Junior Software/ Software Engineer<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Description:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMandatory Skills<br />\r\nÂ· Working experience in Embedded C programming.<br />\r\nÂ· Good knowledge of MISRA Coding guidelines.<br />\r\nÂ· Experience: 1-4 years<br />\r\nÂ· Majority of working experience should be in programming.<br />\r\nÂ· Hands on experience in tool chain used for any embedded development<br />\r\nÂ· Good communication and comprehension skills<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nKey Functions & Roles of the Candidate:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· Working knowledge on RTOS.<br />\r\nÂ· Knowledge on automotive communication protocols like CAN, LIN, FLEXRAY, MOST etc<br />\r\nÂ· Knowledge on standards like ISO26262, UDS, KWP2000, OBDII<br />\r\nÂ· Good understanding of AUTOSAR based software architecture<br />\r\nÂ· Good understanding of layered software architecture<br />\r\nÂ· Hands on experience on VECTOR Tools like CANOE, KVASER, etc<br />\r\nÂ· Interpersonal skills (Networking, negotiation, and tolerance):<br />\r\nÂ· The ability to work with cross functional, multiregional, internal and external teams that can have different priorities<br />\r\nÂ· Ability to manage urgent situations and manage priorities<br />\r\nÂ· Tolerance to ambiguity and dealing with complex engineering problems<br />\r\nÂ· Ability to make decisions with minimal supervision and limited information<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nMinimum/Maximum/ Work Experience Required: 1-4<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLocation(s) of Job: Bangalore & Coimbatore<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMinimum Education Requirements: B.Tech/ B.E<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNo of rounds of Interviews: 4<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCTC â€“ Market Standard.', 'Email: starter13@multirecruit.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 08041212005', 'MCA/B Tech./ M Tech.', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '16 March, 2017', '2017-03-16', 62, '2017-03-16 02:38:45', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49391265, 0, 'IRB Regulatory Coordinator', 'Aerotek', '', '1', '90', '27 Jun, 2017', '4', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Philadelphia, PA ', 'an ability to prioritize, meet deadlines, multitask, work independently and work interdependently', '', '1', '117', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Regulatory (IRB) Coordinator position with a leading research hospital in Philadelphia, PA. The Regulatory Coordinator will be responsible for coordination of all aspects of clinical trials and investigator initiated research protocols including the implementation of research protocols within oncology practice, submission of protocol and compliance with regulatory authorities (FDA/IRB).<br />\r\nResponsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Managing regulatory documentation work flow for 20+ clinical trials through the use of project management techniques and tools (spreadsheets, progress reports, priority setting etc.)<br />\r\n    Review all communications from Cooperative, Pharmaceutical Companies, FDA, NCI postings and determine the required amendments and safety updates that relate to trials<br />\r\n    Ensure that regulatory preparations for all sponsor audits visits, monitor visits, are done in a timely and efficient manner by the regulatory staff<br />\r\n    Establish and manage a Quality Assurance program to ensure that regulatory document is concordant with the sponsor template version control is maintained , that regulatory documents are QCd before submission to the IRB or the FDA and that all clinical trial documentation<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Candidates must have prior experience submitting to the IRB<br />\r\n    Knowledge and understanding human subject research regulations and federal guidance documents<br />\r\n    Excellent interpersonal and organizational skills, strong problem-solving skills, an ability to prioritize, meet deadlines, multitask, work independently and work interdependently<br />\r\n    Excellent computer skills with proficiency with Microsoft Office; precision and accuracy in data entry and written communications; oral and written communication skills are required<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbout Aerotek:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOur people are everything. As a Best of StaffingÂ® Client and Talent leader, AerotekÂ® Inc. has distinguished itself as a leader in recruiting and staffing services, by having a deep understanding of the intersection of talent and business. As a strategic partner to more than 17,000 clients and 300,000 contract employees every year, Aerotekâ€™s people-focused approach yields competitive advantages for its clients and rewarding careers for its contract employees. Headquartered in Hanover, Md., Aerotek operates a network of over 230 non-franchised offices with more than 6,000 internal employees dedicated to serving our customers. Aerotek is an operating company of Allegis Group, a global talent solutions provider. To learn more, visit aerotek.com.<br />\r\nThe company is an equal opportunity employer and will consider all applications without regards to race, sex, age, color, religion, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information or any characteristic protected by law.<br />\r\nIf you would like to request a reasonable accommodation, such as the modification or adjustment of the job application process or interviewing process due to a disability, please call 888-237-6835 or email accommodation@aerotek.com for other accommodation options. However, if you have questions about this position, please contact the Recruiter located at the bottom of the job posting. The Recruiter is the sole point of contact for questions about this position. ', '', 'Bachelor\'s', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '29 March, 2017', '2017-03-29', 49, '2017-03-29 07:20:50', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49398966, 81896, 'Job openins in IT Companies', 'Aranyani Groups', '', '30', '0', '', '0', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', '', '', '', 'Bangalore, ', 'software jobs', 'http://www.aranyanigroups.com', '23', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Openings in mnc companies<br />\r\njava, dotnet and teshing<br />\r\n2013-2016 passouts<br />\r\nLocation: Bangalore & Hyderabad.<br />\r\nPackage: 3.2 to 4 lacks<br />\r\ninterested contact us<br />\r\nChaitra<br />\r\nHr-Manager<br />\r\nAranya Groups<br />\r\n7892047557<br />\r\nBangalore<br />\r\nwww,aranyanigroups.com ', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '05 January, 2017', '2017-01-05', 132, '2017-01-05 04:38:44', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49675270, 0, 'EDI Manager', 'HellermannTyton', '', '1', '90', '22 Jun, 2017', '4', '9', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Milwaukee, WI', 'Executive/Senior Level Mgmt', '', '1', '94', '', '', '', 'Qualifications (skills, knowledge, experience)<br />\r\nBachelor\'s degree strongly preferred; associate\'s degree required.<br />\r\nMinimum 4 years\' experience working with EDI in an ERP integrated environment.<br />\r\nExperience managing and developing an EDI team.<br />\r\nProven ability to quickly learn new applications, processes, and procedures.<br />\r\nAbility to effectively manage multiple priorities in a fast paced environment.', 'Key Competencies<br />\r\nProven understanding of core EDI processes, tools, and strategies. Demonstrated strong analytical skills and technical aptitude to implement customer requirements through EDI solutions. Experience implementing EDI programs with core project management discipline and tools.<br />\r\nDemonstrated ability to form meaningful partnerships with people (internal/external) at all organizational levels resulting in practical solutions to complex problems ensuring commitment to the customer as the key emphasis.<br />\r\nAbility to influence and collaborate cross functionally (e.g. IT, sales, marketing, etc.) at all levels. Excellent verbal and written communication skills including the ability to recognize and customize communications to different audiences including utilizing diverse information from a variety of sources to present the HellermannTyton value proposition in an effective manner. Persistent, yet reasonable approach to communicating and driving results.<br />\r\nDemonstrated detail orientation and disciplined time management and ability to prioritize work from multiple customers ensuring completion of multiple activities to the established timelines. Must be effective at follow-up and management of urgent requests in a timely and professional manner. ', '', 'The EDI Manager plays a critical role by connecting our customers more efficiently and accurately through Electronic Data Interchange (EDI). The manager supervises the daily EDI functions as well as the planning, implementation and maintenance of EDI processes. This role provides valuable insights to information systems linkages and assists other EDI functions. The EDI Manager will work closely with a managed services provider to setup, test, and implement effective EDI with new and current trading partners. This position will also support timely and accurate exchange of electronic information between HellermannTyton and trading partners.<br />\r\nEssential Functions:<br />\r\nLead EDI team to ensure that all EDI requirements are processed in accordance with HellermannTyton standards and guidelines.<br />\r\nDevelops processes and policies related to EDI including testing, production implementation, transmission requirements and support.<br />\r\nAnalyze and identify ways to improve EDI processes and improve the effectiveness Prepare project documentation which includes project plan, requirements definition, and acceptable solution, coding specification, test plan, acceptance criteria and system test plan.<br />\r\nConsult with customers and work with IT to translate requirements into technical specifications.<br />\r\nDevelop and execute integration test plans and facilitate user acceptance.', '', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 March, 2017', '2017-03-24', 54, '2017-03-24 04:51:00', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49727005, 0, 'Urgent Requirement fresher candidate MCA and B.Tech (IT,CS)', 'Recom Infotech Pvt Ltd', '', '1', '', '', '0', '1', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '1299', '437026', 'Ghazipur, Ghaziabad', 'SEO   Java   ASP   .NET', '', '23', '29', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Dear Candidate<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUrgent Requirement for MCA/BCA / B.Tech (CS, IT) Fresher Candidate only<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKey Skills: ASP.NET/PHP/JAVA/SEO<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCompany: Recom InfoTech Pvt.Ltd.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Location: Ghaziabad<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesignation: Software developer/Associate software Developer/Programmer/Trainee<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNo. Of Vacancies: 20<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterview Time: 11:00 am to 2:00 pm<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAddress: 236 2nd floor, New Arya Nagar, Meerut Road Ghaziabad near Opp. Shiva Bajaj agency, Above samsung showroom<br />\r\n<br />\r\nContact: Mayank Raghav<br />\r\n<br />\r\n9457654260<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThanks', 'Email: recominfosolution@gmail.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9457654260', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '27 February, 2017', '2017-02-27', 79, '2017-02-27 03:15:31', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49761560, 0, 'ios Developerc', 'Hire IT People, LLC', '', '1', '90', '03 Jul, 2017', '5', '9', 'Contract', '', '6 - 12 Months', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Overland Park, KS', 'C ,MAC OS ,XCODE ', '', '23', '21', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Role : iOS Developer<br />\r\nLocation : Overland Park, KS<br />\r\nDuration : 8 Months<br />\r\nInterview : F2F<br />\r\nNo of Positions : 2<br />\r\nPrimary Skills : iOS Developer Object C ,MAC OS ,XCODE<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequired Skills:<br />\r\nStrong hands on Experience in iOS Development<br />\r\nObject C ,MAC OS ,XCODE<br />\r\nExperience : 5+ Years<br />\r\n', '', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '04 April, 2017', '2017-04-04', 43, '2017-04-04 03:37:41', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(49832283, 68910, 'Urgent Requirement of PHP Developer', 'Adixsoft Technology Pvt Ltd', '', '2', '0', '', '1', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'Noida, ', 'CSS/XHTML, Dreamweaver, WordPress, Joomla, PHP, Mysql ', '', '23', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Job Description<br />\r\nAdixsoft Technologies is looking for an Urgent expert PHP Developer with minimum Experience of 06 months - 3 Years in the same field. <br />\r\nCandidate Must have knowledge about PHP ,Magento ,WordPress briefly,Kindly carry your updated resume with projects and sample work.<br />\r\nSkills Required: CSS/XHTML, Dreamweaver, WordPress, Joomla, PHP, Mysql <br />\r\n', 'send your resume- hr@adixsoft.com', 'Any Graduate', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '27 January, 2017', '2017-01-27', 110, '2017-01-27 06:55:25', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(50041512, 0, 'Technical Support- Inbound technical Support(Voice or Non-voice)', 'Convergys India Services Private limited.', '', '4', '90', '13 Jun, 2017', '0', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '', '', 'Gurgaon', 'call centre non voice callcenter CSO customerservice fresher Chat inbound calling customercare technicalsupport voice ', '', '9', '12', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Job Description: - Inbound technical Support.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterface with customers via inbound or outbound calls or the Internet for resolving routine problems with products or services like internet, DTH or desktop.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRoles & Responsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGreet customers in a courteous, friendly, and professional manner using agreed upon procedures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nClarify customer requirements; probe for and confirm understanding of requirements or problem.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSupport customers across Telecommunication, Financial Services, Healthcare and Technology vertical.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTroubleshoot customer issues related to internet broadband, cable, DTH, modem, router, mobile handset etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCandidate Profile-<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAny Graduate / Under-Graduate / drop out / pursuing Bachelors- any fresher can apply.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBE/Btech fresherâ€™s are not eligible (at least 6 months ICC Experience)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFlexible with 24/7 Environment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary up to 24,000 take home & attractive Incentives amount.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nAdditional Benefits-<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTwo way A/C cabs. (Convergys was awarded for best in industry transport service).<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMedical insurance worth 1 lakhs.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGroup Term Life Insurance / Group Personal accident Insurance worth 5 lakhs<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGratuity<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEducation Assistance plan â€“ Annual entitlement of up to INR 24,000.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEmployee / corporate discounts at majority of retail chains / hospitals / laboratories.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nFor telephonic interview or to inquire about more job openings, please connect with Convergys Hiring Specialist OR Walk-In at below mentioned address:-<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nConvergys Recruitment Center:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nE2/10, 2nd Floor Malviya Nagar, Main Market, Opp Subway Shop above Jogur, Garment, New Delhi, Delhi 110017<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nContact Details:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRohit-9999125126, Shruti-9999125128<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMohit.Kumra@convergys.com, dsg.mn@convergys.com', 'Email: mohit.kumra@convergys.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9999125126', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '15 March, 2017', '2017-03-15', 63, '2017-03-15 01:39:54', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(50079026, 0, 'Project Engineer/Manager', 'Argus Technical Services', '', '1', '90', '20 Jun, 2017', '7', '13', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Franklin, WI', 'Engineering - Civil, Engineering - CAD Design, Project Management', '', '16', '37', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Our client is a preferred designer and manufacturer of steel structures, including mezzanines, mezzanine systems, equipment platforms, towers, catwalks and crossovers for material handling and storage, and support for conveyors, equipment and machinery, and other industrial and commercial uses, with installations throughout the world.<br />\r\nPosition Summary, Project Engineer/Manager<br />\r\nUnder general direction of the Director of Technical Services, develops and execute projects of standard design structures and effectively customize standard designs to meet order-specific customer requirements. Represents the company in communication and coordinate with customers and suppliers.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nDuties and Responsibilities:<br />\r\n <br />\r\nIndependently completes project activity.  Projects can be either product/process improvement or production design process improvement.  Contributes ideas for further improvements.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nResponsible for completing work on multiple projects with respect for completeness, accuracy and adherence to design standards.  All work must be completed in an efficient, accurate and timely manner<br />\r\n <br />\r\nDetail Orientated, ability to communicate with all Drafting, Engineering and Sales/Marketing personnel<br />\r\n\"           Responsible for calculating project cost changes and scope changes and communicating those cost changes to Sales/Marketing to negotiate with customer<br />\r\n\"           Maintaining and updated Project Database for respected projects<br />\r\n\"           Provide guidance and technical support to Associate Project Engineer and Drafting personnel.<br />\r\n\"           Communicate and update stake holders.<br />\r\n\"           Accountable for typical items in project flow chart.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nWorks independently to solve problems, but uses good judgment in seeking guidance where appropriate.  Interfaces with other departments regularly in completing routine work.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nWork content is an even mixture of routine and non-routine tasks.  Typical work requires an understanding of Engineering processes, familiarity with Engineering information and familiarity with data sources.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nIndependently completes complex production designs through utilization of design standards and tools in a 3D CAD modeling environment, often working outside the scope of the tools.  Also completes moderately complex designs or designs that fall outside the scope of the design system.  Able to review more complex customer specifications and make decisions regarding customer specific requirements.  Fluent in product and process knowledge as well as in production structural and mechanical design principles.  Uses this knowledge in decision making.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nComputer literacy is critical as most work requires the use of computer-based systems, a personal computer and a 3D CAD modeling system. <br />\r\n <br />\r\nTypical information used is and required to understand bills of material, drawings, design data and design standards <br />\r\nShare<br />\r\n', '', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '22 March, 2017', '2017-03-22', 56, '2017-03-22 01:09:10', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', '');
