(59312758, 0, 'Urgent Hiring for Tele Sales into Telecom Industry-New Delhi(Near Chattarpur)', 'Indus Global Resources Portal Hiring For Tele sale', '', '2', '90', '04 Jun, 2017', '0', '1', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'IN', '', '434079', 'Delhi ', 'tele sales  international sales', '', '26', '116', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Department: Tele Sales <br />\r\n<br />\r\nLocation: HO <br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary â€“ 20,000 (depending on the current salary) + high Incentives<br />\r\n<br />\r\n Job Summary: <br />\r\n<br />\r\nPurpose of this role is to support the sales team in achieving their targets by generating quality leads for them.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Details:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· To generate quality leads for Sales Team with high probability of conversion.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· Updating the confirmed appointments on the companyâ€™s software and conveying the same to the sales team<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ·Assessing customer\'s need, addressing their queries and suggesting most-suited packages/ plans.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· Responsible for meeting monthly metrics, such as setting appointments, lead conversions and identifying new prospects.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· Maintaining the confidentiality of the data provided by the company for generating the leads.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ·Create rewarding customer experience to ensure retention and providing them with after sales service through proper follow ups<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· Timely maintenance of data and report on the number of leads generated and the allocation of the lead among the sales team.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience - 6 months +<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesired Skills:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· Good Communication and interpersonal skills<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· Customer Focus<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÂ· Excellent Convincing skills', 'Email: hr1.igr@outlook.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 8237304252', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '06 March, 2017', '2017-03-06', 72, '2017-03-06 02:31:11', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(59411199, 0, 'Farm Labor', 'Butterball', '', '2', '90', '28 Jun, 2017', '1', '8', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Raeford, NC', 'Maintain breeder house living conditions by monitoring and troubleshooting issues with feed lines, drinkers, fans, barns, appearance, nest doors,', '', '4', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The statements herein are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by employees and are not to be construed as an exhaustive list of what is required of personnel so classified. They do not imply or establish a contract for employment and are subject to change at the discretion of the employer.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIncumbents in this position are expected to perform the essential functions, tasks, duties, responsibilities, and physical requirements of this role with or without reasonable accommodation within the described work environment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nButterball, LLC is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to the fair and impartial treatment of all employees and applicants for employment without regard to gender, age, race, religion, color, national origin, physical or mental disability, military/veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, genetic information, marital status, parental status, pregnancy, or any other status protected by law.<br />\r\nFarm Labor<br />\r\nLocation:	Tarheel Turkey Farms		FLSA Status:	Non-Exempt<br />\r\nRegion:	Live Operations Farm		City:	Raeford<br />\r\nDepartment:	Live Operations		State:	North Carolina<br />\r\nDescription<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPosition Summary:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIn a timely, safe and humane manner, the associate maybe be responsible for ensuring birds are moved within the turkey house and.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMay require to collect eggs from each nest while removing hens from the nests. Eggs will be placed in flats and taken to egg wash room. Will be responsible for the day to day management of the turkey barn.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEssential Duties, Functions and responsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHelp remove hens from nesting boxes while gathering eggs<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMay maneuver a push cart along breeder house aisles to collect eggs in nesting boxes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWalk through breeder house to collect eggs outside the nesting boxes, and ensure that all birds are moved<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTransfer flats of eggs from the barn to the egg wash room and record the number of eggs collected<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAssist in washing eggs and maintain sanitary conditions in the egg wash room<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWash and disinfect drinkers daily, and replenish drinkers throughout the day to ensure continuous fresh drinking water for the birds<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMaintain breeder house living conditions by monitoring and troubleshooting issues with feed lines, drinkers, fans, barns, appearance, nest doors, etc<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGuide movement of birds within the house<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIdentify and treat any birds with mites<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPerform manual tasks in extreme hot and/or cold temperatures<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to follow Animal Care Well Being and Bio-Security policies and procedures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKnowledge, Skills and Abilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to work up to 6 days a week<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to understand oral and written instructions, and perform simple tasks<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to perform essential duties in a safe and efficient manner.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to follow Animal Care Well Being and Bio-Security policies and procedures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to maintain and record egg gathering information.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to gather eggs in a manner that prevents excessive breakage.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to work with chemicals, such as detergents, disinfectants, etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBasic skills in reading, writing, and arithmetic.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to perform work that is repetitive in nature.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPhysical Requirements:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nStand for long periods of time.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGrip, grasp or twist using hands and wrists<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLift, carry, push, and/or pull up to 50lbs or more.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBend and/or stoop repetitively throughout out shift.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking Conditions/Department Description:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking in a poultry house environment, including working outdoors and in seasonal conditions such as:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking in very hot temperatures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking in very cold temperatures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking in dry and/or dusty environment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking in damp and/or wet climate.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking with live animals, and the associated environment, including but not limited to:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking around farm related smells or foul odors<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking in a loud/noisy environment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWorking in an environment with substantial dust circulation. ', '', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '30 March, 2017', '2017-03-30', 48, '2017-03-30 03:06:50', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(59521224, 0, 'Asst Manager- Company Secretary', 'RJH Consultants.', '', '2', '90', '02 Jul, 2017', '1', '6', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Industry Standards', 'IN', '', '', 'Kolkata', 'Should be a COMPANY SECRETARY', '', '10', '121', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Compliance of Listing Agreements,Company Law,filing of Returns through MCA e-portal,Secretarial functions for facilitating holding of Board,Audit Committee,Investor Grievance Committee and Board\'s Committee Meetings,draft of various agreements etc. <br />\r\nExperience in compliance of Listing Agreements,Company Law, filing of Returns through MCA e-portal, Secretarial functions for facilitating holding of Board, Audit Committee, Board\'s Committee Meetings, draft of various agreements and contracts etc.', 'Email: rjh@airtelmail.in<br />\r\nTelephone: 3324634993', 'CS', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 April, 2017', '2017-04-03', 44, '2017-04-03 02:53:03', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(59525720, 0, 'Sales Officer', 'Life Style Foods Pvt. Ltd.', '', '2', '90', '07 Jun, 2017', '6', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'IN', '', '', 'Delhi', 'sales business Development ', '', '23', '80', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Managing the Team of Sales Representatives in their respective area.<br />\r\nManaging Distributor network in their Respective area.<br />\r\nMeeting Target of his respective area.<br />\r\nHold on A Class Stores in his respective areas.<br />\r\nKnowledge of Computer to prepare Sales reports and Stock Reports of their respective areas', '    Company Name: Life Style Foods Pvt. Ltd.<br />\r\n    Email: hr.lifestylefoodspvtltd@gmail.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 1146370000', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '09 March, 2017', '2017-03-09', 69, '2017-03-09 02:43:19', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(59591111, 0, 'General Admin', 'SRI FAMILY BIZNET PRIVATE LIMITED', '', '2', '90', '22 Jun, 2017', '0', '2', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Chennai/Madras', 'admin office assistant front-office facility management office management Front office Front Office Management ', '', '37', '62', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Dear Candidate,<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe are looking at a immediate joinee for Admin role in our organisation. Please find the details below:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nLocation: OMR, chennai<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nExp: Fresher/Exp all are welcome<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary: 15 to 20K/PM<br />\r\n<br />\r\nImmediate joinee needed<br />\r\n<br />\r\nADMIN RESPONSIBILITIES AT SANGEETHA OMR<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. Software / Hardware issues<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. Resolving Billing software issues and attending system, CCTV, Printer, Weighting scales hardware issues<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. All Insurance renewal : Hotels and staffs Medi-claims (new and renewals)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. All licenses Renewals: All statutory documents - periodical renewal.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. All AMC - Renewals<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6. Vendor follow up & Creative works follow up<br />\r\n<br />\r\n7. Cheques & Payment vouchers verification<br />\r\n<br />\r\n8. Rental agreements<br />\r\n<br />\r\n9. Telephone & EB Payment follow up<br />\r\n<br />\r\n10. Returnable &Non Returnale Gate pass verifications<br />\r\n<br />\r\n11. Security Handling & Attendance Maintenance<br />\r\n<br />\r\n12. Monthly Reports - MIS<br />\r\n<br />\r\n13. Maintenance & DG / EB Register Checking<br />\r\n<br />\r\n14. Incentives verifying<br />\r\n<br />\r\n15. Checking of fire extinguisher and re- filling in time<br />\r\n<br />\r\n16. OT slip Authorizing & New account opening form Authorizing<br />\r\n<br />\r\n17. Staff and Employees Conveyance Check and Approval<br />\r\n<br />\r\n18. Any Maintenance & Office material purchase to approved before Owner<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nRegards,<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTeam HR', 'Email: gopi.r@srifamily.in<br />\r\nTelephone: 9840793308', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 March, 2017', '2017-03-24', 54, '2017-03-24 04:00:36', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(59598746, 0, 'Automobile Sales - Relationship Manager', 'NEXA - Pratham Motors Pvt Ltd', '', '1', '90', '30 May, 2017', '2', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'IN', '', '', 'Bangalore', 'sales business Development ', '', '29', '117', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Background: Sales in Auto / Retail / Hospitality / Aviation & other relevant industries<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIndustry: Automobile / Hospitality Sales / Service Industry etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualification: Min. Graduation Competency Required:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Result oriented - Team player - Good Product knowledge & flair for automobile industry<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Preferably having operational knowledge on retail finance, insurance, exchange etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Excellent Communication & Selling skills - Customer Centric - Valid Car Driving License is compulsory<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPre Sales: Lead generation / Referrals/ Offering Test Drives to customers<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Sales : Cars/ Accessories/ Exchange / Finance / Insurance / Loyalty Card<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Post Sales : Delivery / Service - Understands Customer\'s requirement for finance & Guides Customer on options/ documentation based on his profile.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Keeping track of Customer\'s car related requirements & keeping him posted with regular updates<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Responsible for Customer Satisfaction & long term relationship building', '    Company Name: NEXA - Pratham Motors Pvt Ltd<br />\r\n    Email: hr@nexabangalore.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 9611435655', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '01 March, 2017', '2017-03-01', 77, '2017-03-01 05:54:10', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(59735416, 0, 'Inside Sales & Marketing Representative', 'Dynamic Team Member Wanted!!', '', '1', '90', '05 Jun, 2017', '4', '7', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '11', 'US', '', '', 'Waukesha, WI', 'Marketing - General, Sales - Inside, Sales - Representatives/Service', '', '20', '116', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Accounting firm looking to add a new member to our Inside Sales & Marketing team! Commission plus base pay averages from $12 to $18 per hour. EWH Small Business Accounting is a well-established and quickly expanding firm located in Waukesha, WI.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe are looking for someone reliable and enthusiastic to join us! Paid training in a professional environment is provided. Inside Sales & Marketing team member must enjoy communicating with prospective clients on the phone.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBase pay + Commission, 28 hours per week.<br />\r\nGreat job for supplemental income, a stay at home parent, or anyone looking for a change.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis could be you!<br />\r\nCall Joseph Hastreiter at 262-923-7845<br />\r\njhastreiter@EWHSBA.com', 'Call Joseph Hastreiter at 262-923-7845<br />\r\njhastreiter@EWHSBA.com<br />\r\nSh', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '07 March, 2017', '2017-03-07', 71, '2017-03-07 02:07:15', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(59930042, 17262, 'US IT Recruiter/Techncal Recruiter(US Staffing)', 'Vision InfoSystems Pvt Ltd', '', '10', '30', '02 Apr, 2017', '1', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', 'IN', '', '', 'Noida', 'Recruiter,IT Recruitment,US IT Recruitment,IT Recruiter,1099,C2C,GC', '', '21', '125', '', '', '', 'Meal+Cab', '', '', 'Desired Experience : 6 Months to  3 years  <br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualification: B.SC(IT)/BCA/B.Tech(CS/IT), MCA, PGDIT,MBA,PGDM or Any IT Diploma in 2 Yrs+ Program<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequired Skills :<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCandidates from US Staffing industry / Domestic Recruitment / Consulting Firm / Contract to Hire Agency with Hands on experience on sourcing and End to End Recruitment experiences.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbility to demonstrate Full Recruiting Lifecycle (gathering requirements, candidate prospecting, candidate screening, Negotiations, candidate submission, follow-up, Interview & On Boarding etc)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nProficient in sourcing right candidates through extensive portal search and Vendors.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nShould have excellent communication, convincing skills and negotiation skills<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExcellent understanding of technology and associated technical skill sets<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCandidate shall be self motivated & high on achievement orientation, Should have the ability to deliver results and handle pressure.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nComfortable to work in night shift and Must be able to commute by himself<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRoles & Responsibilities <br />\r\n<br />\r\nResponsible for handling IT requirements from US based clients.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTo understand IT requirements of clients IT resource need and deliver qualified consultants<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSourcing and screening potential IT candidates from effective usage of Internal Systems / Database, Job Portals, Postings and Networking within time frame<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPosting vacancies on portals. Match the profile of the candidate on technical grounds<br />\r\n<br />\r\nResponsible for negotiation, paper work validation and closed candidates for assigned requisitions.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nResponsible for editing and formatting resumes matching consistency and giving visual and technical perfection to them for presenting it to clients.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMaintaining Candidate/Vendor relation on the progress of submittals made, Interview Coordination and taking care of the joining formalities.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n', 'mail to hr@vision-us.com', 'Graduate/Post Graduate', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 March, 2017', '2017-03-03', 75, '2017-03-03 11:22:09', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(60070355, 0, 'Systems Analyst', 'Cal State University, Chancellors Office,', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '7', '12', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Long Beach, CA', 'CHRS Completion Project), and the HR/Student split project', '', '1', '117', '', '', '', '', '', '', ' Chancellor\'s Office Statement<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJoin our team at the California State University, Office of the Chancellor, and make a difference in providing access to higher education. We are currently seeking experienced candidates for the position of HR Business Systems Analyst. The CSU Chancellor\'s Office, located on the waterfront adjacent to the Aquarium of the Pacific in downtown Long Beach, is the headquarters for the nation\'s largest and most diverse system of higher education. The CSU Chancellor\'s Office offers a premium benefit package that includes outstanding vacation, health, and dental plans; a fee waiver education program; membership in the California Public Employees Retirement System (PERS); and 14 paid holidays a year.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUNIQUE OPPORTUNITY!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis is an opportunity to join the largest public university in the nation and become part of the CSU team for a system-wide strategic initiative. Come join the excitement with this rather unique opportunity!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary<br />\r\nThe salary range for this classification is $3,470 to $5,994 per month.<br />\r\nPosition Information<br />\r\nThe California State University, Office of the Chancellor, is seeking a HR Business Systems Analyst to provide functional support for CSU\'s PeopleSoft HCM application within Information Systems. Information Systems\' Application Development area encompasses application support and upgrade activities for 23 campuses and the CSU Chancellor\'s Office (CO), integration with other third-party/external and/or internal systems, the consolidation of the HR databases implementation (CHRS Completion Project), and the HR/Student split project. The HR Business Systems Analyst requires proactive initiative to resolve the most complex HCM application issues in support/development areas that include implementation, system analysis, planning, design, development and support of the HR application. Specific functional support assignments may change at any time based on Application Development\'s projects and priorities, including supporting other applications within the area.<br />\r\nResponsibilities<br />\r\nUnder the general direction of the Project Manager, the HR Business Systems Analyst will:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Participate on project teams as appropriate to implement new system functionality within the PeopleSoft HCM application. Analyze, test and document custom modifications required to address CSU business requirements. Support the HR / Student split activities as well as the CHRS implementation project.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Conduct unit, system, integration and regression testing of PeopleSoft bundles, maintenance pack releases, PeopleTools and Oracle upgrades, and CSU updates and fixes. Coordinate program and functional specification development/testing as well as time and cost estimates for customizations, upgrades and other project activity. This includes conducting conference calls or webinars with the HUG (HR User Group), sub-committees and campus representatives.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Undertake special projects as directed including working with other SME teams to facilitate cross training and coverage of all application areas.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Provide functional production support for 23 CSU campuses and the Chancellor\'s Office by analyzing and troubleshooting campus application issues reported through Service-now cases. Adhere to published Service Level Agreements (SLAs) and Application Development procedures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Create and maintain functional documentation required to support the CSU PeopleSoft HCM application.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Collaborate with all Application Development teams to understand and resolve campus application issues as needed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Produce deliverables that adhere to quality standards and comply with Application Development procedures and practices.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualifications<br />\r\n-This position requires a BA/BS in Computer Science or a related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience, as well as course work in the PeopleSoft HCM application.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Minimum 3-5 years of HR functional experience working with the PeopleSoft HCM application or other similar ERP is required.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-In-depth functional knowledge and experience with at least one HCM module, such as Absence Management, Benefits Administration, Time and Labor, Workforce Administration, Position Management, Recruiting Solutions, or Faculty is required.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Excellent application implementation life cycle skills including experience developing requirements, fit/gap analysis, application configuration and security functional specifications and the ability to translate business requirements into functional designs.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Excellent written and advanced verbal communication skills (including exceptional listening mentoring and collaboration abilities).<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Working knowledge and experience with Human Resources practices and systems in a higher education environment and proficient knowledge of PeopleSoft rules based processing is preferred.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nApplication Period<br />\r\nResumes will be accepted until posting is removed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHow To Apply<br />\r\nApply online at https://cmsweb.cms.csulb.edu/HLBPRD/cocsu_jobs.html<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhen applying please include cover letter and resume in one document<br />\r\nEqual Employment Opportunity<br />\r\nThe university is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate against persons on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, gender, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, medical condition, National origin, sex, sexual orientation, covered veteran status, or any other protected status. Reasonable accommodations will be provided for qualified applicants with disabilities who self-disclose by contacting the Senior Human Resources Manager.<br />\r\nE-Verify<br />\r\nThis position requires new hire employment verification to be processed through the E-Verify program administered by the Department of Homeland Security, U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (DHSUSCIS)\' in partnership with the Social Security Administration (SSA).<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf hired, you will be required to furnish proof that you are legally authorized to work in the United States.<br />\r\nMandated Reporter Per CANRA<br />\r\nThe person holding this position is considered a \'mandated reporter\' under the California Child Abuse and Neglect Reporting Act and is required to comply with the requirements set forth in CSU Executive Order 1083 as a condition of employment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBackground<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe Chancellor\'s Office policy requires that the successful candidate complete a full background check (including a criminal records check) prior to assuming this position.', '', 'Graduation', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '10 April, 2017', '2017-04-10', 37, '2017-04-10 05:48:22', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(60250740, 74820, 'AVP - Investment Banking - Financial Group', 'Dimensions HRD Consultants', '', '', '90', '12 Jun, 2017', '0', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '2', 'IN', '', '434079', 'Delhi', 'Valuation, Financial Modelling, Finance, Investment Banking, Financial, Advisory, Strategy', 'http://careers.dimensionshrd.com', '10', '110', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Position based in Gurgaon with a large Financial Group<br />\r\n<br />\r\nConducting detailed industry research & identifying sectors for Business Development (deal origination)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFinancial Modeling Analysis and Credit Monitoring Arrangements<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIdentifying challenges in the transactions, based on detailed study and analysis<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPreparing presentations and pitch-books on strategic and financial advisory, sector analysis, evaluation of acquisition opportunities and competitor benchmarking<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDeveloping financial forecasts, three statement modelling and analysing performance metrics<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBuilding valuation models', '', 'Any Postgraduate and Graduate', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '14 March, 2017', '2017-03-14', 64, '2017-03-14 04:33:49', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(60386340, 0, 'Data Governance Lead (HR / Finance)', 'The Carrera Agency', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '4', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'San Jose, CA', 'Business Intelligence, Change Management, Customer Service, Development, EDM, ERP, Manager, Management, Metrics, Oracle, Oracle Financials, Project, Project Management, SAP ', '', '2', '133', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'We are seeking a Data Quality Lead to join the Enterprise Data Management (EDM) group for our client, a leader in their industry. Their culture promotes associates to focus on providing quality work, producing robust and innovative products, along with amazing customer service and operational excellence. This is a Contract-to-Hire position, based preferably out of the client\'s San Jose office, but may also be based in Irvine.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n** W2 and Independent Contractors only, please. Sorry, no 3rd party applicants. **<br />\r\n<br />\r\nData Quality Lead - Enterprise Data Governance<br />\r\nThe Data Quality Leads report to the Sr. Manager, Enterprise Data Quality within Enterprise Data Governance / IT organization. The Data Quality Lead is a facilitator of data stewardship which is the process for making decisions about the business rules for data and determining who will be responsible for the quality of the data. This person plays a pivotal role in supporting the business data stewards who are the primary point of responsibility, accountability and activity for the assessment, improvement and ongoing maintenance of critical data assets.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPrimary responsibilities<br />\r\n* Facilitate the identification of business and technical data stewards<br />\r\n* Coordinate functional and technical data stewards (function specific) to ensure best practices and common processes are followed, coordinate data stewardship program activities and data standards definition<br />\r\n* Document business rules and define business data standards<br />\r\n* Report on the effectiveness of standards processes (standards defined, where applied, etc. - not quality of content)<br />\r\n* Facilitate the standards exception process and answers questions on standards usage/scope<br />\r\n* Propose upgrade/enhancement projects as required to meet Data Quality requirements<br />\r\n* Consult on projects to provide guidance/support on Data Governance and Data Quality best practices and processes, data profiling readiness and execution, data profiling results analysis, documentation and data quality recommendations<br />\r\n* Provide training on data governance, data quality, data profiling and analysis<br />\r\n* Facilitate Stewardship Communities of Interest to<br />\r\no Build consensus for data related issues (issue management, change management, etc)<br />\r\no Improve visibility to process metrics and critical information<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Oversight: commitment to best practices and process improvement opportunities<br />\r\n<br />\r\no Change evaluation: review and evaluate impacts of change<br />\r\no Establish communication between business process owners, functional area leads, SME\'s and business analysts<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBecause of the focus of this role, it has specific activities that differ from other Data Quality Leads:<br />\r\n* Learning, following and upholding HR, Financial and Legal policies and procedures established by the client and external regulatory agencies.<br />\r\n* Implement data quality processes and procedures in accordance with record retention requirements established by the client and external regulatory agencies.<br />\r\n* Perform periodic internal reviews and support the Legal department on efforts such as an annual gap analysis and internal controls certification process to ensure continued compliance with corporate financial policies, administrative and accounting procedures.<br />\r\n* Participate in initiatives, programs and projects such as MDM and ERP to ensure appropriate stakeholders are involved, regulatory interests are considered, and data stewards are supported in the interests of ensuring high quality data.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualifications<br />\r\n* Degree in Information Management, Data Governance, Computer Science or other related field<br />\r\n* 10+ years relevant experience in data management, data warehousing/business intelligence leadership roles; successful track record of implementing pragmatic impactful data strategy, standards, and quality programs with effective business adoption and analytic focus<br />\r\n* Solid understanding and working knowledge of data governance principals and best practices<br />\r\n* Broad knowledge of engineering industry operations preferred<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSkills<br />\r\n* Business Domain knowledge (HR, Legal or Finance)<br />\r\n* Subject Matter Expertise in area of Data Standards and Data Quality<br />\r\n* Experience in project management and meeting facilitation<br />\r\n* Previous experience executing in a senior level role with minimum oversight<br />\r\n* Excellent oral/written communication<br />\r\n* Experience with at least one Enterprise Business Application, System or similar (Ex: People Soft, SAP, Oracle Financials, etc.)<br />\r\n* People focused - excellent interpersonal skills, including communication and facilitation and is comfortable coaching people at all levels of the organization<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbilities<br />\r\n* Produce a variety of management reports for executive audiences<br />\r\n* Effectively present information to influence organizational leaders and key stakeholders<br />\r\n* Analyze and synthesize data to form options and recommendations<br />\r\n* Collaborate with people at different levels within the organization to accomplish a common goal<br />\r\n* Clearly and confidently convey information to a wide audience<br />\r\n* Build long-term collaborative working relationships with senior managers<br />\r\n* Model corporate values in personal work behaviors, decision-making, contributions and interpersonal interactions; manage own career development by soliciting feedback and valuing other perspectives.', '', 'Graduation', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '10 April, 2017', '2017-04-10', 37, '2017-04-10 05:41:50', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(60402841, 0, 'Administrative Assistant ', 'Swasthik sahits solutions private limited', '', '2', '90', '22 Jun, 2017', '0', '2', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Chennai/Madras', 'General Office Administration Administrative Assistant ', '', '1', '117', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Administrative Assistant will be responsible for the General Office Administration, visit to various locations like Banks, Vendors, Clients for pickup and drop of documents. Must have the knowledge of driving the two wheeler and possess licensed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMale Candidates with 10+2 qualified to handle the general administration of the office. Must be willing to travel witthin the City on Two Wheeler. Handling Computers will be an added advantage', '    Company Name: Swasthik sahits solutions private limited<br />\r\n    Email: swasthikstaff@gmail.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 9087140008', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 March, 2017', '2017-03-24', 54, '2017-03-24 03:58:18', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', '');
INSERT INTO `jobs` (`jobid`, `uid`, `job_title`, `company_name`, `about_company`, `vacancies`, `jobs_active`, `job_expiry`, `work_experience_min`, `work_experience_max`, `job_type`, `contract_rate`, `contract_duration`, `internship_salary`, `internship_duration`, `salary`, `job_country`, `job_state`, `job_city`, `location`, `key_skills`, `job_url`, `industry`, `functional_area`, `youtube_url`, `telecommute`, `security_clearance`, `benefits`, `requirements`, `instruction`, `description`, `how_apply`, `academic_degree`, `dress_code`, `WorkAuthorize`, `PreferredEmployment`, `us_citizen`, `gc`, `ead`, `h1b`, `corp_corp`, `w2_permanant`, `w2_contract`, `1099_contract`, `contract_hire`, `date`, `count_date`, `days_ago`, `datetime`, `country_from`, `status`, `facebook_url`, `twitter_url`, `gplush_url`, `message`) VALUES
(60790564, 0, 'MALE Manager (Architect) Reqd at Vijaywada Exp 8 yrs Sal 9 LPA', 'A & J Global Solutions Private Limited', '', '1', '90', '15 Jun, 2017', '8', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '5', 'IN', '', '', 'Vijayawada', 'Engineering Sales Financial Projections CAD Management CIVIL Design Marketing Reports DRAWING Evaluation MS office Estate Management Construction AMP ', '', '16', '99', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Dear Job seeker,<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGreeting from A&J Global Solutions !!!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOne of our esteemed client having corporate office in Hyderabad. They have an urgent requirement for MALE Manager (Architect) for their residential projects at Vijayawada.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesignation: Manager (Architect)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n(ONLY MALE CANDIDATE)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExperience: Minimum 8 years in property development, preferably handling large scale residential developments.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIndustry: Construction Company<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualification: B.Tech / BE in Civil Engineering , B.Arch and Post graduate diploma/degree in Real Estate management.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nComputer skills: Auto cad, Ms Office (Words / Excel / Power point), Microsoft Projects planner<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary: 75,000 Per Month<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLocation: Vijayawada<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Description :<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Coordination with all consultants for design development.<br />\r\n    Coordination with Construction department for the evaluation, analyzing, expedite work progress & drawing management.<br />\r\n    Supervise the Construction progress and quality.<br />\r\n    Preparation & monitor status reports of authority, design progress<br />\r\n    Liaison with authorities for entire development (Residential & Commercial) approvals.<br />\r\n    Develop / Evaluate feasibility studies for new parcels of land for development.<br />\r\n    Preparing property development budgets for financial projections.<br />\r\n    Develop data & information required for marketing promos & sales kit.', 'Email: civiljobs.ajglobal@gmail.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9397617779', 'B.Tech / BE in Civil Engineering , B.Arch and Post graduate diploma/degree in Real Estate management.', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '17 March, 2017', '2017-03-17', 61, '2017-03-17 02:41:06', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(60864348, 0, 'Protocol Developer', 'Silverlink Technologies.', '', '2', '90', '15 Jun, 2017', '5', '8', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '5', 'IN', '', '', 'Hyderabad', 'TP VTP ', '', '16', '99', '', '', '', '', '', '', '5+ years of experience on Network Switching L2/L3 protocols De- STP, RSTP, MSTP, VLAN, VTP, LACP, HSRP, VRRP, ATM, PPP, 802.1X 5+ years of experience on Network Routing L2/L3 protocols Dev-OSPF, BGP, RIP, IGRP, EIGRP, RSVP, LDP, VPN, QoS .', 'Email: devaprasad@silverlinktechnologies.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 4782552211', 'B.Tech / BE in Civil Engineering , B.Arch and Post graduate diploma/degree in Real Estate management.', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '17 March, 2017', '2017-03-17', 61, '2017-03-17 02:42:53', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(60947172, 74820, 'Linux/Security Architect', '1 Point System LLC', '', '', '30', '08 Apr, 2017', '1', '4', 'Contract', 'Open', '0 - 3 Months', '', '', '', 'US', '', '', 'Naperville, IL', 'RedHat Linux, Solaris', '', '23', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Experience - Large enterprise shop - Physical, Virtual and public cloud environments - Financial industry - RedHat Linux (PAM, syslog, auditd) - IBM / AIX (authentication, syslog, audit) - Solaris (PAM, syslog, auditd) - Oracle (ExaData / ExaLogic) - MS Server - LDAP (DSEE) & AD - SUDO - Privileged Account Access Products (CyberArk, Quest, CA) - vmWare (ESX, NSX) - Host based security monitoring and controls <br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- want to bring in someone who is already an expert<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- address how they are doing things - if they need to fix things, why and how?<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- they know this is not usually pushed out through Beeline but they want to see if their suppliers can fill this<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- technical person: the big part of the role is assessment and working with the SMEs \' may get involved with some of the implementation<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-platform group - Linux specific<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- job titles that would be good: Architectural, security focused, Engineer works as well<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- financial background is a plus but not mandatory: governmental or highly regulated environments are fine<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Top skills: large enterprise shop, Linux experience, and security tools<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- very possible to go longer than 3 months<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- no specific product<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Phone then onsite interview', 'Vineet Mishra<br />\r\nP: 803-317-2541 E : vineet@1pointsys.com', '', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '09 March, 2017', '2017-03-09', 69, '2017-03-08 13:16:08', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(61193030, 0, 'RN - NICU - Florida Hospital for Children - Nights', 'Florida Hospital', '', '1', '90', '05 Jul, 2017', '5', '10', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Orlando, FL', 'EKG, ACLS, PALS, NRP ', '', '31', '106', '', '', '', '', '', '', '<br />\r\nRN Neonatal ICU â€“ Florida Hospital for Children â€“ Orlando - Nights<br />\r\n <br />\r\nFlorida Hospital for Children seeks to hire a Neonatal ICU Registered Nurse who will embrace our mission to extend the healing ministry of Christ. <br />\r\n <br />\r\nFlorida Hospital for Children Profile<br />\r\n <br />\r\nSince opening our doors in 1908, Florida Hospital has offered one of the most comprehensive childrenâ€™s health programs in Central Florida. Today, we continue this legacy of pediatric excellence at the MagnetÂ® recognized Walt Disney Pavilion at Florida Hospital for Children.<br />\r\nOur campus is home to 30 pediatric sub-specialties led by a team of 400+ nurses and physicians. We provide specialized care in various state-of-the-art settings, including an 81-bed Neonatal Intensive Care Unit with private family-centered rooms, an Advanced Center for Pediatric Surgery handling nearly 4,000 cases each year, and one of the few pediatric oncology programs in the area. Weâ€™re also Central Floridaâ€™s only pediatric provider for bone marrow transplant, kidney transplant, Gamma Knife services, trilogy radiation and Level III epilepsy care. But perhaps most exciting of all, is that this is the firstâ€”and onlyâ€”hospital to bear the DisneyÂ® name.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nNeonatal Intensive Care Unit<br />\r\n <br />\r\nWalt Disney Pavilion at Florida Hospital for Children is home to a 53-bed Level III NICU and a 28-bed Level II NICU, where we provide the highest level of care for Godâ€™s tiniest miracles. Weâ€™re proud to have successfully helped more than 11,000 babies overcome serious health issues through our Neonatal Intensive Care Unit.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nWork Hours/Shifts<br />\r\n <br />\r\nFull- time: Nights, 7:00p- 7:00a 3/12 hr shifts per week, including every other weekend<br />\r\n <br />\r\nJob Summary<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    As a NICU RN with Florida Hospital for Children you will make providing service your priority while caring for the whole person in a faith-based atmosphere.<br />\r\n    The RN is a registered professional nurse who is responsible for providing and supervising direct and indirect total nursing care responsibilities to identified age specific groups. Utilizing the nursing process (assessing, planning, implementing and evaluating) in achieving the goals of the nursing department.  For job class codes GRN and R120, graduates nurses and experienced nurses entering a training program will be under the direct supervision of a preceptor for all principal duties and responsibilities during the training program with eventual transition to independent practice after successful training program completion. Adheres to the Florida Hospital Corporate Compliance Plan and to all rules and regulations of all applicable local, state and federal agencies and accrediting bodies. Actively participates in outstanding customer service and accepts responsibility in maintaining relationships that are equally respectful to all. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nKnowledge, Skills, Education and Experience Required<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    American Heart Association (AHA) Basic Life Support (BLS) certification<br />\r\n    If certification is from another agency, certification from AHA must be obtained within 90 days of hire AND<br />\r\n    AHA Advanced life support certification (ACLS, PALS, NRP) per specialty/unit requirements<br />\r\n    If certification is from another agency, certification from AHA must be obtained by 90 day evaluation<br />\r\n    EKG, ACLS, PALS, NRP (based on patient population; See document EKG and Advanced Life Support Requirements) (preferred)<br />\r\n    Graduate of a school of nursing<br />\r\n    For Graduate Registered Nurse (GRN), graduate of an accredited school of nursing<br />\r\n    For all job classes except GRN and R120, unit related experience is required for unit placement<br />\r\n    Bachelorâ€™s degree in Nursing (preferred)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\nLicensure, Certification or Registration Required<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Current registration with Florida State Board of Nursing as a registered professional nurse.<br />\r\n    Professional certification (preferred)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\nJob Responsibilities<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Demonstrates through behavior Florida Hospitalâ€™s Core Values of Integrity, Compassion, Balance, Excellence, Stewardship and Teamwork as outlined in the organizationâ€™s Performance Excellence Program.<br />\r\n    NURSING PROCESS: Completes timely assessments per Practice Guidelines including physiological, psychological, developmental, sociocultural, spiritual and life-style factors, including signs of abuse or neglect. Makes appropriate decisions and interventions and nursing diagnosis according to patients actual or potential health conditions or needs. (American Nurses Association [ANA], 2012)<br />\r\n    NURSING PROCESS: Based on the assessment and diagnosis, sets measurable and achievable short and long-range goals for the patient (ANA, 2012), assisting in the development and implementation of an individualized plan of care. Prioritizes and completes follow up assessments, evaluates and modifies plan of care as need. Nursing practice reflects mutual goal setting and whole person care including meeting the needs of the mind, body and spirit. (King, 1995)<br />\r\n    NURSING KNOWLEDGE: Demonstrates the ability to assess and interpret diagnostic data relative to patient age and condition, including, but not limited to lab results, non-invasive monitoring data and interdisciplinary team notes. Nursing practice reflects the application of knowledge and skills pertaining to all diagnoses, procedures, medications, complications, and equipment associated with unit patient population. <br />\r\n    PATIENT SAFETY: Nursing practice reflects the application of knowledge, skill and adherence to all pertinent regulatory standards.  Follows strict infection prevention precautions. Adheres to policy and procedure regarding all aspects of medication safety. Practice reflects importance of patient teaching and takes advantage of opportunities, both planned and unplanned, to carry it out in accordance with plan of care.<br />\r\n    COMMUNICATION: Promotes an exceptional patient experience by abiding to compassion and image standards and fostering excellent nurse-patient relationships through effective/therapeutic communication with the patient, family, and visitors, including but not limited to and as applicable, hourly rounding. Exhibits ability to utilize appropriate techniques, verbiage, and resources in all interactions with the patient to their level of understanding.  Communicates effectively with interdisciplinary team by completing thorough hand off communication in all situations. Follows chain of command when appropriate.<br />\r\n    DOCUMENTATION: Demonstrates knowledge and skill in the recording and accessing of all patient information in electronic medical record according to policy and in real time. Performs appropriate and legible documentation, recording all procedures and assessments within established timeframes, and in accordance with standards of care, departmental policy and practice guidelines. <br />\r\n    PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT: Abides by American Nurses Association Scope, Standards and Code of Ethics. Participates in practice changes, process improvement initiatives and completes all required education by the due date. Supports quality standards and initiatives set by the department.  Exhibits desire to learn, teach, mentor and advance nursing skills. <br />\r\n    RELIEF CHARGE NURSE (as applicable): Under the supervision of a manager, assumes authority of the daily operations of the unit/department and is the primary resource nurse for a specific shift. Manages staff accountability and adherence to regulatory requirements. The leadership responsibility includes but is not limited to facilitation of the team dynamics of patient care, patient experience and patient flow including managing staff assignments.  Additional management responsibilities include effective conflict resolution, patient/staff rounding and communication, resource utilization, comprehensive hand off communication and completion of unit specific audits/checklists as required or assigned.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\nIf you want to be a part of a team that is dedicated to delivering the highest quality in patient care, we invite you to explore the Neonatal ICU Registered Nurse opportunity with Florida Hospital for Children and apply online today.<br />\r\n <br />\r\n NICU, III, Full Time, Orlando, Nights, Full Time, Neonatal, Florida Hospital for Children ', '', 'Associate\'s Degree', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '06 April, 2017', '2017-04-06', 41, '2017-04-05 23:08:52', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(61239019, 0, 'Senior Personal Banker', 'National Residential', '', '1', '90', '13 Jun, 2017', '3', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '12', 'US', '', '', 'Madison, WI', 'Banking', '', '10', '62', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'The Senior Personal Banker is responsible for building retail relationships with our customers and helping them exceed their financial expectations through extraordinary delivery of products and services.<br />\r\n <br />\r\nResponsibilities:<br />\r\n <br />\r\n1. Offer and sell financial products and services to both consumer and small business customers. Including, but not limited to:<br />\r\na. Checking and Savings Accounts<br />\r\nb. Certificates of Deposit<br />\r\nc. Individual Retirement Accounts (IRAs)<br />\r\nd. Health Savings Accounts<br />\r\ne. Consumer Loans<br />\r\nf. Credit Life/Disability, GAP and MOB insurance on consumer loans<br />\r\ng. Home Equity Loans/Lines of Credit<br />\r\nh. Credit Cards<br />\r\n2. Provide first line back up for all Personal Banking positions daily to include but not limited to:<br />\r\na. Operating a transaction window (when required based on banking center needs)<br />\r\nb. Open, close and service customer accounts<br />\r\nc. Processing customer checking, savings and loan transactions<br />\r\n3. Provide excellent customer service while listening for sales opportunities; explains and promotes bank products or services to customers<br />\r\n4. Follow up with prospects and current customers by telephone or letter to promote new products and services and/or thanking customers for existing business.<br />\r\n5. Actively monitor the status of key customer relationships to promote business growth and service quality<br />\r\n6. Answer questions and solve problems for customers and<br />\r\n7. Opens, closes, and allows, customer\'s access to their safety deposit box following specified procedures if necessary<br />\r\n8. Opens and closes the banking center according to bank security policy<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequirements:<br />\r\n1. High School Diploma/GED. Bachelor\'s Degree preferred.<br />\r\n2. 3-5 years of experience in sales & customer service<br />\r\n3. Customer facing banking experience preferred but not required<br />\r\n4. Proven ability to meet sales goals<br />\r\n5. High attention to detail<br />\r\nApply online at: www.htlf.com/#/careers<br />\r\n', 'www.htlf.com/#/careers', 'MBA', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '15 March, 2017', '2017-03-15', 63, '2017-03-15 02:09:53', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(61619251, 0, 'Marketing Communications Intern', 'Master Lock Company', '', '1', '90', '22 Jun, 2017', '2', '7', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Oak Creek, WI', 'Marketing - General, Internships, Marketing - Communications/PR', '', '1', '72', '', '', '', '', 'QUALIFICATIONS:<br />\r\n*Minimum of Junior standing in an accredited Marketing program<br />\r\n*Grade Point: 3.0 or higher<br />\r\n*Year Round Availability (summer up to 40 hours/week)<br />\r\n*Strong organization and analytical skills and attention to detail<br />\r\n*Ability to manage timelines<br />\r\n*Strong oral and written communication skills<br />\r\n*Proficient in Excel, Powerpoint, Word, etc.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n	<br />\r\n	<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe Master Lock Company is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants are considered for positions without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex, sexual preference, age (40 and over), disability, genetic information, military or veteran status, citizenship, or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. The Master Lock Company also prohibits harassment of applicants or employees based on any of these protected categories.', '', 'DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES:<br />\r\nPackage Development:<br />\r\n*Assist in proofing all packaging text for appropriate content.<br />\r\n*Assist in obtaining verification of all translations with Canada and Nogales.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nProduct Launches:<br />\r\n*Assist in coordinating launch materials with Marketing Services Specialist.<br />\r\n*Order product and supplies such as special boxes, bubble wrap promotional item<br />\r\n*Assist in packing and shipping launch kits<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLine Reviews:<br />\r\n*Assist in tracking status of product/ packaging and merchandise components needed to complete line review planogram set up.<br />\r\n*Complete packaging mockups as needed<br />\r\n*Set up planogram with required materials<br />\r\n*Assist in providing any planogram or product photography to sales/marketing for presentations.<br />\r\n*Pack and ship planograms if needed for sales presentations<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTrade Shows:<br />\r\n*Order product<br />\r\n*Order literature<br />\r\n*Gather new items from product managers<br />\r\n*Track product shipment & review spreadsheet of items received at The Design Agency to confirm all products, literature and signage has been received<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCatalogs & Literature/Website Materials:<br />\r\n*Obtain literature numbers from fulfillment site coordinator<br />\r\n*Notify fulfillment site of new material and quantities<br />\r\n*Notify fulfillment site of obsolete materials and quantities<br />\r\n*Review monthly log from fulfillment site for reprints and work with product manager to determine status of piece (ie; reprint,obsolete)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWebsites:<br />\r\n*Update and proof websites for accuracy, facilitating changes with appropriate parties as needed<br />\r\n*Includes Master Lock websites and customer websites<br />\r\n*Assist in monitoring Facebook page activity<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPurchase Orders:<br />\r\n*Assist in process all purchase order related to development and production of design work for packaging, merchandising and collateral<br />\r\n*Match invoices to purchase orders<br />\r\n*Maintain files<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMeeting Room Organization:<br />\r\n*Maintain neat and ordering product displays in core retail meeting room, work room and planogram room<br />\r\n*Order replacement product as needed<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKey Relationships:<br />\r\n*Work closely with marketing services specialist, internal graphic designer, marketing, sales, and outside marketing communications suppliers<br />\r\n<br />\r\nVALUES:<br />\r\n*Demonstrates INTEGRITY<br />\r\n*WORKS AS A TEAM<br />\r\n*Takes OWNERSHIP<br />\r\n*ACTION - biased<br />\r\n*Fosters a WINNING spirit<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKEY COMPETENCIES:<br />\r\n*Collaborate: Build partnerships and work collaboratively with others to meet shared objectives<br />\r\n*Communicate Effectively: Develop and deliver multi-mode communications that convey a clear understanding of the unique needs of different audiences<br />\r\n*Instill Trust: Gain the confidence and trust of others through honest, integrity and authenticity<br />\r\n*Drives Results: Consistently achieves results, even under tough circumstances<br />\r\n*Plans and Aligns: Plan and prioritize work to meet commitments aligned with organizational goals<br />\r\n*Action Oriented: Take on new opportunities and tough challenges with a sense of urgency, high energy and enthusiasm', '', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '24 March, 2017', '2017-03-24', 54, '2017-03-24 04:57:43', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(61817516, 0, 'Hiring For Assistant Manager ( Contract Management ) In Finance', 'Career Innovators Hiring For Career Innovators Pvt', '', '2', '0', '', '2', '6', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Bangalore', 'Senior Management   FinanceManagement', '', '10', '39', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'We are looking for Assistant Manager for Contract Management ( Finance) profile in Finance Department for a Leading Company based out in Gurgaon.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary Bracket of 60K- 70K Rs / Month<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe contract managers task is to ensure consistent management of all proposals and contracts. This generally includes oversight of the contract management process, as well as development of specific standards and document management. The contract managers role in the contract management process requires close collaboration with various departments, including the user department, legal department and other stakeholders<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRESPONSIBILITIES<br />\r\n<br />\r\nParticipate in organizational contract development and management activities, and enforce organizational principles of integrity and compliance<br />\r\nDraft contractual provisions based on strategy discussions, senior management input, and organizational needs and expectations.<br />\r\nAssure accuracy and appropriateness of contract text and attachments.<br />\r\nCarry out Interface with user department(s) within the company<br />\r\nMaintain deadlines on deliverables and communicate on an ongoing basis with internal clients about contractual issues<br />\r\nReview contractual performance of both parties to ensure compliance with terms and to identify conflicts or changes requiring resolution at contract renewal<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQUALIFICATIONS<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAssistant Manager <br />\r\nMBA (Finance) from a premier institute or CA, having relevant experience as outlined above in the Aviation Industry. The candidate should have an experience of around 4-5 years.<br />\r\nMBA or CA (Inter.) having an experience of over 2 years preferably in the Aviation Industry<br />\r\nRequired Skills: <br />\r\nExcellent Communication skills,<br />\r\nAbility to work in a dynamic and challenging environment is essential.<br />\r\nGood Command over Spoken English.<br />\r\nExcellent problem solving skills<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCall on to Apply:-<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCall or Whats App on +91 9560377764 ( HR JOSHNA)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDrop Cvs on<br />\r\n<br />\r\njobs@careerinnovators.com<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWebsite :www.careerinnovators.com<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCorporate Office <br />\r\nCAREER INNOVATORS PVT.LTD Corporate Tower- 2nd floor, Dwarka Mor metro station, opposite Metro Pillar no 766, New Delhi Land Mark Above Yes Bank<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIMPORTANT NOTE: We are the Authorized Consultants for a lot Companies in India and Dubai Hence DO NOT CHARGE any Placement Charges Before or after your Job (FREE RECRUITMENT) www.careerinnovators.com<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n**** Thank You for Making us No.1 HR Consultant www.careerinnovators.com ****', 'Email: jobs@careerinnovators.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9560377764', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '21 February, 2017', '2017-02-21', 85, '2017-02-21 08:11:28', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(61868746, 86018, 'Urgent requirement for BPO Voice Process', 'Staffing Solution & Service', '', '', '0', '', '0', '1', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'Jaipur, ', '', '', '9', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', '', '', 'Excellent Communication Skills (oral & written)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nâ€¢ Minimum qualification - Graduation/Diploma (10+2+3)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nâ€¢ Should be willing to work in shifts or 24/7 environment<br />\r\n<br />\r\nâ€¢ Location of Posting will be Jaipur<br />\r\n<br />\r\nâ€¢ Should be willing to work in a voice process', '', 'Any Graduation ', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '07 February, 2017', '2017-02-07', 99, '2017-02-07 00:24:32', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62068045, 17527, 'Corporate Sales', 'Career  Glitz', '', '10', '0', '', '1', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'New Delhi, ', 'Customer Support, Customer Service, Corporate Sales, Corporate Marketing', '', '3', 'Select Functional Area', '', '', 'Y', '', 'Requirement: <br />\r\nÃ˜   minimum 1-5 years exp.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÃ˜  Time Management Skills.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÃ˜  Should be Proactive, Innovative and Enthusiastic with Positive Attitude.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nÃ˜  Excellent Communication skills (Verbal & Non-verbal).', '', 'Please find the below Job Description:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nResponsibilities:<br />\r\nCorporate Marketing and Relationship Management for Research services, Media Based Branding platforms and Publishing.<br />\r\nTo Develop & maintain productive business relationship with key decision makers across client organizations.<br />\r\nSet up strategic partnerships with leading institutions to position the organization as a preferred outsourcing partner for Research based Branding Platforms<br />\r\nMedia Monitoring and benchmarking<br />\r\nCustomer Relationship Management<br />\r\n', 'Interested candidates can share your resume to sneha@careerglitz.com or can call at 01141035353', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '14 November, 2016', '2016-11-14', 184, '2016-11-14 06:41:36', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62089354, 0, 'Accountancy/Finance Recruitment Consultant New York ', 'Ruth Moran Consulting', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '6', '11', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', ' New York', 'Selection\' \'recruitment managerâ€™ \'branch managerâ€™ \'', '', '2', '117', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'EXPERIENCE OF WORKING WITHIN RECRUITMENT IS ESSENTIAL.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOur client is a market leader in its sector. They have experienced over 100% growth year on year Based at their expanding New York site, they genuinely focus on offering a quality service to both clients and candidates, their aim being to provide the best candidates at all times for their clients via both a superb candidate database and a variety of marketing tools As a result of this they have some extremely strong markets and have significant connections to attract the very best.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFor further information please contact Ruth Moran weekdays 8am-9pm or apply online. You can also visit the Ruth Moran Consulting website.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRuth Moran Consulting, founded in 1999, is one of the longest established recruitment to recruitment consultancies, working across the UK and Internationally. If you are an experienced recruitment professional looking for advice and guidance about the market and your next role, please do not hesitate to contact us in the strictest of confidence.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlease note we are only able to respond to Candidates who have Recruitment Agency experience. If you have not heard from us within three working days, unfortunately, on this occasion, your application has not been successful.', 'Address: 10 Butts Ct, Leeds LS1 5JS, UK<br />\r\nPhone: +44 113 246 0062', 'Graduation', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '10 April, 2017', '2017-04-10', 37, '2017-04-10 05:26:10', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62093537, 0, 'URGENT OPENING FOR TEAM LEADER,GROUP LEADER IN A RENOWNED RO INDUSTRY IN KANPUR', 'EHC Pvt. Ltd.', '', '1', '90', '05 Jul, 2017', '1', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Industry Standards', 'IN', '', '', 'Kanpur', 'sales executive ', '', '1', '38', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Greetings of the day!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nSupports team manager and performs management duties when manager is absent or out of office<br />\r\nManages inventories and stock, including keeping detailed records of inventory use and sales, and advising management on ordering where necessary<br />\r\nProvides encouragement to team members, including communicating team goals and identifying areas for new training or skill checks<br />\r\nAssists management with hiring processes and new team member training<br />\r\nAnswers team member questions, helps with team member problems, and oversees team member work for quality and guideline compliance<br />\r\nCommunicates deadlines and sales goals to team members<br />\r\nDevelops strategies to promote team member adherence to company regulations and performance goals<br />\r\nConducts team meetings to update members on best practices and continuing expectations<br />\r\nGenerates and shares comprehensive and detailed reports about team performance, mission-related objectives, and deadlines<br />\r\nEnsures company brand materials and physical working spaces meet and exceed company presentation standards<br />\r\nProvides quality customer service, including interacting with customers, answering customer enquiries, and effectively handling customer complaints<br />\r\nTeam Leader Skills and Qualifications:<br />\r\nTeam Leadership Experience, Product Knowledge and Industry Experience, Leadership Skills, Strong Oral and Written Communication Skills, Motivational Skills, Results-Oriented, Employee Training Experience, Interviewing Skills, Sales Skills, Self-Motivation, Strong Relationship Building, Customer Service Skills.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nEXPERIENCE: 1-3YRS<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLOCATION: KANPUR, LUCKNOW<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSALARY:2.5L<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nBest Regards,<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\npoonam<br />\r\n<br />\r\n9910809224<br />\r\n<br />\r\npunam8561@gmail.com', '    Company Name: EHC Pvt. Ltd.<br />\r\n    Company Description:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    ECONNEXIONS HR CONSULTANTS PVT. LTD.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n     <br />\r\n<br />\r\n     <br />\r\n    With Regards.<br />\r\n    Neha Bulsara<br />\r\n    HR Recruiter-Econnexion HR consultants<br />\r\n    (9428069154,8160842824)<br />\r\n     <br />\r\n<br />\r\n     <br />\r\n<br />\r\n     <br />\r\n    Email: punam8561@gmail.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 9910809224', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '06 April, 2017', '2017-04-06', 41, '2017-04-05 22:50:12', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62098404, 0, 'Accounting Manager, Multi-Platform Media Company in LA', 'CyberCoders,', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '6', '9', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Los Angeles, CA', 'Corporate Accounting, Excel, TV/Movie Production Lifecycle, CPA - Corporate Accounting, Excel, TV/Movie Production Lifecycle, CPA ', '', '2', '39', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Minimum Required Skills:<br />\r\nCorporate Accounting, Excel, TV/Movie Production Lifecycle, CPA<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf you are an Accounting Manager with experience in Corporate Accounting and understanding of TV Production Finance, please read on!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe are a global multi-platform media company, a leading destination for original programming serving the global Gen Z audience. We\'re a family of complementary brands, including: a global creator community, an influencer talent management company, and we connect our brands with our audience through our brand partnerships division.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhat You Will Be Doing<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe Manager of Accounting role will be a liaison between Corporate Accounting, Corporate Finance, and Production. This individual must have a strong understanding of traditional & entertainment accounting, along with knowledge of production operations and production finance, to drive on-going development of our policies, processes, and reporting to strengthen the internal controls and procedures. This role is fast-paced and dynamic, which requires someone who is a self-starter, independent, and willing to wear multiple hats.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhat You Need for this Position<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMust-Have Skills:<br />\r\n- 6+ Years of Corporate Accounting experience (balance sheets, monthly reports, AR/AP)<br />\r\n- TV Production Accounting/Finance knowledge and experience<br />\r\n- Proven ability to lead and manage a team<br />\r\n- Strong systems skills - proficiency in MS Office skills including Word, Excel<br />\r\n- Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills<br />\r\n- Ability to understand and articulate issues using creative, production, or financial context<br />\r\n- B.A./B.S. in Accounting or Finance<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBonus Skills:<br />\r\n- CPA and/or MBA (HIGHLY preferred to have CPA)<br />\r\n- Ease/Vista experience a plusSo, if you are a Manager of Accounting with experience in Corporate & TV Production Accounting, with strong Excel skills, please apply today!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nApplicants must be authorized to work in the U.S.Please apply directly to by clicking \'Click Here to Apply\' with your Word resume!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLooking forward to receiving your resume and going over the position in more detail with you.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Not a fit for this position? Click the link at the bottom of this email to search all of our open positions.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLooking forward to receiving your resume!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCyberCoders<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCyberCoders, Inc is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAll qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYour Right to Work - In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification document form upon hire.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCyberCoders will consider for Employment in the City of Los Angeles qualified Applicants with Criminal Histories in a manner consistent with the requirements of the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring (Ban the Box) Ordinance.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCopyright Â© 1999 - 2017 . CyberCoders, Inc. All rights reserved. ', ' 6591 Irvine Center Drive<br />\r\nSuite 200<br />\r\nIrvine, CA 92618<br />\r\nEmail<br />\r\ninfo@cybercoders.com<br />\r\nTelephone<br />\r\n949-885-5151 ', 'Graduation', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '26 April, 2017', '2017-04-26', 21, '2017-04-26 08:10:32', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62164635, 0, 'Immediate Requirement of sales officer & Sr. Sales Officer', 'Mandovi Motors Pvt. Ltd.', '', '2', '90', '29 Jun, 2017', '0', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Bangalore', 'Sales Officer Sales Executive ', '', '7', '80', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Mandovi Motors Hiring for Sales Officer / Sr. Sales officer<br />\r\n<br />\r\nResponsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Greet the customers<br />\r\n    Handover photo visiting card to customer<br />\r\n    Have knowledge of various products.<br />\r\n    Probe and understand customer needs<br />\r\n    Give proper DEMO of the car to the customer<br />\r\n    Offer test drive to the customer<br />\r\n    Advise customer on suitable models & deals with finance details<br />\r\n    Maintain honesty and integrity  in his/her dealings so as to gain trust and build long term relationship with customers.<br />\r\n    Promote Autocard & MGA <br />\r\n    Should have clear understanding about various schemes and products.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequirements:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Qualification :Any Graduate/Diploma holders.<br />\r\n    Fluent in English & Kannada , and other languages are added advantages<br />\r\n    Good Communication skills and convincing ability.<br />\r\n    Should have Two Wheeler Vehicle and should have Driving License of 2 & 4 Wheeler.<br />\r\n    Target Oriented and Should have Go better attitude.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterested candidates can directly walk-in or can  contact to HR Dept.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMr. Anand S(99720720 66) & Prashanth M(9880912403) ', '    Company Name: Mandovi Motors Pvt. Ltd.<br />\r\n    Email: hrd@mandovi.in<br />\r\n    Telephone: 9972072066', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '31 March, 2017', '2017-03-31', 47, '2017-03-31 03:01:03', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62204126, 0, 'Assistant Manager - Business Development', 'Weavings Manpower Solutions Pvt. Ltd', '', '2', '', '', '3', '6', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '1276', '434089', 'New Delhi, ', ' sales     business development', '', '29', '47', '', '', '', '', '', '', '1- Sales Strategy Formulation<br />\r\n2- Sells by establishing contact and developing relationships with prospects corporate clients<br />\r\n3- MIS <br />\r\n4- Market Awareness & Analysis', 'Email: shabari.shetty@weavings.in<br />\r\nTelephone: 2271234519', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '27 February, 2017', '2017-02-27', 79, '2017-02-27 03:43:58', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62279943, 0, 'Hiring for fresher Mechanical diploma Engineers', 'Manpower Global', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '3', '8', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Industry Standards', 'IN', '', '', 'Rajapur(Ghaziabad)', 'mechanical engineer', '', '1', '131', '', '', '', '', '', '', '        Required diploma /degree mechanical engrs in delhi ncr <br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        MechanicalEngineers holding a MechanicalEngineering degree / diploma in the industry and knowledge of computers and ISO procedures an added advantage.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        Candidate needs knowledge of production, quality controls.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\n        Press Tool design with CAD/CAM will be an advantage.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary:INR Depends on the candidate<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIndustry: Industrial Products / Heavy Machinery<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFunctional Area: Production , Manufacturing , Maintenance<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRole Category:Production/Manufacturing/Maintenance', 'Email: manpower_global@yahoo.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9891911575', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '26 April, 2017', '2017-04-26', 21, '2017-04-26 07:25:53', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62350470, 0, 'Entry Level Civil CAD Technician', 'Olsson Associates', '', '2', '90', '29 Jun, 2017', '1', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Oklahoma City, OK', 'Ability to contribute and work well on a team', '', '6', '94', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Tracking Code<br />\r\n1095-681<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Description<br />\r\n<br />\r\nImagine a place where responsibility is shared equally among all employees. Where leaders are approachable, and the open-door policy is the rule. Where employees are tasked to be innovative and work with an entrepreneurial spirit.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWelcome to Olsson Associates. We see problems as an opportunity for creativity, and we are looking for problem solvers to join our dynamic team. Our firm is organized into small teams to give you a strong sense of accountability and to achieve great results. The dress is business casual, the work environment is pleasant, our unique work hours allow for flexibility, and we have a lot of fun.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYOU ARE INTERESTED IN:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Civil Engineering projects: Site Civil, Land Development or Transportation<br />\r\n    Solving complex problems<br />\r\n    Drafting and Design<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYOU BRING TO THE TEAM:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Ability to contribute and work well on a team<br />\r\n    Strong communication skills<br />\r\n    Knowledge of AutoCAD or Microstation required<br />\r\n    Experience with Civil 3D or Inroads a plus<br />\r\n    Associate\'s degree in drafting a plus<br />\r\n    1 - 4 years\' experience in drafting preferred, not required.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nABOUT THE ROLE:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEach one of our projects gives our clients the opportunity to create a lasting impression on the communities in which they live, while respecting existing land uses, available infrastructure, and local, state, and federal ordinances. As a CAD Technician, you will perform red lines to mid-level design on projects under the supervision of an engineer or senior CAD technician, , and may travel to job sites for observation or field work. May also attend client meetings.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nABOUT US:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOlsson Associates is a nationally-recognized, employee-owned engineering and design firm that has been creating public and private projects throughout the United States. We\'ve been around since 1956, and we offer comprehensive design and consulting services in site/civil, transportation, water, environmental, field operations, survey, and facilities.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWith over 1,000 employees (and growing), nearly 30 offices in seven states, and a lengthy list of diverse clients, we believe you are our greatest asset and the key to our success. We seek to hire great people and put them in the right roles for their strengths.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAs an Olsson employee, you\'ll receive our traditional benefits package (health care, vision, dental, paid time off, etc.),<br />\r\n<br />\r\nplus these great perks:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    The opportunity to be an owner in the company after your first year through Olsson\'s ESOP program.<br />\r\n    A great 401(k) match<br />\r\n    A wellness program promoting healthy lifestyles<br />\r\n    A bonus system that rewards performance<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAre you in?<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEOE/AA/M/F/Vet/Disability Employer<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Location<br />\r\nOklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPosition Type<br />\r\nFull-Time/Regular<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFLSA Status<br />\r\nN/A<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEOE/AA/M/F/Vet/Disability Employer<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOlsson Associates is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetics, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or other classes protected by applicable law.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOlsson Associates strives to make our website accessible to any and all users. If you would like to contact us regarding the accessibility of our website or need assistance in completing the application process, please contact Human Resources at (402) 458-5027 or accommodations@olssonassociates.com. This contact information is for accommodation requests only and cannot be used to inquire about the status of applications.', 'Phone: 402.474.6311<br />\r\nToll Free: 877.831.6389<br />\r\nFax: 402.474.5160  ', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '31 March, 2017', '2017-03-31', 47, '2017-03-31 03:26:23', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62352528, 0, 'Consultant - Civil Engineering', 'Dargent Consultants', '', '2', '90', '02 Jul, 2017', '1', '3', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Hyderabad', 'Project Management Structural Engineering civil supervisor civil incharge Civil Engineering site construction ', '', '16', '130', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Coordination with consultants- Structural, Electrical, Plumbing etc. and checking and approval to their drawings.Periodical visits to all project sites to ensure progress and check quality of works.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary: 20K to 75K /Cab/Meal<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIndustry:Construction / Engineering / Cement / Metals/ Vocational Cousese<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFunctional Area:Site Engineering , Project Management and Civil Engineer<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRole Category:Site Engineering<br />\r\n<br />\r\nKeyskills<br />\r\nElectricals Plumbing Civil Engineering diploma civil civil engineer engineering structural engineering<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesired Candidate Profile<br />\r\nEducation:-<br />\r\nUG: Any Graduate - Any Specialization, <br />\r\nPG:Any Postgraduate - Any Specialization,<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDoctorate:Any Doctorate - Any Specialization <br />\r\nPlease refer to the Job description above<br />\r\nCompany Profile:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nA major technology, engineering, construction, manufacturing Company<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFunctional Area:Engineering Design / Construction<br />\r\nIndustry:Engineering / Construction<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterested candidates will be entertained at 91-9643393750,call before processing your resume<br />\r\n<br />\r\n <br />\r\n<br />\r\nThanks & Reagrds<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHR TEAM.', 'Email: ajaykumarsinghhr@gmail.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9643393750', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 April, 2017', '2017-04-03', 44, '2017-04-03 03:07:11', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(62576959, 27531, 'Accounts Executive', 'charteredclub.com', '', '1', '0', '', '2', '4', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', '', '', '', 'Delhi', 'QuickBooks, Payroll, accounting entries, accounting books, ', '', '1', '3', '', '', 'Y', 'As part of a high growth organization, this role will have significant growth opportunities along with exposure to implementing and scaling processes', 'Experience :<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- 2-3 years of experience in finance & accounting background preferably in Service Sector.  Startups ecosystem experience preferable.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Familiarity and deep knowledge of accounting and taxation software â€“ Tally, Spectrum, Genius, Busy e.t.c<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Working Knowledge of QuickBooks software or ERP â€“ Finance Module preferable<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSkills Required<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-Strong technical skills along with a desire and hunger to learn and improve.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- High quality written and verbal skills that will allow you to communicate well across teams, across geographies.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Tech savvy person comfortable with technology tools like google docs, excel, hangouts, gmail over and above the tools of the trade (primarily Quickbooks).<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- A flexible and hardworking personality willing to put in the hours to learn and deliver in a demanding startup environment.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Being proactive and the ability to work independently with minimal direction will see you rise through the ranks quickly.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Apart from the ability follow processes, if you can create efficient and intuitive processes you have a high chance of success in this role.', '', 'Responsibilities <br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Processing of accounting entries, reimbursements & payroll.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Reconciliations at bank, member and vendors levels.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Process owner for accounts at our hubs and new vendor onboarding.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis is primarily a generalist accounts profile with a focus on coordination between multiple stakeholders, preparing accounting entries and closing books of accounts.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Assist in tax and compliances including - Service Tax, TDS, PF, ESI, Professional Tax and VAT.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Facilitate internal audit queries, monthly MIS and closure of books.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n- Train hub teams on new processes and ongoing transactions.<br />\r\n', 'If interested, share your updated Cv at jobs@charteredclub.com', 'B.com, CA/CS-Inter', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '02 November, 2016', '2016-11-02', 196, '2016-11-02 06:12:59', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', '');
