(81731897, 0, 'VP, IT Delivery Manager', 'Atrilogy Solutions Group, Inc.', '', '1', '90', '25 Jul, 2017', '3', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Los Angeles, CA ', 'VP, Vice President, Manager, IT Delivery, Bachelor, Program Management, Project Management, Application Management, Financial Services, driving execution, agile, iterative, waterfall, drive, delivery ', '', '1', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Los Angeles, CA for a full-time, direct hire position. This position is responsible for leading the successful delivery of solutions across a variety of new technologies as well as overseeing program management for new technology initiatives across multiple business units. This position leads a team of project resources focused on delivering the bankâ€™s high priority technology initiatives and is actively engaged in day to day activities as needed. The person in this role engages with all levels of staff and management in the technology and business units. This role operates in a fast-paced environment with teams of motivated colleagues to deliver high quality solutions that add value to colleague and client experiences. Successful incumbent will be capable of working in a rapidly changing industry/environment, can tolerate ambiguity, demonstrate problem-solving leadership and act as a change agent at both the organizational level and via solutions delivery.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBasic Qualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Bachelorâ€™s degree<br />\r\n    Minimum 10 years of experience in IT<br />\r\n    Minimum 7 years of experience in Program/Project Management and/or Application Management<br />\r\n    Minimum 5 years of experience in Financial Services<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAbilities, Job Skills and Knowledge:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    10+ years of program/project management experience with a proven track record for delivering projects and driving execution.<br />\r\n    5+ years of experience managing direct report teams preferred<br />\r\n    Demonstrated experience of program/project management in an environment employing a variety of software development methodologies (agile, iterative, waterfall, etc)<br />\r\n    Demonstrated experience and success in influencing, leading, and coaching without direct leadership responsibility.<br />\r\n    Strong interpersonal, analytical, problem solving, facilitation, organizational, prioritization, effective decision making, and conflict resolution skills. Ability to negotiate or persuade others in complex situations.<br />\r\n    Strong problem solving and analysis skills, combined with impeccable business judgment and ability to communicate with highly technical and business management teams<br />\r\n    Ability to build, manage and sustain strong collaborative and productive relationships with business partners<br />\r\n    Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to translate technical information to non-technical audiences and vice versa.<br />\r\n    Strong planning and organization skills<br />\r\n    Experience of managing multiple stakeholders at all levels of the organization<br />\r\n    Demonstrated experience in motivating and leading project management teams<br />\r\n    Strong people management skills, including an understanding of how to attract, develop and retain talented individuals and experience in identifying and implementing training & development plans<br />\r\n    Demonstrated ability to lead complex strategic initiatives within a technical and/or business environment<br />\r\n    Understanding of finance and capital budgeting principles<br />\r\n    Understanding of end-to-end project and software development lifecycles<br />\r\n    Experience working in a multi-vendor (outsourced) environment strongly preferred.<br />\r\n    Demonstrates resilience and flexibility when presented with challenges or changing priorities<br />\r\n<br />\r\nResponsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Oversee and drive the successful delivery of a portfolio of programs and projects on scope, budget and time.<br />\r\n    Work with business teams to understand the requirements for future projects, efficiently scheduling available resources to develop world class products and services.<br />\r\n    Appropriately structure the delivery model and process to ensure that resources are prioritized and scheduled across projects to maximize effectiveness.<br />\r\n    Develop and maintain a high performing team through effective hiring, coaching, rigorous performance/talent management processes, and vendor partner management.<br />\r\n    Foster a collaborative, success-oriented team environment where resources are empowered and accountable. Provide work direction, delegation, and prioritization to team.<br />\r\n    Provide thought leadership and significant influence to the continuous improvement of processes, policies and best practices to optimize delivery of technologies.<br />\r\n    Ensure ongoing improvements align with standard process/service management principles and technology Systems Development Life Cycle (SDLC) methodologies.<br />\r\n    Define, track and measure overall department performance and metrics. Complete and distribute applicable reports, models, status updates, statistics, etc., to technology leadership as required.<br />\r\n    Provide proper escalation to leadership for issues/problems as necessary. Participate in the organization\'s strategic and financial planning process.<br />\r\n    Gain and maintain a broad understanding of business, business needs, and how assigned technologies/domain drive and support the business.<br />\r\n    Provide effective and timely reporting on in-progress and forthcoming projects<br />\r\n    Ensure that risks and dependencies across the project portfolio are managed effectively and reported to senior management.<br />\r\n    Work in partnership with business and technology resource managers to plan the appropriate allocation of resources to ensure efficient project delivery.<br />\r\n    Ensure program/project standards (documentation, risk/dependency management, budget tracking, reporting, and governance) are consistent across the department and meet the needs of stakeholders.<br />\r\n    Ensure compliance with company\'s policies, processes and procedures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFor immediate consideration please submit your resume in Word format, along with daytime contact information. LOCAL CANDIDATES ONLY PLEASE unless you are willing to relocate yourself at your own expense. Client is unable to provide H-1B Visa sponsorship at this time. All submittals will be treated confidentially. Selected candidate may be asked to pass a comprehensive background, credit and/or drug screening. Principals only, no third parties please.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEstablished in 2000, Atrilogy Solutions Group, Inc. provides organizations of all sizes with high-quality, cost effective information technology (IT), business process and health care consulting and staffing services. Our industry-leading service model combines experienced project managers with seasoned technical and functional consultants to eliminate client uncertainty and deliver superior value and results. Clients turn to Atrilogy for expertise in:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    IT staffing and placement (Project Managers, Business Analysts, DBAâ€™s, Developers, Quality Assurance and Testing, Software Configuration Management, etc.)<br />\r\n    All major Enterprise Resource Planning packages (including Oracle, PeopleSoft, JD Edwards, SAP, Microsoft, Lawson)<br />\r\n    Health care consulting resources and services (including ICD-10)<br />\r\n    Customer Relationship Management (CRM)<br />\r\n    Creative (Interactive Project Manager/Art Director, Information Architect, UI/UX Designer, Web/Graphic Design)<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAtrilogy has been recognized by CRN magazine as one of the nationâ€™s fastest-growing IT solution providers and by Inc. magazine as one of the nationâ€™s fastest-growing, privately-held companies. Based in Irvine, California, Atrilogy also has offices in Denver, Phoenix, and Atlanta.', '1 Jenner, Suite 240<br />\r\nIrvine, CA 92618<br />\r\n949.777.4700 T<br />\r\n949.777.4777 F', 'Graduation', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '26 April, 2017', '2017-04-26', 21, '2017-04-26 08:12:29', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(81838536, 0, 'ICICI BANK HIRING FOR Assistant Manager', 'Moving Up Aiero Hiring For Moving Up Aiero', '', '1', '90', '26 Jun, 2017', '0', '1', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '4', 'IN', '', '', ' Faridabad', 'Assistant Manager Branch manager', '', '10', '10', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'ICIC BANK HIRING BACK OFFICE <br />\r\nAssistant Manager Finance/Account/Audit<br />\r\nDeciding the financial needs<br />\r\nRaising the funds required<br />\r\nAllocation of funds<br />\r\nFixed assets management<br />\r\nWorking capital management<br />\r\nAllocation of Income<br />\r\nControl of Funds<br />\r\nEvaluation of Performance<br />\r\nCorporate Taxation<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInterested Candidate Please send their updated Resume & Call 9953201642', 'Email: movingupconsultants@gmail.com<br />\r\nTelephone: 9953201642', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '28 March, 2017', '2017-03-28', 50, '2017-03-28 00:39:58', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(81847513, 0, 'Lean Six Sigma Project Manager', 'Rockwell Automation', '', '2', '90', '20 Jun, 2017', '5', '11', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Milwaukee, WI', 'Engineering - General, Project Management', '', '16', '37', '', '', '', '', '<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCompany Overview<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRockwell Automation, the world\'s largest company dedicated to industrial automation, makes its customers more productive and the world more sustainable. Throughout the world, our flagship Allen-Bradley and Rockwell Software product brands are recognized for innovation and excellence.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWhen you choose Rockwell Automation, you join countless talented employees who have helped us establish our leadership position in the automation industry over the past century.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYou join a diverse, inclusive and global community with a passion for innovation. A place where you can partner with great minds and inspiring people. And a corporation backed by the financial strength that drives growth - and career opportunities.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAs much as we focus on our customers, we know our employees are key to our success and future. Helping you develop a rewarding career is a top priority. Because when you succeed, we succeed.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEEO Statement<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRockwell Automation is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, or veteran status. If you are an individual with a disability and you need assistance or an accommodation during the application process, email our Talent Acquisition representative at .<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRockwell Automation is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, or veteran status.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf you are an individual with a disability and you need assistance or an accommodation during the application process, email our Talent Acquisition representative at ratalentacquisition@ra.rockwell.com ', '', 'Summary/Scope of Position:<br />\r\nThe Lean Six Sigma (LSS) Project Manager has the primary responsibility for leading continuous improvement related projects and developing a culture that supports LSS led process improvements across all of our Global Sales and Marketing (GSM) processes to include Sales and other field related functions.<br />\r\nThe LSS Project Manager will work closely with business leaders and team members while applying LSS methods to solve business problems. This individual also works closely with other Lean Six Sigma Project Managers to ensure that process improvement projects follow a standard operating rhythm and disciplined approach to solving problems and maximizing results. The LSS Project Manager will also coach, mentor, and train others on expanding the knowledge of Continuous Improvement within GSM, developing team member LSS skills, and helping others apply LSS methods within the organization.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nEssential Functions:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Analyzes, plans, and implements process improvement needs<br />\r\n    Evaluates and models existing processes<br />\r\n    Organizes leads and facilitates cross-functional projects<br />\r\n    Collects data to identify root causes to problems<br />\r\n    Identifies improvement options<br />\r\n    Develops metrics that provide data for process management and indicators for future improvement opportunities<br />\r\n    Measures performance against process requirements, aligning improvement projects to close performance shortfalls<br />\r\n    Identifies and manages resources, including cross-functional team members to successfully execute projects<br />\r\n    Employs good change management techniques to facilitate change<br />\r\n    Ensures that solutions in the Project Control Phase are continuously monitored and sustained<br />\r\n    Provides consultation on the use of LSS methods and techniques to improve process performance<br />\r\n    Develops the skills of others through training materials and the application of LSS practices and methods<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Complexity:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Works on complex issues across the organization where analysis of situations or data requires an in-depth evaluation of many factors<br />\r\n    Participates in GSM development of methods, techniques and evaluation criteria for projects, programs and people within the region<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Helps drive process improvements by organizing and leading continuous improvement activities<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMinimum Qualifications<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMinimum Qualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Bachelor\'s Degree<br />\r\n    Typically requires a minimum of 5+ years of related experience<br />\r\n    Lean or Six Sigma Green Belt certification<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDesired Qualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Black Belt certification preferred<br />\r\n    Direct experience related to Sales, Sales Operations, or related function is preferred<br />\r\n    Has wide-ranging experiences, uses LSS professional concepts and skills to resolve complex issues in creative and effective ways<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\nScope:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Establishes continuous improvement objectives and work plans within areas of responsibility related to Sales, Marketing, Customer Experience, Global Pricing, and other GSM functions<br />\r\n    Coaches, trains, and mentors other employees at all levels of the organization<br />\r\n<br />\r\nInteraction:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Frequently interacts with peers and customers to gain cooperation of others or conduct presentations of complex technical information/project activities<br />\r\n    Networks with key contacts outside own area of expertise<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRequisition Number<br />\r\n<br />\r\n66911BR<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBusiness Group<br />\r\n<br />\r\nGlobal Sales & Marketing<br />\r\n<br />\r\nJob Category<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSales, Services, and Solutions<br />\r\n<br />\r\nRelocation Eligible<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNo<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPosition Type<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFull Time<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNo. of Positions<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWork State/City<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMilwaukee - Wisconsin<br />\r\n', 'ratalentacquisition@ra.rockwell.com ', '', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '22 March, 2017', '2017-03-22', 56, '2017-03-22 01:14:01', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(82075590, 0, 'Staff Accountant', 'Wenck Associates', '', '1', '90', '05 Jun, 2017', '10', '20', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '12', 'US', '', '', 'Maple Plain, MN', ' Accounting - General, Accounting - Bookkeeping/Clerical, Accounting - Management', '', '2', '47', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Wenck Associates, Inc. is a leading engineering & consulting firm, dedicated to providing innovative solutions through our strategic engineering, environmental, and consulting services.  Founded in Minnesota in 1985, our engineering coverage spans throughout the U.S., including offices in Minnesota, North Dakota, Georgia, Wyoming and Colorado.  We provide industries and local, state and federal agencies a full spectrum of services related to infrastructure, water, air, land, waste, and industrial processes.  Wenck is known for delighting our clients by being responsive, reliable, and proactive, thereby adding the most value possible to your business or organization.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWe are seeking a full-time Staff Accountant to join our corporate accounting team.  The position will be located in Maple Plain, MN.  This is a high visibility position that has daily contact with multiple members throughout the firm. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nOur company prides itself on providing employees a workplace that allows them to thrive in addition to excellent compensation and benefit package, and we are always looking for qualified people.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nQualifications:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    4 year college degree with emphasis in accounting/finance or 10 years relevant work experience<br />\r\n    0-5 years of general accounting and bookkeeping experience.<br />\r\n    Proficiency in the use of MS Excel, Word and Outlook.<br />\r\n    10-key and Data Entry experience.<br />\r\n    Experience with ERP systems - Deltek Vision a plus.<br />\r\n    Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written.<br />\r\n    Strong technical skills and ability to learn quickly.<br />\r\n    Strong analytical skills and ability to process information logically.<br />\r\n    Ability to work in a collaborative team environment.<br />\r\n    Hard working and enjoy learning.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPrimary Responsibilities:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Transaction processing of accounts payable and employee expense reports.<br />\r\n    General Ledger and Transactional Review and Analysis<br />\r\n    Financial Reporting and Analysis<br />\r\n    Account Reconciliation<br />\r\n    Budget Tracking<br />\r\n    Data archiving and filing.<br />\r\n    Special projects as assigned.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSalary: <br />\r\n<br />\r\n    Commensurate with education, training, and experience.<br />\r\n', '', 'Graduation / PG', 'Formal', 'US Citizen', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '07 March, 2017', '2017-03-07', 71, '2017-03-07 02:03:31', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(82113912, 21094, 'SAP Web Developer - Intern', 'Adobe', '', '5', '0', '', '1', '5', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '12', 'US', '2998', '1180598', 'California City, California', 'HTML, XML, JavaScript', 'https://adobe.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/external_university/job/San-Jose/SAP-Web-Developer---Intern_49219', '40', '138', '', 'Y', 'Y', '', 'What you need to succeed<br />\r\n1. HTML Development skills<br />\r\n2. XML Development skills<br />\r\n3. Java Script (nice to have)<br />\r\n4. CSS (nice to have)<br />\r\n5. Solid verbal, written and interpersonal communication skills<br />\r\n6. Collaborative<br />\r\n7. High energy<br />\r\n8. Sense of ownership<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAt Adobe, you will be immersed in an exceptional work environment that is recognized throughout the world on Best Companies lists. You will also be surrounded by colleagues who are committed to helping each other grow through our unique Check-In approach where ongoing feedback flows freely.<br />\r\nIf youâ€™re looking to grow your career, Adobeâ€™s the place for you. Discover what our employees are saying about their career experiences through the Adobe Life magazine.<br />\r\nAdobe is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome and encourage diversity in the workplace regardless of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability or veteran status.', '', 'The SAP Web Developer Intern will be part of the SAP Technical Services within Cloud Tech. that supports ongoing SAP as well as analytics projects. In this role, he/she will design and develop Web User Interface for one of our SAP Security applications. This application is used at Adobe to implement overall management of users and security roles for SAP systems. The Web user Interface is going to enhance the user experience and operational excellence for potentially 16,000+ users across Adobe.', 'From our website', 'Graduate', 'Formal', 'US Citizen, GC, EAD (OPT/CPT/GC/H4), H1B', 'Corp-Corp, W2-Permanant, W2-Contract, 1099-Contract, Contract to Hire', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '13 February, 2017', '2017-02-13', 93, '2017-02-12 22:03:23', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', '');
