\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span style=\"background: yellow; mso-highlight: yellow;\">15 -30 Days</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 27.0pt; border: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-top: none; padding: 0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"36\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 441.0pt; border-top: none; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"588\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span style=\"color: #1f497d;\">If interested can share me updated CV to nageshchitha@isquaresoft.com</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&nbsp;</p>', '', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '13 July, 2016', '2016-07-13', 308, '2016-07-13 07:19:13', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(90119522, 0, 'HR COUNSELOR', 'Softcrayons Tech Solution Pvt Ltd', '', '1', '90', '26 Jun, 2017', '0', '1', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', '3', 'IN', '', '', 'Ghaziabad', 'ling the telephonic inquiries H ', '', '21', '117', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Counselling Students and parents about our courses and programs<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2.Campaigning entire student cycle: Prospecting, Counseling, Admission, Orientation, Support, Satisfaction, Retention and Productive Output.<br />\r\n3.Interaction with students<br />\r\non routine basis for doubt clearing, general counselling and progress feedback and when requried Monitor class schedules to ensure smooth running of classes.<br />\r\n4.Conducting test papers, assignments etc Study material distribution and allocation.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5.Fee collection and petty cash management as and when required Liaison with Head Office for upcoming programs, admission tests, schemes and other offers. Handling assigned administrative responsibilities Handling the centre administration.<br />\r\n6. Handling the telephonic inquiries<br />\r\n7. Convince and convert the inquiries<br />\r\n8. Collect the feedback from the participants and<br />\r\n9.Consolidate the same<br />\r\n10.Counseling the students for various programs<br />\r\n11.Preparing MIS Reports<br />\r\n12.Should be comfortable with day to day target', '    Company Name: Softcrayons Tech Solution Pvt Ltd<br />\r\n    Company Description:<br />\r\n    Softcrayons Tech Solution Pvt Ltd<br />\r\n    Email: hr@softcrayons.com<br />\r\n    Telephone: 1204262233', 'MBA- HR', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '28 March, 2017', '2017-03-28', 50, '2017-03-28 00:33:40', 'IN', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
(90132810, 0, 'Interpretive Specialist', 'City of Fridley', '', '1', '90', '02 Jul, 2017', '3', '8', 'Full-Time', '', '', '', '', 'Market', 'US', '', '', 'Fridley, MN', 'volunteers, purchasing animal supplies, and providing animal care ', '', '1', '80', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'ORGANIZATIONAL MISSION:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIn 2014, the Fridley City Council adopted the following organizational mission: \"We believe Fridley in a Fridley that is a safe, vibrant, friendly and stable home for families and businesses.\" In addition, City staff committed to the vision by focusing on the core values of being responsive, driven and friendly.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPOSITION OBJECTIVE:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTo serve the community and Springbrook Nature Center visitors by developing and presenting environmental education programs and to work closely with Springbrook staff to facilitate the volunteer, rental, and animal care programs while maintaining a high level of positive interaction with park guests.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. Conduct environmental education programming for general public, schools and community groups on-site and off-site.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. Plan, prepare and evaluate interpretive programming for a variety of audiences.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. Mentor and work alongside volunteers of all ages.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. Schedule building rentals and community events.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. Assist with the volunteer program including recruitment, recognition, communication and training.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6. Implement care and treatment of the exhibit and program animals including, but not limited to: training of animal care volunteers, purchasing animal supplies, and providing animal care through feeding and enclosure maintenance, and evaluate animal housing/enclosures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n7. Work with nature center staff and volunteers to plan and implement community events.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n8. Help facilitate the Springbrook summer camp program by being involved in curriculum writing, supply purchasing, and day to day operations of summer camp programming.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n9. Assist in maintaining the appearance, preparation and functionality of all public spaces (inside and outside) including exhibits, classrooms, trails, exterior amenities (amphitheater and nature play).<br />\r\n<br />\r\nOTHER JOB FUNCTIONS:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. Respond to inquiries by telephone, email and in-person concerning a broad spectrum of natural resource information.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. Interact with park and interpretive center guests.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. Process program registrations and schedule groups and programs.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. Serve as a liaison to rental groups using the interpretive center.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. Promote programs and services using print, online and social media.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6. Other duties as assigned<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. Bachelorâ€™s degree in Environmental Education, Natural Science, or related field<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. Minimum of 6 months of experience in interpretive programming with youth<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. Must be at least eighteen (18) years of age<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. Valid driverâ€™s license, with good driving history.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. Must complete and successfully pass a thorough criminal background, reference check and pre-placement drug test.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6. Comfort working outdoors and meet the physical requirements of the position.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nDESIRED QUALIFICATIONS:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. Experience using graphic design software such as InDesign or Illustrator<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. Experience and comfort level with handling and caring for live animals<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. Comfort level with using hand tools and performing outdoor work such as trail maintenance and habitat management<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. Excellent customer service skills and ability to engage with park visitors<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. High level of motivation to serve the public<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6. Experience working with people from a diverse range of cultural, economic and social backgrounds in an educational setting<br />\r\n<br />\r\nESSENTIAL KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES:<br />\r\n<br />\r\n1. Communications: Must have the ability to actively listen to others for understanding of their needs and situations; ability to speak and write English clearly. Must be able to assertively control conversations in order to quickly and accurately gather pertinent information and be able to communicate this information professionally and precisely to the proper recipient. Must be able to read and understand correspondence, memoranda, and directives. Must be able to present information, data and material in a clear and concise manner to various audiences and in group settings. Must be able to effectively represent the City and its administrative operations to management and the public.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n2. Decision Making: Must act in a decisive manner, exercise good judgment. Be able to assess problems and situations, be able to anticipate needs and evaluate alternatives. Have knowledge of the utilization of appropriate resources and the willingness to initiate use of available resources to the public. Be able to deal with stressful situations, to avoid overreaction, to maintain flexibility in adjusting to situations and procedures, to support and carry out directives.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n3. Interpersonal Relationships: Must be consistent in dealing with the public; be sensitive to othersâ€™ problems without direct involvement. Must exclude personal biases from work performance. Have the ability to accept criticism and/or discipline. Have the ability to work varying shifts or times as tasks and assignments required. Have the ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with other professionals, co-workers, and the public, using tact and diplomacy.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n4. Professional Attitude: Must have commitment to the organization and the agencies that the City serves; willingness to take initiative; dependability; maturity in relationships with others; and self-confidence. Must be able to be punctual, reliable and dependable for schedules, activities and events. Represent the City to other agencies and the public with a courteous, positive, helpful, accurate and businesslike attitude in all written, telephone, and other types of contact. Have the ability to keep management informed of matters relating to the performance of the responsibility of the position. Must have the ability and willingness to work as a team member.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n5. General Knowledge: Must understand philosophies and goals of department. Must understand environmental and natural sciences systems and have a basic understanding of human behavior and diverse cultures. Have the ability to apply positive and effective teaching principles and techniques for community and public relations. Must have the ability to apply methods, techniques and implementation of program development as well as youth and public education.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n6. Technical knowledge: Have the ability to become proficient and/or certified in the use of personal computers and equipment associated with the facility. The ability and skill to safely operate a motor vehicle and other assigned equipment. Have the ability to perform simple mathematical functions such as adding numbers or calculating rates or charges for fees as well as to understand and perform simple statistical analysis.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n7. Special Requirements: Must have the ability to maintain confidential sensitive information handled in accordance with data practices rules and regulations as well as department policies. Ability to be creative, imaginative and innovative in programming and in teaching youth.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n8. Physical Abilities: Must have the ability to read and discern visual images on a variety of media. Must have the ability to vocalize and make presentations in a clear and concise manner in front of groups. Have the ability to hear conversations over the telephone or in a public meeting setting. Must have the ability to carry, lift, transport, set up, tear down displays, charts, event materials, supplies, equipment and/or items necessary for a variety of programs and events.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWORK ENVIRONMENT:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe attached work environment characteristics are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of Interpretive Specialist. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable a person with disabilities to perform the essential job functions.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNOTICE:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe above job profile does not include all essential and nonessential duties of this job. All employees with disabilities are encouraged to contact the Human Resources Department to review and discuss<br />\r\n<br />\r\nthe essential and nonessential functions of the job. An employee with a disability can evaluate the job in greater detail to determine if she/he can safely perform the essential function of this job with or without reasonable accommodation. If you are disabled and need additional assistance in completing this application or you need assistance with the testing process, please call (763) 572-3507. The City\'s TDD number is (763) 572-3534.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nWORK SCHEDULE:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis position is classified as a full-time non-exempt (hourly) position and is scheduled to work 40 hours per week, Tuesday through Saturday from 8:30 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Some flexibility will be required to work evenings, weekends and/or holidays for community events, programs and meetings.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCOMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nExpected hiring rate is: $22.20 per hour. Benefits include a variety of options, paid entirely or in part for the employee by the City, which includes life, health, and dental insurance; short-term disability; eighteen (18) days of annual leave per year; eleven (11) paid holidays per year; employee wellness program; as well as the employer\'s share of payments to workers\' compensation, unemployment compensation, and Public Employees Retirement Association. Additional voluntary benefits include a flexible spending account program, supplemental, life insurance for employee, spouse, and dependents; long-term disability; and special events/activities organized by the Employee Relations Committee.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAPPLICATION PROCEDURE:<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSubmit the City of Fridley employment application along with a cover letter and resume. Application materials may be downloaded from the City of Fridleyâ€™s website at www.fridleymn.gov or contact the City of Fridley directly at 6431 University Avenue, N.E., Fridley, MN 55432 (763) 572-3504. All application materials are due by 4:00 p.m. on Monday, April 17, 2017.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFinalists will be asked to provide examples of their work (i.e. writing examples, a portfolio or sample promotional materials) and be prepared to discuss materials in interviews as well as to complete additional testing or presentations.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMarch 2017<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe City of Fridley will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, creed, color, religion, sex, national origin, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, disability, age, membership on a local human rights commission, or sexual orientation. ', 'Application materials may be downloaded from the City of Fridleyâ€™s website at www.fridleymn.gov or contact the City of Fridley directly at 6431 University Avenue, N.E., Fridley, MN 55432 (763) 572-3504. All application materials are due by 4:00 p.m. on Monday, April 17, 2017. ', 'Bachelorâ€™s degree in Environmental Education', 'Formal', '', '', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', 'N', '03 April, 2017', '2017-04-03', 44, '2017-04-03 02:44:33', 'US', 'Y', '', '', '', ''),
